EU Ambassador and EU Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia Appreciate the Performance of the General Department of Customs and Excise
This is according to the press release of the General Department of Customs and Excise, which was received by Fresh News this morning, November 21, 2018, after the end of a luncheon hosted by the European Union Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia on the 20th. This November 2018, in order to understand the new progress of customs policy, trade facilitation, customs procedures and customs prospects in the future.
In his opening remarks, Mr. Arnaud Darc, President of the Board of the European Union Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, highlighted the important role of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia in actively participating in improving international trade and competition. Diversify the Cambodian economy.
He thanked and commended the progress and efficiency of the General Department of Customs and Excise in improving the business environment and diversifying the Cambodian economy, and especially the past cooperation between the Customs and the Chamber of Commerce. The European Union in Cambodia in the private sector customs mechanism has addressed a number of notable issues.
The Ambassador also mentioned the EU Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia and praised the two important roles of the Customs Institutions in revenue collection and trade facilitation, and reaffirmed the EU's support for Cambodia to optimize customs operations and simplify customs procedures through the ARISE PLUS program.
In response to the intervention, Dr. Kun Nhem highlighted the progress of the General Department of Customs, especially the success of the revenue collection exceeded the plan and increased every year, covering about 50% of fiscal revenue, despite the circumstances Tariffs on most goods are reduced to 0% within the framework of free trade agreements, and the internal tax revenue collected by the General Department of Taxation is steadily increasing.
He said that the intervention of customs policy and vision, including: customs policy, vision and strategy of customs reform and modernization 2019-2023.
Mr. Kun Nhim thanked the European Union for its assistance in the development and implementation of the Customs Data Automation System (ASIA) project, initially supported by a financial assistance project from a development partner under the auspices of The World Bank, which currently covers the country of export and import operations, and has worked closely within the framework of the Customs-Private Partnership in the past.
In this conversation, he addressed and received some suggestions raised by relevant business people who participated in the event.
