Kampong Cham Provincial Commissioner Pays Tribute to Police Chief of Ta Prok Administration, Chamkar Leu District, Who Died While Working
(Kampong Cham): Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, on November 21, 2018, led the Commission of Commissioners, Chiefs of Special Offices, including Inspectors, Deputy Inspectors and Officers of Chamkar Leu District Police Inspectorate to pay their respects and honor their ranks. Post-mortem to the body of Colonel Jimach, No. 19374, Chief of Police, Ta Prok Administrative Police Station, who died while on duty on November 20.
At present, the family is preparing for the traditional ceremony at their home in Thnal Bek Lech village, Svay Teap commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province, following the Buddhist tradition.
With the invitation to pay their respects to the late Colonel Chi Mach, Major General Em Kosal and his colleagues lit incense and offered prayers dedicated to the deceased, both saddened and deeply saddened by the loss of an active official who had served the country. Many years ago.
On that occasion, the General Commissioner and Chairman of the Provincial Veterans brought the budget of Kampong Cham Provincial Police in the amount of 6,035,000 Riels, 01B rice, 04 cases of orange juice, 06 cases of pure water, 06 cases of noodles. These funds were given to the families of the corpses to organize the rituals in the traditional Buddhist way.
On that occasion, the family of the deceased thanked the General Commissioner and his colleagues, as well as the benefactors who always take care of the subordinates.
