(Phnom Penh): Under the development policy of the Royal Government, especially under the care of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, as well as relevant government officials, nearly 600 families living in the village Chicken cage, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok has received the official land title.
The handover ceremony took place in the presence of Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of the Capital, Mr. Sak Chankanharith, Deputy Governor of Sen Sok District and Mr. Pov Narith, Director of the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction, Cadastral and Land. Khan Sen Sok on November 20, 2018.
Having received the plan to promote the registration of people in the Borey area by the Phnom Penh Capital Hall to the Sen Sok District Land Office, as well as Sangkat O'Beak Kam and Khan Sen Sok to cooperate to promote this work to the people who have not yet received. After obtaining the title deed, Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, introduced the survey work to the people in the above Trung Moan village, in which the team measured 598 plots of land.
After completing this work, the Department submitted a letter to the Ministry of Land Management to request the issuance of title deeds to the people. There are 573 cards. The other 25 plots were issued to the owners by requesting to separate the plots.
Pov Narith, the director of the office, recalled that the site used to be a former K warehouse, but later, during 2006, there was a proposal to develop a residential area in the form of an apartment complex, and after construction, the co-owners Resale to people who are customers and also have multiple resellings from one generation to another.
This makes it difficult for people in the area to pay a lot of money to pay taxes to the state. Seeing this difficulty, the Royal Government decided to pay a one-time tax, regardless of whether the house or land was resold to many people.
Until now, the authorities have decided to measure and request the issuance of a card at the back of each house so that people can come to fulfill their tax obligations only once and can get a certificate identifying the property owner.
On that occasion, the director of the department, Sarin Vanna, and the deputy governor, Sak Chankanharith, instructed the people who received the title that the title is as valuable as gold and silver, so people should take care of the title. This to be comfortable.
With thanks, the people of Trung Moan Village, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok were very happy to receive the title deed.
