(Tbong Khmum): 134 bins supported by the Australian Center for Training (ACE) from the Run for the Environment Fund in the past were distributed to district halls, commune halls, schools in O Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, this morning, November 20, 2018, under the chairmanship of Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, representing Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment.
Trash delivery now wants to send a message to good waste management and all trash must be put in the trash and sorted into different types of trash.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra said that currently about 10,000 tons of garbage is generated every day and about 3.6 million tons of garbage is generated every year. From year to year, the amount of garbage in Cambodia is increasing by about 10% per year due to population growth, lifestyle changes and packaging of daily necessities, and the understanding of waste sorting according to the type of waste. Technical principles are still limited.
According to the study, in 100% of the garbage, 65% is wet garbage, 20% is plastic bag and more than 10% is solid waste. Garbage recycling is only 20%, making the rate of dumping at landfills 70 to 80%, and some of the rubbish is dumped on public roads, in which we see littering. Plastic scraps, foam plates, plastic bags in public places have drastically reduced the beauty of some towns.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that solid waste management is our duty, so all citizens, students should consider villages, schools, pagodas, cities, towns, other places where you live and study. Working and doing business as a home of relatives who need to be cleaned regularly to maintain the beauty and promote public welfare.
Improper packaging and storage of rubbish, dumping rubbish in public places and along roads will lead to many consequences, such as clogging of drainage systems, causing floods during the rainy season, losing the beauty of the village. Our homes, our schools, our pagodas, our cities and towns, and piles of rubbish create shelters for germs and toxins.
The principle of an environmentally friendly school is a good principle, not only to make the school clean and tidy, but also to be transparent and considerate of environmental impacts, including those activities in the teaching and learning program. . Waste management and waste sorting is an important factor to teach you to understand and participate in reducing plastic waste together to make our community, village, commune and society a good environment.
On the other hand, the successful implementation of the environment, the enforcement of the law is very important in orienting all stakeholders in all socio-economic development activities to comply with the technical guidelines of the Ministry, as well as prevent And suppress all forms of environmental crime in order to ensure the quality of the environment, the balance of ecosystems and sustainable living.
