Nearly 200 Student Teachers in Siem Reap Volunteer to Donate Blood to Blood Donation Center
(Siem Reap): In order to contribute to humanitarian activities and to save the lives of victims who are being treated in hospitals that need blood, 170 teachers of Siem Reap Teacher Training College have donated blood to the center. Blood of Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital. The blood donation took place at the provincial pedagogical school on Saturday, November 17, 2018 this past weekend.
Mr. Lim Heng, Deputy Director of Siem Reap Provincial Hospital, stated that in recent years, the usage rate of Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital has increased significantly and all the expansion and addition of specialized services in the department. This doctor also needs to use more blood.
He pointed out that the blood consumption at Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital in 2016 was about 1,300 units, and in 2017, about 2,500 units were used. Strangely, in 2018, blood will be used to save lives through various surgeries up to about 3,700 blocks.
He added that currently the blood donation center of Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital needs more people to donate blood voluntarily. He said that according to the plan, 100 percent of the blood will be donated voluntarily, while currently there are national and international donors who have come to donate blood voluntarily, about 60 to 70 percent of the blood needed for this year. About 3,700 blocks.
He pointed out that currently most of those who have volunteered to donate blood are young people. In fact, 170 students of Siem Reap Teacher Training College volunteered to donate blood to the Blood Transfusion Center of Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital.
He called on the people and the general public to donate more blood to the Blood Transfusion Center of the Provincial Referral Hospital to save more lives as this department has a steady rate of blood consumption. Especially used for women giving birth, patients, traffic accidents and major surgeries for emergencies.
