The Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns, chanting and worshiping the moon has been around since ancient times, as documented by foreign historians, as well as by the inscriptions of the temples of Angkor. This Royal Festival is always held every year in the Kingdom of Cambodia for 3 days, from the 14th to the 15th and the 1st of Roach Khek Tek on the Tonle Sap.
During the Royal Festival, there are also two other ceremonies, namely the boat race and the Ok Ambok festival to worship the moon god. The boat race lasts for three days, with lanterns floating at night, while the Ok Ambok festival celebrates the moon only on the second day, at midnight on the 15th day of the lunar month.
