Guatemala City: Nearly 4,000 people were evacuated from areas around Guatemala's Fuego volcano earlier this week as it began to erupt again this year. . This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday afternoon, November 20, 2018.
According to the Guatemalan Disaster Management Agency, the volcano spewed ash, lava and toxic gases into the air 500 meters above the crater. There were no immediate reports of injuries.
