(Phnom Penh): Mr. HUN Many, Chairman of the Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism of the National Assembly (7th Committee of the National Assembly) on November 19, 2018, chaired a meeting with Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
The meeting was held in accordance with Article 97 of the Constitution and Article 34 of the new Rules of Procedure of the National Assembly to discuss two agendas, including: Strategic planning in the field of education, youth, sports in response to the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4. And policies for the new generation of schools.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on the night of November 19, 2018, Mr. Hun Many noted the implementation of the policy on the new generation of schools in response to the Rectangular Strategy phase. Fourth, it is also a response to modern education, although the mechanism for implementing this policy is not yet fully smooth.
The Seventh Committee of the National Assembly will continue to monitor the implementation of the policy on the new generation of schools, as well as the political programs and regulations of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to ensure effective implementation.
The chairman of the Seventh Commission stressed that comprehensive policy formulation in response to the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy is important, but the most important thing is the fruitful results of the implementation of that policy. The need, hope and confidence of the electorate who have given their trust through the election of the Cambodian People's Party to continue to lead the country.
According to the press release, in addition to the above success, the Seventh Committee and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports examined, studied and discussed policies and strategies to increase the efficiency of the implementation of the sector, including:
1: Education Management Reform Strategy to Promote Quality Citizenship in Cambodia with four core strategies, including education management reform, administrative management reform, financial management reform and resource management reform. People.
2: Youth Development Reform Strategies that provide opportunities for young people to receive vocational education and training and encourage young people to be creative in their skills in response to the government's concept of "a young person has at least one skill in life. "
3. Strategies for reforming the development of physical education and sports through the development of the legal framework, the development of advanced sports, the development of sports for all, the preservation and development of all kinds of sports, and the development of the sports industry.
For today's meeting, the Seventh Committee considers it an effective dialogue forum to cooperate, improve and promote the implementation of work in the field of education, youth and sports to meet the needs of voters, especially youth, teachers, educators, parents, guardians. Students as well as society as a whole. Russia rejects report that it wants to reopen military base in Cuba
