She also said that the Kathina is a contribution to the promotion of Buddhism, the state religion, and this is to show the next generation to see the celebration of Buddhism, which is a good tradition of Cambodia. We will join in building the country with the Royal Government for development as well.
Mr. Im Chung, Chairman of the Pagoda Committee, said that the construction of this bridge is in collaboration with the Buddhists with generous force, since 2017, and the construction of a 151.2-meter-long and 4.50-meter-wide steel-reinforced concrete bridge. Meters and 8 meters high, with a project cost of 380,000 dollars.
He added that the construction of this bridge is to make it easier for students to go to school and people to transport agricultural products from one side to the other or from one district to another. Finally, he called on philanthropists to join in generously building the bridge to be completed.
Minister of Labor: The company must ensure safety and working conditions for Cambodian workers working abroad
The Minister recommended that the above companies make more efforts to facilitate the successful export of workers to Hong Kong in accordance with the provisions of the law in order to ensure safety, comfort, accuracy, dignity, especially guarantee. Improved working conditions for Cambodian workers who will be working as domestic helpers in Hong Kong in the near future.
In fact, in order for the sending of domestic workers to work in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region to be successful for the first pilot phase in 2017, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has signed a memorandum of understanding with the Cambodian Human Resource Development Association in Hong Kong to Cooperation on providing support and support services for domestic workers and disseminating information about Cambodian domestic workers to Hong Kong employers.
Today, there are about 357,000 domestic workers in Hong Kong, mostly Filipinos and Indonesians, who have the same rights and working conditions as Hong Kong workers.
The government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region has introduced standard employment contracts for additional support for domestic workers, including a minimum wage of about $ 570, which will be regularly reviewed for food or other benefits. US $ 133 per month, free accommodation, free return airfare and free medical treatment.
It should be noted that Cambodia currently sends workers to work abroad in six countries: Thailand, the Republic of Korea, Malaysia, Japan and Singapore and Hong Kong, with a total of about 1.2 million workers.
So far, they have sent more than $ 2 billion a year to Cambodia to support their families. At the end of the employment contract and return to Cambodia, they will be an important human resource to participate in the development of the national economy, because by working abroad, they can not only earn extra income, but also earn Skills, experience, knowledge, language and lifestyle in developed countries.
