Six Chinese nationals working at Crown Diamond Casino Arrested at Pailin Provincial Military Headquarters but Released After Questioning While Prosecutors Unaware
(Pailin): On the night of November 18, 2018, the Pailin Provincial Armed Forces arrested six Chinese nationals in the Diamond Crown Casino at the Cambodian-Thai border in Pailin Province, detained them for more than 10 hours before releasing them.
In connection with the arrest and release, the Pailin provincial prosecutor claimed that he did not know about this because the military had already released the Chinese and reported to him, but the Pailin provincial military commander, Brigadier General Van. Nalong claimed that it was not an arrest, but that the Chinese casino had sent the military to be arrested for gambling.
On the contrary, Toch Sopheakdey, Pailin Provincial Prosecutor, stated that he was not aware of this at all and that he had just received information about their arrest while the military was releasing them, more than 10 hours after their arrest. Body that is against legal procedures.
"The provincial military has arrested six Chinese nationals in connection with more than $ 100,000 in casino money since last night, but did not report it to prosecutors until 10:30 a.m.," the prosecutor added. "Without a release order, it is completely illegal. It could be a crime to detain people for extortion."
