More than 6,000 hectares of farmers' fields in Baray district are suffering from lack of irrigation water, Kampong Thom Provincial Administration released 8 water pumps to intervene
(Kampong Thom): After receiving the news that there are rice fields of farmers in some areas of Treal commune, Pong commune, Sralao commune, Baray district, they have been facing water shortage while the rice is bearing fruit, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom province and professional officials Involved under the supervision of many other provinces to check the condition of their fields in the three communes with water shortage as the rice began to bear fruit and immediately intervened.
The affected area is about 6,428 hectares of the nearly 10,000 hectares of farmland in the area. The provincial governor said that the authorities had provided 1,500 hectares of first aid and 2,500 hectares of rice that could not be saved due to lack of water.
With this natural disaster, the Governor of Kampong Thom Province installed eight water pumps to pump water into rice fields for farmers to prevent fear of brown rice. As for the water source in that area, he said that there is no problem because there are up to 3 main canals for use and many small sub-canals.
The provincial governor also urged the team to rush to install water pumps for farmers on time, so as not to affect the rice farmers. He estimated that some fields lacking water could be affected if there was no water for another five to six days and the sky was hot and dry.
However, he confirmed to the owners that do not worry, the team is helping to solve. Farmers express their gratitude for the attention of the leaders who responded immediately to the people in time after receiving this news. Mangrove forests in Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampot and Kep are being violated. Owning and building houses, the Minister of Agriculture told the 4 provincial governors to take measures to protect
(Phnom Penh): Mangrove forests in Kep, Kampot, Sihanoukville and Koh Kong provinces are being cleared, encroached upon, land grabbing, clearing, land reclamation, mangrove forest fencing and re-issuance of titles.
In response to this worrying issue, the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, on November 19, 2018, sent a letter to the governors of four provinces, including Kep, Kampot, Sihanoukville and Koh Kong, to take control measures. And protect mangrove forests in its occupied geography.
Minister Veng Sakhon also said that recently, mangrove holdings have been issued in many fishing communities, especially in Sihanoukville.
The Minister of Agriculture confirmed to the four provincial governors: The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries requests His Excellency Lok Chumteav, Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors to pay attention to the management, maintenance and protection of mangrove forests within the jurisdiction of each province as the state land management authority.
According to the law on fisheries, flooded forests and mangrove forests play an important role in the fisheries sector, so clearing, encroaching, land reclamation, land acquisition, mangrove land encroachment, etc. In the fishing territory is prohibited.
In addition, Article 3 of Sub-Decree No. 25 dated March 20, 2007 on the management of fishing communities stipulates that "community fishing grounds are public property of the state."
