Good news for people with kidney disease! Royal Phnom Penh Hospital Introduces Non-Surgical Kidney Stone Machine
(Phnom Penh): Royal Phnom Penh Hospital has imported and demonstrated a machine to treat kidney stones by spraying kidney stones without surgery, which is the first technology in Cambodia. On November 17, 2018, the hospital held a workshop to demonstrate its latest technology in Cambodia in the field of health.
He said that this machine is only available in the Royal Hospital in Phnom Penh and in Cambodia as a whole, and even in Thailand, there is no use of such machines, so patients with kidney stones in Cambodia. Be the first to receive treatment by splitting a kidney stone.
He added that the machine is capable of splitting stones smaller than 2 cm, but if the kidney stones are large, it needs to be sprayed several times to break into small pieces and it must come out through the urine. However, if the patient urinates and bleeds a little after the injection, there is no problem, because when the urine comes out, the stones that are sprayed pass through the urethra and there is friction to make blood. Like this.
Dr. Bo Sopheap, a kidney specialist at the Royal Phnom Penh Hospital, said that according to observations in Cambodia, the number of kidney stones is high in major hospitals such as Lok Sang Hospital. Three to four cases daily. Bringing kidney stone injection machine technology to Royal Phnom Penh Hospital is a painless treatment and does not require the patient to be hospitalized.
He said that kidney stones are caused by not drinking enough water, lack of exercise and eating an unbalanced diet. Therefore, Cambodians should consume 2.5 to 3 liters per day to prevent the risk of kidney stones.
It should be noted that Royal Phnom Penh Hospital always brings the first new technology to Cambodia to treat patients with the most convenience, and the hospital has also achieved a lot of success with its new technology imported. In the past. India, Russia launch joint military exercise in Uttar Pradesh
