The meeting was held on November 16, 2018 at Siem Reap Provincial Hall, while the order of parking, disorderly conduct and sales of vendors in the Preah Pithu temple complex are raising complex issues affecting the beauty of the temple. That.
Mr. Sok Sangvar, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority and Chairman of the Committee for Organizing and Coordinating the Order of Vendors in Angkor Resort, confirmed at the meeting that the order of the stalls and the parking lot in front of Preah Pithu Temple are not in order today. The constant noise of the generator also disturbs the tourists who visit the temple.
Recently, the APSARA Authority has set up a separate committee focusing on the study of new locations for these parking lots and stalls. However, officials have yet to find a suitable location, as the site is covered by forests and archeological sites. The purpose of this meeting is to gather additional ideas from the committee so that professional officers can be used as a basis for further study.
Major General Man Chhoeun, Deputy Director of the Department in charge of the Angkor Heritage Protection Unit, confirmed that the stalls in the Angkor area are very complicated, but the team is always ready to cooperate at any time.
