Finally, the Chairman of the Prek Pnov District Assistance Team requested members of the party at all levels to help solve problems for the local people at the same time. After coffee prices fall for a while, farmers in Mondulkiri province return to grow this crop, taste the water, taste the soil because the price is satisfactory
(Mondulkiri): Since the first coffee growing in 2000, coffee farmers in Mondulkiri seem to have revived a bit, but later on, problems also arose for them due to falling coffee prices. So low that there are no buyers, which is why farmers are gradually abandoning coffee cultivation.
After coffee became very popular among the people today and due to the widespread overseas market, the coffee that most farmers used to give up has been replanted in Mondulkiri province forever. To date, coffee cultivation in the northeastern province has increased dramatically, but is still not enough to meet the needs of foreign markets.
The coffee crop in Mondulkiri province is growing well, said Mr. Seng Sao, Director of the Agronomy Office of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Mondulkiri Province. .
During a meeting with journalists from 10 institutions and a civil society organization organized by CEDAC in Mondulkiri province on November 16, 2018, Mr. Seng Sao said that currently the coffee crop in Mondulkiri province is spreading over the area. 286 hectares, but the harvest is still small, only about 70 hectares, yielding 3-7 tons of coffee (dry) per hectare.
Mr. Seng Sao reminded that in Mondulkiri province, there is a history of growing coffee since 2000 or 2001, when the price of coffee was not very expensive, but farmers can accept a small increase in the area under cultivation, but unfortunately In later times, the price of coffee disappointed farmers because they sold a kilogram of dry coffee for only 2,000 riel or 800 riel or less because there were no buyers until some farmers decided Stop growing coffee right away.
It was not until 2017, 2018, that the price of coffee increased again to $ 2.5 per kilogram, so that farmers returned to grow this coffee crop to taste the water. Although it is not possible to predict the exact number, Mr. Seng Sao is still optimistic that in 2020 and in the future, the area of coffee plantations in Mondulkiri will increase even more.
The reason why more farmers and companies are returning to grow coffee in Mondulkiri is because most Cambodians have started to enjoy coffee, which has revived the Cambodian coffee market, especially the recognition of Mondulkiri coffee. In Cambodia, good quality, many customers like.
(Phnom Penh): Try Pheap Boeung Tonle Merech Company of Tycoon Try Pheap, located in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, has announced that its rubber plant has started to bear fruit, and in 2018, about 700 hectares of rubber will be opened.
With the reaffirmation of its rubber plantations, Try Pheap Boeung Tonle Merech also rejected some advertisements alleging that the company was clearing the community land. The company claims that the land was stolen by some crooks and accused the company of encroaching on and clearing the community land.
Try Pheap Boeung Tonle Merech Company received the right to invest in economic forest land concessions from the Royal Government in the above area in 2011. Since receiving the right to invest in this area, the company has been cultivating rubber continuously until now, about 3,500 hectares.
Through the cultivation of rubber, the company has provided many jobs to people in the area, as well as from other provinces. According to Heng Sarum, there are currently about 550 employees working in the rubber plantation with a decent salary. In addition to the salary, the company also provides accommodation and electricity for use.
In addition to planting rubber, the company also built a market, a restaurant, a car park for people in the district to do business. The company claims that it is currently building more accommodation for workers and staff and is also building a rubber factory. The factory is scheduled to open before the Khmer New Year 2019.
In 2016, Samdech Techo Hun Sen visited the development area and also highly appreciated the development in Ton Phong.
