(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, this morning, November 18, 2018, led his subordinates to pay their respects to the late Mr. Prach Chhuon, Emperor Chapey Dang Veng, who passed away on the night of November 17, 2018. At the age of 82, due to old age, he was taken to the Wat Botum Vatey Assembly Hall in Chaktomuk Sangkat, Daun Penh District, Phnom Penh to celebrate the Buddhist tradition.
Mr. Ouch Phea shared his deepest condolences with the family of the deceased and expressed his deepest condolences for the loss of the famous hero, Mr. Prith Phirum, the eloquent Prach Chhuon, the long-time Chapi emperor and who is considered a human heritage. Abstract, which the world recognizes that no one has the skill and rhetoric to perform like his grandfather.
