(Preah Vihear): Mr. Peng Trida, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, said that the prices of agricultural products in the markets have high odds that farmers must strive to double production to improve the living standards of families.
The statement of the Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture was made on the occasion of distributing agricultural materials to 165 families from 3 communes in Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province on November 17, 2018.
"So the price of agricultural products in the farmers' market is no longer low, but what farmers need to do now is to grow more crops to supply the market."
Mr. Peng Trida stated that with the encouragement of the people to work hard to grow crops, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province has distributed agricultural materials to people to produce, cultivate and raise animals to supply the local market.
"Agricultural materials are being distributed to farmers now in order to improve people's livelihoods through the production of agricultural crops, animal husbandry and so on," he said.
Please note that the farmers who came to receive agricultural equipment at this time are 165 families from 3 communes in Rovieng district, including Reak Reay commune, Raksmey commune and Ratana commune, of which 112 families are raising chickens and 53 families are growing vegetables. The materials to be distributed include: water tank with a capacity of 1000 kg and 500 liters, vegetable seeds, nets, vegetable garden nets, chicken coops, chicken coops, vegetable seedlings and chicken vaccines.
