Rice farmers in Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province lack water to irrigate, the provincial governor intervened to install 22 water pumps to help pump water to rice
The affected area is about 500 hectares out of nearly 10,000 hectares of farmland in the area.
Heng Sophornrith, director of the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, installed 22 water pumps to pump water into people's rice fields to prevent rice paddies. Empty because there are up to 6 main canals for use.
Mr. Sar Kakada, Prey Nup District Governor, said that according to the actual inspection, the rice that is currently bearing fruit in Cheung Ko commune is about 200 hectares and Veal Renh commune is on the border with about 300 hectares. It does not seem serious yet. The team is helping farmers with this problem.
Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, urged the team to rush to install water pumps on time so that there will be no problems affecting rice farmers. Cause damage if there is no water for another 5 to 6 days, the sky is hot and dry like this.
