In 2019, the early rains may be slow, causing a shortage of irrigation water and use, the Minister of Water Resources put three measures to solve
(Banteay Meanchey): Due to the unusual weather conditions in recent years, the rainfall at the beginning of the year is fast and the end of the year is different, and in 2019, the rainfall at the beginning of the year may be slow, which is why Concerns about lack of irrigation water and consumption.
On November 17, 2018, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, visited Soeur Commune, Mongkul Borei District, Banteay Meanchey Province for practical review and additional measures to prevent the situation like 2016 from happening. Again.
During this mission, there was also the active participation of Mr. Suon Bavor, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province to have a clear understanding of the weather situation and the measures to be taken.
In order to avoid possible difficulties, Minister Lim Kean Hor has proposed three measures for relevant officials to address, including:
1: Take care and solve by using all possible means to save the work of farmers in all places where there is water source.
2. All ministry leaders who have already been assigned must immediately take over and resolve all issues related to water.
3. All departments must work closely with local authorities at all levels in order to advise farmers to avoid over-cultivation at the beginning of the season, far from water sources, which can be a serious disaster leading to water shortages. More daily life.
At the same time, the Minister also decided to provide 2 new pumping stations equipped with 5 water pump Hun Sen, which is a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as a bond.
