General Kang Sokhon decided to send officers who used their guns to shoot their cars to the unit's disciplinary council to take action and to strictly enforce the discipline of the National Police Force.
(Phnom Penh): General Kang Sokhon, Director General of the General Department of Identification, on November 17, 2018, discussed and decided to send Lt. Col. Din Van Nora, Director of the Office of Logistics and Accounting of the General Administration Department of the General Department of Identification to the Disciplinary Council. Of the unit to take action and strictly enforce the discipline of the National Police Force.
According to the confession, on the morning of November 17, 2018 at 10:45 AM, Colonel Din Van Nora in front of the Director of the Office of Personnel and Training of the Department of Administration - Total.
The cause of the explosion was that he had been under stress for months over family issues (his son had just undergone kidney surgery, and his third brother had been arrested for drug use). And mother-in-law just amputated right leg with diabetes).
Angered by his mother questioning and blaming the restaurant, and because he was under the influence of alcohol, he fired several shots at his car.
After confessing before the Director of the Office of Personnel and Training of the Department of Administration - Total, the person agrees to be punished according to the discipline of the National Police Force.
After carefully examining and investigating the above case, the General Director General of the General Department of Identification decided to send the case to the disciplinary council of the unit to take action and implement the discipline of the National Police Force strictly.
