Indonesian officials confirmed to Xinhua by telephone that at least eight homes had been hit by mudslides after the area was hit by a series of moderate earthquakes in recent days. Indonesian authorities have forced the evacuation of more than 8,000 people in Mamasa district to safety as the area where they live is facing a series of landslides.
The newly-hit western Sulawesi province borders the central Sulawesi province, which was hit by a devastating earthquake and tsunami in September that killed more than 2,000 people.
Two young Cambodian entrepreneurs want to compile a book on business techniques to encourage young people to start a business
(Phnom Penh): Two young entrepreneurs in Cambodia have written two books that showcase business techniques. The purpose of compiling this book is to encourage young people to dare to go out of business and go out on purpose and be successful.
The book, "Selling Emotions," was written by Sam Kosal, who spent time researching well-known businesses in the United States and other leading countries. This book has been synthesized by many key ideas to integrate into the Cambodian business context and reflects the ideas of many large local businesses and companies.
Mr. Sam Kosal said that "successful sales is based on building the right mood in the context of their business, how to make those feelings in the hearts of customers, so that sales in the business does not disappear."
As for the book entitled "Ready to start a business for the right purpose", Mr. Meng Song Hor collected many strong, strong, short ideas of big successful businesses both at home and abroad to synthesize points. Turns out that make businesses successful until there is no way back to decline, especially new entrants help businesses achieve their goals with a clear vision.
Mr. Meng Songhor said, "Before doing business, every business owner must be prepared before going out to practice, such as being physically, mentally, goal-oriented and ready to change to live."
In addition, he cited the point of business failure of many entrepreneurs who choose to go wrong, cause the business to move or collapse.
The authors of both books express their confidence and belief that these two books will cultivate the ideas of those who are not on target business to turn to the goal and those who fail to walk the path of success and those who do not. Be out of business, have the courage to do business and be successful.
