Cambodia-Malaysia Ministry of Education Holds Study Fair to Encourage Students to Seek More Study Opportunities in Malaysia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. San Vathana, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, spoke positively about the organization of the Education Fair in Malaysia and job opportunities for 2018, held by the Ministry of Education of Cambodia and Malaysia, that will provide many opportunities. For Cambodian students to find opportunities to study more.
This statement was made by the Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the occasion of his participation in the 2018 Education Fair in Macedonia and Job Opportunities for 2018, which was held on November 17, 2018 with the participation of From many students.
Dr. San Vathana said, "The purpose of this exhibition is to focus on the establishment of cooperation and communication between institutions of higher education of the two countries, focusing on encouraging students to seek more learning opportunities, motivate teachers. "Teachers exchange experiences on teaching methods and encourage researchers from both countries to consider the possibility of joint scientific research."
He added that in order to contribute to improving the quality of education and exchange of governance experience between the two countries, Cambodia-Malaysia in the field of higher education, as well as information sharing and mutual understanding between Cambodian youth. - Malaysia.
He added that the factors that students should continue to study in Malaysia, in addition to seeing the quality of education in addition to seeing job opportunities are:
1. The distance between Cambodia and Malaysia is close. 2. The cost of living is low compared to other countries. 3. For food, climate and culture are similar to Cambodia. Economic, social and political development between the two countries is moving in the same direction.
He added that the conditions for receiving the scholarship are focused on the student's study, which means focusing on the student's previous education, in relation to the score, which is to prove that this student is a hard worker. Study or not, check the family situation (poor), the main point is high English score.
Please be informed that this exhibition has the participation of 47 Malaysian educational institutions. Currently, 180,000 international students are studying in Matabisi. This number of international students has made Matabasi a destination for study in the world, with students receiving degrees from accredited institutions of value and value. Appropriate.
Cambodia tells US that Cambodian constitution does not allow foreign military bases on its territory
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also stressed that the issue of information on the deployment of naval bases off the coast of Cambodia was a rumor arising from the increase in Chinese investment in the coastal area of Koh Kong province. .
This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on November 17, 2018 on the outcome of the meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and US Deputy Secretary of State John Sulllin on November 15, 2018. On the occasion of the 33rd ASEAN Summit and related meetings in Singapore.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also reiterated to the United States that the Royal Government of Cambodia will not violate the Constitution.
Meanwhile, the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia, through the spokesman of General Chhum Socheat, on November 17, 2018, issued a statement rejecting the publication of some foreign media, including the Asia Times. That Cambodia has allowed other countries, most likely China, to use Cambodian territory as a military base.
The statement from the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense came after a number of foreign media outlets, including the Asia Times online newspaper, copied without a clear source that other countries intended to use Cambodian territory as a military base for a naval base and that Cambodia was At the center of the Cold War between China and the United States. Discover another giant planet orbiting a star just 6 light-years away!
On November 15, 2018, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received US Deputy Secretary of State John Sullivan on the sidelines of the 33rd ASEAN Summit. Relevant meetings in Singapore.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and US Deputy Secretary of State discussed the strengthening of Cambodia-US relations and cooperation.
Following are the results of the meeting between Mr. Prak Sokhon and US Deputy Secretary of State: 295 boats participated in the celebration of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns, worshiping the moon and Ok Ambok
Please be informed that the Water Festival, Ok Ambok, Moon Worship and Lantern Floating Festival are always held every year in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The boat race lasts for 3 days, from the 14th and 15th to the 1st day of the lunar month, and at night there are also floating lanterns. As for the Ok Ambok festival to worship the moon god, it is held on the second day only, that is, in the middle of the night on the 15th day of the lunar month.
Officials: Chob Koki checkpoint in Oddar Meanchey province turned into Chob Koki international border checkpoint
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Vat Paranin, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, said that in the area of the Cambodian-Thai border, the Dangrek mountain range is Chob Koki, which used to be a humanitarian checkpoint, but has now been turned into Chob Kokiri International Border Gate. Official.
Mr. Vat Paranin made the remarks at the official inauguration ceremony of the director of the Chob Korki International Border Crossing, Mr. Rem Phal Ravi, in place of Mr. Yoeun Vibol, who will be the Deputy Director of Administration of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Hall. November 16, 2018 at the entrance of Chob Koki checkpoint in Chob Koki North village, Banteay Ampil commune, Oddar Meanchey province.
Mr. Vat Paranin mentioned about the historical background of Chub Koki, that in the past, Chub Koki was a humanitarian channel with little exchange of goods between the people of Cambodia and Thailand. Today, the Koki checkpoint has become an international border checkpoint, which allows the two people to exchange goods on a daily basis.
The Deputy Governor also instructed the new director of the Koki checkpoint, as well as all officials under the Koki checkpoint, to increase internal solidarity and better cooperation with relevant institutions, both the armed forces and the authorities. Territories at all levels, especially cooperation with our neighboring countries, will be more effective forever.
At the same time, Mr. Rem Phal Ravi pledged to strengthen the work discipline and maintain the internal solidarity between the Kokiri border institution and the relevant authorities at all levels in order to strengthen the technical capacity of the management of the international border checkpoint.
