Stung Treng Cam Control Officer Inspects Goods Sold at Exhibition Boards During “E” Boat Race Program in Stung Treng Province
(Stung Treng): On November 17, 2018, Stung Treng CamControl Branch Officer, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and City Hall officials, inspected for chemicals in food and expired goods at Stung Treng Provincial Exhibition Hall. Along the mouth of the Sekong River in Stung Treng to protect the health of the people before the "E" boat race tomorrow.
Mr. Kim Pros, President of CamControl Stung Treng Branch, said that the inspection of goods and food sold at the exhibition booth in the "E" boat race program tomorrow is to protect the health of people who go shopping. Foods that contain chemicals and are out of date cause serious damage to people's health.
He said that because of the booths that sell a variety of food and goods, most sellers and buyers are aware that there are no sellers of defective goods. After inspecting the goods and food at the exhibition booth, the experts confirmed that the goods sold and the food were free of chemicals and out of date.
It should be noted that Stung Treng Camcontrol Branch always cooperates with the Department of Commerce to inspect food at stalls in the province and confiscate many exhibits and burn them.
US Deputy Secretary of State: Improving relations with Cambodia is a US priority
(Phnom Penh): US Deputy Secretary of State John Sulivan has said that enhancing Cambodia-US bilateral relations is a US priority and the United States welcomes the decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia to resume the search for the remains of soldiers. The United States disappeared during the war in Cambodia.
The US Deputy Secretary of State made the remarks during a working meeting with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation, in Singapore on November 15, 2018, during the ASEAN Summit. 33rd.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon responded that through a series of meetings with US leaders, there was an agreement to maintain relations between the two countries and to continue cooperating in various fields with a focus on common interests. The Cambodian Foreign Minister also thanked the United States for providing new concessions for US exports of travel equipment, which could jump to $ 500 million this year.
Mr. Prak Sokhon also told the US Deputy Secretary of State that Cambodia and the United States have different views and understandings on political issues, but that Cambodia and the United States should strive to continue cooperating in areas that are not linked to this political obstacle. And find a way to narrow this difference.
Mr. Hak Sokrin, President of CamControl Battambang Branch, said that the professional officers continue to regularly inspect and educate through the media by putting stickers on the outlets or educating directly about the health effects of food on sale. In the market, inspect all imports, display of defective goods, mix chemicals without a specific date to prevent further traffic on the market.
He also called on people to be careful before buying goods at the market, especially daily food, please check carefully first to avoid damaging goods to harm your health in the future.
