The National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils was registered by the Ministry of Interior by letter No. 842, dated 16 May 2013, after the General Assembly on 27-28 March 2013.
The National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils was established with the aim of enhancing the capacity development capacity of the Capital-Provincial Council and protecting the legitimate interests of its members.
At present, the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils has 25 Capital and Provincial Councils, of which 393 are Capital / Provincial Councilors.
