(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, November 17, 2018, presided over the opening ceremony of the 5th National Conference on Agriculture and Rural Development under the theme "Sustainable Rural Economy. Climate-wise agriculture, processing and agribusiness ”at Prek Leap National School of Agriculture.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated all stakeholders who organized this event to link education and training in the spirit of continuing to contribute to the development of human resources with the potential to respond to the policies of the Royal Government and the needs of the country. National development of agriculture in the context of digitalization and the fourth industrial revolution.
According to the theme of the conference, Minister Veng Sakhon emphasized that the vision for the agricultural sector to 2030 is to modernize agriculture to contribute to food security, poverty eradication and the use of natural resources. "Sustainable."
The Minister stated that in the transition of national economic growth, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has set the main strategic directions to implement, including:
1. Increase productivity, diversify and commercialize agriculture by boosting production of all crops by around 10% per year.
2: Promoting animal production and animal health by promoting animal husbandry at a growth rate of 3% per year, based on the effectiveness of research and dissemination of competitive animal husbandry techniques, increase capacity on animal disease prevention, guarantee Supply of hygienic animal products, quality, safety and sustainability.
3: Promote the development of aquaculture at a growth rate of 15% per year, improve the quality and safety of fishery products for domestic consumption and export, especially the conservation of natural resources and endangered fish.
4: Promoting the management and use of agricultural, forestry and fishery resources to balance conservation and development with brotherhood. Certainly, the Royal Government has been supporting, strengthening and expanding the partnership between all stakeholders, especially the partnership between the state and the state, the state and the private sector to promote agriculture and rural economy to grow.
For example, the Royal Government recently launched a policy on supporting, promoting and developing small and medium enterprises in the agricultural and agro-industrial sectors to create jobs to attract workers to work at the grassroots level. Today's topic is important in the transition of agricultural development and national economic growth.
Some other key points should also be considered, such as:
First, promote the implementation of sustainable agricultural diversification and climate change resilience by incorporating basic ecological principles. At the same time, it is necessary to identify and promote smart agricultural practices and to improve the identification and management of natural risks in line with climate change at all levels.
Second, all measures must be implemented to reduce the destruction of land quality, unsustainable land use, and must continue to work together to determine the appropriate agricultural land area for long-term use goals and to implement relevant principles to achieve natural resource management. Born from sustainable development measures concentrated in ecosystem management and development based on biodiversity.
At the same time, it is necessary to improve the land use policy to help farmers with small farms with equity and maintain the stability of land use and natural resources through diversified agriculture to meet the needs. Practical marketing.
Third, to modernize the curriculum, experiments, research, study materials, continuous capacity building in line with the growth trends of the market and society.
