This Timor's coffee company representative has been working hard to help coffee farmers in Busra commune, Pech Reada district, Mondulkiri province from the beginning until now, he helped them from the first group of farmers, only 5 families and now farmers With the support of his team, there are no less than 40 families, which focus on growing coffee, harvesting and roasting coffee beans.
He said that the buyers of the above countries also have a lot of orders, but the coffee yield collected is not enough to order because most of the coffee of farmers in Busra commune is supplied to the country more than the excess. From 12 tons.
Although farmers have not yet been able to pack their own coffee, he has contacted some of the shops or shops that accept coffee from farmers to help pack later because farmers only buy their own coffee.
In the past, indigenous coffee in Busra commune was also bought from S Cafe in Toul Kork district, Phnom Penh. Until 2018, he will be able to continue to provide financial, material and other means to indigenous farmers in Busra commune, 40 families.
What is even more special is that his Timor Coffee Company also has a budget for farmers to borrow money to grow coffee without interest, of which 120 million riels.
