Zaman International School changed its name to "Paragon International School of Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): Zaman International School, one of the educational institutions in Cambodia, on November 16, 2018, officially announced the change of name to "Paragon Cambodia International".
The announcement of the change of name from Zaman International School to "Paragon Cambodia" International School was made in the presence of Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Chairman of the Honorary Council and Ms. Chea Sophanny, Chairman and sole proprietor of both Zaman International School. 3 languages, including Zaman University in Phnom Penh.
The board said the name change was necessary to bring new strength and energy to the next stage in the education sector, and after much deliberation, the board decided to choose the name of the school. Internationally, "Paragon Cambodia" is an appropriate name for the school's educational identity. The university will be renamed "Paragon International University (Cambodia)" instead.
The school continues to offer the same bilingual education program, with students able to study both Khmer and international language programs. For international students, they have to take the Cambridge test, while students studying in the national curriculum have to follow the same curriculum as public schools.
