Cambodia to host World AIDS Day on December 1, 1 million people die of AIDS each year
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will host the World AIDS Day on December 1, 2018 at the Koh Pich Center in Phnom Penh.
The program will be organized by the AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) in collaboration with government agencies, with an expected number of 1,000 participants.
The doctor said that the day also included a parade at the Koh Pich Center, emotional dance, a parade and a blood test for HIV and the participation of celebrities such as Mr. Khemarak Sereymon comedy group. And many more stars.
According to the doctor, the World AIDS Day on December 1, 2018 is to remind humanity that the war on AIDS is not over every year, there are about 1 million people. The disease has killed more than 1.8 million people.
He said that the event of this day will show to the people of Cambodia that HIV can be prevented and treated for people living with HIV, they can still live a healthy life and have access to support and access to HIV treatment. Properly, too.
He said that currently there are about 67,000 people in Cambodia living with HIV, more than half of whom are receiving support and treatment with AHF support.
Dr. Chhim Sarath hopes that "World AIDS Day will make the fight against AIDS better in Cambodia and around the world."
Dr. Teng Kunthy, Secretary General of the National AIDS Authority, said that the World AIDS Day, which is held on December 1, 2018, the National AIDS Authority has organized a banner ceremony. Roads across the country, 250 banners as well. Each banner will carry a slogan related to HIV / AIDS to remind the public to understand and protect themselves from contracting HIV.
Dr. continued that at the same time, the National Authority also organized a concert at Wat Phnom, as well as the participation of many famous Cambodian singers to sing, dance and dance for the public.
