(Phnom Penh): After the successful implementation of the Royal Government's policy to protect the price of rice from farmers, the Rural Development Bank (RDB), the state specialized bank, plans to request 50 budget packages from the Royal Government. Another million dollars to expand credit to the rice sector.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank, confirmed that the Royal Government's special loan package of $ 50 million through the Rural Development Bank has been disbursed for $ 49 million to support the rice sector. Only $ 1 million left, as more mill owners apply for more loans as the harvest season approaches.
Many rice warehouses and dryers are being put into operation, leading to continued demand for credit, he said.
"Due to the growing demand for credit, the Rural Development Bank will request an additional $ 50 million from the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance to meet the credit needs to support Cambodia's rice industry," said Kao Thach. Decide the policy of the Royal Government.
"The company still wants to consider and continue to support the loan project to the farming community so that he can expand the cultivation in accordance with our contract," he said.
At the same time, according to Mr. Kao Thach, it is planned to turn this Rural Development Bank into a bank that functions as a commercial bank and a bank that serves the policy of the Royal Government in 2019 to get the source Public and government capital and other sources respond to the growth of the digital economy. He said the shift was aimed at providing banking services nationwide, with regional branches and mobile offices as well.
Please be informed that this morning, November 16, 2018, the Rural Development Bank organized the 6th Board Meeting of the 7th Mandate under the chairmanship of Mr. Ros Silva, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Rural Development Bank and Mr. Kao. Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank.
The Board of Directors of the Rural Development Bank met to discuss the draft plan to transform the Rural Development Bank into a commercial bank and a policy bank, with the main goal of serving the development of agriculture and rural economy in line with development. National economy.
The Rural Development Bank was established in 1998 by Sub-Decree No. 01, dated January 21, 1998, in order to fill the gap between demand and supply of financial services in rural areas to contribute to poverty reduction. Of the Cambodian people.
