China, ASEAN join hands to move towards 2030
The "China-ASEAN Strategic Partnership Concept 2030", adopted at the Singapore Conference, has boosted the Bilateral Strategic Partnership towards 2030. This shows that after going through a decade of cooperation in the past and a decade of diamonds in the present, China and ASEAN will continue to work together to accelerate the path to common development. .
"Departure together" comes from both sides having the same expectations and confidence in future development between each other. Economic and trade cooperation has always been a solid foundation of China-ASEAN relations, and a common expectation and trust between the two sides.
"Departing together" is the result of both sides' constant commitment to safeguarding free trade and multilateralism. In communicating with ASEAN countries in the fields of economy and trade, China has always emphasized the principles of mutual benefit and win-win, and has used all means to open up the Chinese market to other countries. ASEAN will also promote the popularity of ASEAN products.
Since China and ASEAN established a strategic partnership 15 years ago, despite the complex international and regional situation, the two sides have made steady efforts to boost bilateral cooperation. Political, economic and trade dialogue, cultural exchanges, humanity and security.
Analysts point out that in line with the launch of the "China-ASEAN Strategic Partnership Concept 2030" in the future, China and ASEAN will deepen the connection between the One Belt and One Road initiative and the community concept. ASEAN 2025 in order to strengthen and expand construction in the three major areas: political security, economic and trade cooperation, as well as human cultural exchanges.
