It should be noted that the hearing on the evidence in Case 002/02 began with the indictment on 17 October 2014 and ended on 11 January 2017. The trial, which included closing statements, lasted a total of 283 days.
During the trial, the Trial Chamber heard testimony from a total of 185 individuals, including 114 factual witnesses, 63 Civil Parties and eight experts. The hearing was well received by the public, with a total of 82,780 people attending and watching the trial live.
The defendants to be tried in Case 002/02 are Nuon Chea, Deputy Secretary of the Communist Party of Kampuchea, and Khieu Samphan, Head of State of Democratic Kampuchea.
The Trial Chamber also heard evidence on allegations of the nature of the armed conflict between Democratic Kampuchea and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, the role of defendants in government, as well as evidence on the administrative structure and communication system of Democratic Kampuchea. .
