Business woman in Kampong Speu province filed a complaint with the prosecutor to arrest a woman who falsified a loan of tens of thousands of dollars and then escaped
(Kampong Speu): A 25-year-old woman named Pheung Sophoan, a resident of Preah Khe Village, Kaheng Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, has filed a complaint with the Provincial Prosecutor to take action and issue an arrest warrant for Duch Chanrasmey. Forgery and use of forged documents as stated in Article 626, Article 627 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that Ms. Sophoan and Ms. Duch Chanraksmey used to collaborate on money laundering together, but later Ms. Sophoan was sued by many business people and the court arrested and imprisoned her. Later, and according to the research, Ms. Sophoan also cheated on a woman named Duch Chanrasmey by falsifying her fingerprints and borrowing tens of thousands of dollars.
Therefore, Phoeun Sophoan, on November 13, 2018, after she was released on bail, filed a complaint with the prosecutor against Duch Chanrasmey, who was on the run.
Ms. Phoeung Sophoan said that in the past, a woman named Duch Chanrasmey was also in the group of pawn shops named Sim Phally, who was responsible for coordinating loans and mortgages together until she was involved in many losses in the past.
Later, it was reported that Duch Chanraksmey lied to customers that the money he borrowed from all the businessmen was given to Phuong Sophoan. But in fact, he did not know this large amount of money, and Duch Chanrasmey took this money from his relatives, escaped to this day and blamed her for falsifying documents that she borrowed. .
Phoeung Sophoan also admitted that there was a lot of money resulting from the loss of Sim Phally Shop, but she was responsible and gradually reimbursed customers as much as possible.
It should be noted that Ms. Phoeun Sophorn was sent to Kampong Speu Provincial Prison on April 27, 2018 on charges of defrauding traders of millions of dollars.
