(Phnom Penh): After the close of the 33rd ASEAN Summit and related meetings full of busy three days ago, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in Wales at around 11 am on the 16th. This November 2018, led the delegation to return to Cambodia.
The 33rd ASEAN Summit was held under the theme "Building ASEAN Innovation and Strength". On this topic, all ASEAN member countries discussed the focus on improving the strength of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations, as well as improving the trade economy in the region.
Although the ASEAN community is valued for its solidarity and respect for the values and interests of its member countries, a number of challenges to ASEAN unity were also raised at the meeting. In his opening remarks at the ASEAN Summit, Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong and ASEAN Chair highlighted a number of notable issues.
In addition to showing the progress of ASEAN, the strength of ASEAN, Lee Hsien Loong raised his concerns about the current competition of the superpowers, which is giving ASEAN member countries different directions to take advantage of. Body.
Despite concerns over the disintegration of ASEAN due to the political, economic, and economic influence of the superpower, the Prime Minister of Singapore expressed hope that all ASEAN member states will continue to unite to achieve a common destiny. .
In the presence of all ASEAN members, the Prime Minister of Singapore expressed confidence that ASEAN would remain strong if not divided. "By uniting in a common voice rather than dividing, all ASEAN members have a strong position in the world," he said. "Through ASEAN, we have the ability to engage and collaborate with major countries and international organizations with the organization of ASEAN meetings such as ASEAN Plus Three and the EAS."
"Through our economic integration, we have helped our people benefit from regional employment and strengthened the value of ASEAN proposals to investors," he added. Today, ASEAN is a major economic player in the world. "With the growth of middle-aged and working-age youth, ASEAN will become the world's fourth largest economy by 2030."
The ASEAN Annual Summit is not only a time for meetings of the top 10 leaders of ASEAN, but also a time for meetings between ASEAN leaders, leaders of world powers and economies. More include the United States, China, Russia, Japan, South Korea, Australia and India. For this year's meeting, it is interesting to note the absence of US President Donald Trump.
Through the ASEAN + US Summit, ASEAN Plus China, ASEAN Plus Russia, ASEAN Plus Australia, ASEAN Plus Japan, ASEAN Plus South Korea, ASEAN Plus India, ASEAN Plus 3 (ASEAN Plus China, Japan, South Korea) and Asia. East leaders, etc., have highlighted the progress of trade relations, as well as the challenges between partners, regional issues and global issues that need to be addressed and improved together.
In both the ASEAN Summit and related summits, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, like other ASEAN leaders, contributed many ideas to improving cooperation and promoting economic growth. Trade as well as address challenges.
Although the 33rd ASEAN Summit and related meetings had many issues to be discussed and resolved, both hot and cold, the ASEAN Summit and related summits were successfully concluded and a statement was issued. Its annual joint venture as well.
Speaking at the closing ceremony, Lee Hsien Loong praised all ASEAN leaders who have done a lot of work for the benefit of the nation in the region over the past year. In particular, together solve all the challenges in promoting internal cooperation with countries outside the region with the brightest results.
The Singaporean Prime Minister also praised Singapore's efforts to address the challenges of achieving the brilliant results of hosting the 32-33 ASEAN Summit and related summits. With the most brilliant results.
It should be noted that according to the principle of rotation according to the Latin alphabet, Thailand is a member country that will be responsible for hosting the 34-35 ASEAN Summit and related summits in 2019.
