Phnom Penh International Airport Completes New 3,000-Meter Runway Project to Improve Air Safety
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh International Airport has been strengthening air safety by completing a project to develop more than 3,000 meters of new runway infrastructure at a cost of more than $ 12 million to meet the growing number of tourists from year to year. Coming to Cambodia, as well as to ensure the safety of landing large aircraft, and also to prepare for the future.
"For Phnom Penh International Airport from January to November 2018, the flight has increased by up to 20% compared to last year with only 50,000 to 50,000 landings," he said. "Only 5,000 aircraft, so the main purpose of the new repairs and upgrades is to ensure a safe landing of all types of aircraft, both now and for the next 15 years."
He said that at Phnom Penh International Airport, there will be further development projects, with the vision of expanding the airport to 10 more places, as well as expanding the reception building, the building for a variety of food and now. A new building is being built to store trucks, supplies, tourists, and fire trucks.
On that occasion, Mr. Soy Sokhan, Undersecretary of State of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, said, "The strengthening of the new runway is the construction of a new runway to modern standards, ensuring high safety and tourist attraction. Well. ”
At the same time, he said that the Royal Government through civil aviation has been examining the feasibility of projects to develop a number of additional domestic airports, such as in Stung Treng, Poipet, Ratanakkiri, and Mondulkiri. Separately, the Royal Government has also decided to build a new airport for Class E in Siem Reap, which can land all kinds of aircraft.
Please note that Cambodia currently has 38 international airlines and 8 domestic airlines operating flights from domestic to foreign. At the same time, it has the capacity to receive 8 million tourists in 2017 and 10 million in 2018, and expects that in 2019, the number of tourists entering and leaving through this international port will increase until To 12 million people.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen brings relics and suffixes to monks at two pagodas in Mondulkiri Province (Video inside) (Mondulkiri): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and the accompanying delegation On the afternoon of November 15, 2018, he offered candles, incense and flowers to Samma Samput and brought the relics, including the suffix, to the monks at Wat Sen Monorom and Wat Preah Puth Mondulkiri in Mondulkiri Province.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit was very generous and Buddhism also gave his personal suffix and gave gifts to the grandparents of the pagoda abbot and a total of 75 students, each of whom received 50,000 Riels and 1 piece of white cloth. Ten thousand riels more.
Please be informed that Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, a clear Buddhist supporter in Buddhism, always leads officials at all levels of the Cambodian Red Cross and many other officials to burn candles, incense, flowers to bring the Buddha and bring many relics, including After that, the monks stayed in the pagodas to support and raise the flag of Buddhism, the state religion.
The noble gesture of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen in Buddhism has been highly praised and appreciated by monks, nuns, pagoda abbots and Buddhists in general.
Please be informed that in addition to the noble gestures in Buddhism by bringing relics and suffixes to the monks at two pagodas in Mondulkiri today, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for the past 2 days on the 14th On November 15, 2018, he also led a delegation to visit and distribute CRC humanitarian donations to nearly 4,000 vulnerable families in Mondulkiri province.
