The King issued a Royal Decree to promote the rank of Major General (2 stars) to Brigadier General Peng Bora, Cambodian National Police.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree ordering the promotion of the rank of Major General (2 stars) to a senior police officer within the Cambodian National Police within the Ministry of Interior. Brigadier General Peng Bora. This is according to the Royal Decree of the King, which was received by Fresh News on November 15, 2018.
Brigadier General Peng Bora, ID 0999, was also appointed by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as a Deputy Director of the Personnel Department with the same status and privileges as the Director of the Department.
Please read the details of the Royal Decree below: Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, November 15: 1,316 illegal vehicles were found and 889 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for November 15, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 7,290 vehicles and found 1,316 vehicles (81% motorcycles), 427 education vehicles and park 889 fines, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,855 helmets and goggles were inspected on November 15, 603 education helmets and 384 helmets were fined.
For the results of the 15-day inspection from November 1 to 15, the police inspected 37,953 vehicles and found 14,459 offending vehicles (82% motorcycles). 011 units and a fine of 11,848 units. Cambodia-Japan Natural Vegetable Garden in Koh Thom District, Kandal Province Inaugurated!
This Cambodian-Japanese natural vegetable garden was established with the cooperation of experts from Japan to grow quality organic vegetables without chemicals based on the principle of public comfort.
In the past, it has been seen that some farmers have grown vegetables with excessive chemicals, which has had a serious impact on people's health. Therefore, to change the cultivation habits of farmers using chemicals and turn to growing vegetables using natural techniques.
On that occasion, the Director General of the Rural Development Bank proposed to establish a pilot natural vegetable garden in Koh Thom district, Kandal province, with the technical cooperation from a team from Japan directly.
In the event that this natural vegetable garden is successfully cultivated, Mr. Kao Thach will request to continue to expand the cultivation to all locations in communes, districts, provinces and in vegetable-producing areas by organizing farmers and vegetable growers into communities, including Fertilizer techniques and help find a market for the community as well.
Mr. Kao Thach strongly hopes that through the presence of the Cambodian-Japanese natural vegetable garden in this geography, it will serve as a model for farmers to positively change their cultivation practices using chemicals instead of natural cultivation, and we can Reduce the import of vegetables containing chemicals from abroad. Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued a sub-decree to appoint two national police officers as Deputy Heads of Personnel Department with the same rank and privileges
In the above sub-decree, the two appointed National Police officers are:
* First: Lt. Gen. Sok Monorom ID 77776 is the Deputy Director of the Personnel Department with the same rank and privileges as the Director of the Department * Second: Brigadier General Peng Bora ID No. 0999 is the Deputy Director of the Personnel Department with the same rank and privileges as the Director Department.
Please read the details in the sub-decree of Samdech Techo Hun Sen below: Representative of Dr. Men Sam An Cremation Ceremony for Mr. Khem Chea Sophoan, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kang Nem, Secretary of State, Ms. Men Sam On, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, presided over the cremation ceremony of Mr. Khem Chea Sophoan, Undersecretary of State at 12 noon. 45 minutes past midnight on Tuesday, the 6th day of the lunar month of Samreth Sak 2562, which falls on November 13, 2018 at the age of 67 due to illness.
The ceremony was held at Wat Tuol Santivan (called Wat Tuol Asa Lok) in Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh on the morning of Thursday, November 15, 2018. Also in attendance were many members of the Armed Forces.
Finally, there was a cremation by Bhikkhu Kosal Rakkhito Ken Sok at the Chief Bishop of Wat Tuol Santivan (called Wat Tuol Asa Lok) as the end of the ceremony.
For the 7-day anniversary program was also held on Sunday, November 18, 2018 at 3:00 pm to meet Buddhists, relatives and close friends to celebrate. Preah Ratanak Trai Samathan Sil invites monks to prosper and give sermons. On the morning of Monday, November 19, 2018, the monks and nuns will be counted as the end of the festival.
33rd ASEAN Summit and related summits close, Thailand to take over ASEAN chairmanship next year
(Singapore): The 33rd ASEAN Summit and related summits held from 13 to 15 November 2018 have concluded with high appreciation from Director Lee Hsien Loong. Minister of Singapore and Chair of ASEAN.
Addressing the closing ceremony, Lee Hsien Loong praised all ASEAN leaders who have done a lot of work for the benefit of the nations in the region, especially over the past year. All the challenges in promoting and promoting internal cooperation with countries outside the region with the brightest results.
After receiving the symbolic wooden hammer as the ASEAN chair in 2019 from the former chair, Thai Prime Minister Gen. Prayuth Chan-o-cha and chair of the 2019 ASEAN Summit expressed his deep gratitude for hosting the event. The 34-35th ASEAN Summit and related summits in 2019 were a resounding success.
The General also respectfully invited and invited all ASEAN leaders to attend the 34-35th ASEAN Summit and related summits in the Kingdom of Thailand in 2019 to explore all means for the benefit and viability. Progress for our region together.
