(Tbong Khmum): For the past two days, the mobile laboratory vehicles of the General Department of CamControl inspected chemicals on vegetables, fruits and food at the markets and border gates in Tbong Khmum province.
On November 15, 2018, CamControl officials brought CamControl mobile laboratory vehicles in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and the Deputy Governor of Memot District, and the authorities inspected 32 samples of vegetables, fruits and food for analysis. Find banned chemicals that cause harm to consumers' health at Memot Market in Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province.
He said that after the inspection and analysis by CamControl's mobile laboratory vehicle on all of the above vegetables, fruits and food, out of the 32 samples, there were 2 samples of boracic acid in the total amount of 15 kg Immediately confiscated from two vendors.
CAMCONTROL officials also instructed, educated and contracted to stop the use of borax (juice) in other dessert products from now on because it will affect the health of consumers.
Khmer Breweries Road Cleaning Truck Starts Cleaning Phnom Penh for Water Festival 2018
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries Road Cleaning Truck has started cleaning the streets in Phnom Penh to welcome national and international tourists to visit Phnom Penh on the occasion of the upcoming Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon. .
To clean this road, the company used four vehicles to clean in Phnom Penh from the 15th to the end of November 2018.
"Every day, we go out to clean up the streets in the city to improve the environment in Phnom Penh," said Hong An, head of the road cleaning team at Khmer Breweries. We have to traffic and clean the road in the sun almost every day. "Even though this work is tiring, we are happy to have contributed to a cleaner environment."
Road cleaning truck drivers are busy clearing roads in Phnom Penh to celebrate the upcoming traditional festival.
He said that we are happy to complete this work to make people happy and enjoy during the Water Festival in the city with a clean environment.
SEOUL: Thirteen fishermen were rescued in time after their South Korean fishing boat sank in a collision with another Japanese fishing boat. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the evening of Thursday, November 15, 2018.
The incident took place at sea about 330 kilometers northeast of the disputed archipelago, which Japan called Takeshima and South Korea called Dokdo. After colliding with a Japanese fishing boat weighing 100 tons, a South Korean fishing boat weighing only 48 tons sank. The 13 South Korean boatmen were rescued by several private company fishing boats present nearby.
The Japanese fishing boat not only did not sink, but no casualties were reported. The South Korean patrol fleet is investigating the cause of the accident.
Capitol Bus Company Donates 2 Million Riels to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police for Cracking Down on 8 Offenders
(Kampong Chhnang): After receiving the information that the police force of Kampong Chhnang province cracked down and arrested 8 perpetrators who threw glass of people's cars on the streets at night in Rolea Bier and Bariboun districts. Capitol Passenger Car Company has donated 2 million Riels to the police as an incentive to successfully prevent this act.
However, the representative of this company also called on the authorities of Kampong Chhnang to help prevent more effective, especially on National Road 5 near the school No. 5, and also called on the authorities of Phnom Penh - Kandal to help prevent On National Road No. 1 around Kbal Koh and National Road No. 6 around Trapeang Chhouk and in Santuk district.
It should be noted that 8 out of 11 perpetrators who always threw the windshield of people's cars on the national road at night in Rolea Bier and Baribon district, Kampong Chhnang province were searched by the police until they were arrested and Building a case to send to court.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Loch Vannara on the afternoon of November 14, 2018, told Fresh News that his police force arrested eight suspects in the case of throwing glass on the night of the 12th. November 14, 2018 Between km 94 to 117, Rolea Bier and Bariboun districts, we have arrested 11 people.
The General Commissioner also ordered all police forces in districts, especially districts with national and major roads to cross, to monitor and prevent this crime from happening again, causing danger to the people. Journey.
According to the commissioner, the suspects carried out these activities: they had a mastermind who was a drug addict and a drug dealer, and all eight of them were drug addicts, so their mastermind used To do this in exchange for drugs. He said the perpetrators were riding motorcycles in reverse and the occupants, who were holding stones, threw stones at cars, mostly trucks and vans.
In this case, a car was seriously injured by a stone. Their activities took place on the night of November 12-13, and last night they tried to continue their activities but were stopped by his police force in time. This was confirmed by the commissioner.
All eight suspects are being questioned at the provincial police commission for drug testing and further offenses, while three others are on the run. The suspects were born and lived in Phsar commune, Bariboun district. After the arrest of the suspects, the police also confiscated some exhibits such as stones and motorcycles that were riding in the activity.
Speaking on the occasion with Mr. Lim Chea Vutha, Executive Director of Fresh News, Mr. Raththy described, “On the night of November 13, 2018, on the program of Radio Free Asia in Khmer, a report was quoted, citing "Some people commented on the response of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to the speculation by Sam Rainsy about the release or non-release of Kem Sokha."
In the report, RFA claimed that the interpreter was a group of lawyers and lawyers, and even referred to a person who had studied law for a doctorate degree as "Dr. Lawyer". Despite the fact that the person is not a lawyer and is not on the list of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The use of the name of a group of lawyers or lawyers does not refer to those who have studied law or have studied law, but refer to those who have legal professional qualifications, including: judges, prosecutors, clerks, clerks, lawyers, associates ... or officials. Or an employee who has worked in the legal field in a state institution or may be a professor with many years of experience and expertise.
On November 15, 2018, the Bar Association of Cambodia issued a statement confirming that Mr. Heang Rithy, former Vice President of the Beehive Social Democratic Party, is not a lawyer registered by the Bar Association.
The Bar Association considered that the call to use the functions, roles and status as a lawyer was different from the truth, misleading the public and causing damage to the honor and dignity of lawyers and the Bar Association. The Bar Association of Cambodia also announced to take action by all means in accordance with legal procedures.
The speech of General Hun Manet on November 15, 2018 on the occasion of the opening of the 25th parachute training course, the closing of the B40-B41 weapons training course, the second generation of air defense weapons and the inauguration of Official use of construction techniques, parachute skills training.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also reminded that all troops must pay more attention to training, tactics, techniques, education, psychology, strengthening discipline, moral character and respect for state law to have sufficient professional skills to respond. Be on time for any problems and situations that arise, as well as the construction of technical structures that serve the training.
According to Mr. HUN Manet, the training and building of human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is a correct and timely response to the Royal Government's policy to reform the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to build and strengthen the defense sector and work. Integrate the army into the international community by building the Cambodian army into a professional army to participate in global missions, defend the territorial integrity and develop the nation.
He stressed that the focus on training is important to ensure the sustainability and effectiveness of all generations of forces in carrying out national defense, territorial integrity and security. At this stage, be prepared to take this golden opportunity to train for generations, and special forces in this era must expand to build features and history for hundreds of years to come.
On this occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet would like to commend and appreciate the achievements of the 911 Parachute Special Brigade in the past, especially on the parachute training that serves other units of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. So far, so good.
It should be noted that the 911 Parachute Brigade has already opened 24 sessions, with 17 units participating and a total of 3,680 participants. The 911 Brigade also participated in many tasks, including the protection of territorial integrity, security, rescue of people.
Samnang Asia Lottery Company officially opens its first branch in Po Sen Chey District, Phnom Penh
The inauguration of the first branch of Samnang Asia Lottery was presided over by Mr. Heng Pheakdey, Managing Director of Samnang Asia Lottery, Mr. Chhin Lucky, Marketing Manager of Samnang Asia Lottery, as well as relevant authorities and guests.
He added that the establishment of the lottery is not only to use the proceeds to support the company, the company has a policy to help the poor, orphans and other schools in need. He added that Samnang Asia Lottery, in addition to the branch in Toul Pong, the company aims to expand to 20 more branches in Phnom Penh and will expand to all 25 provinces.
Please be informed that on the occasion of the opening of the new branch, Samnang Asia Lottery also organizes mosquito nets, dancing, singing, modeling, games, free lottery and many more prizes. Such as refrigerators, air conditioners, microwave ovens, electric cookers and hot water heaters, and the company will continue to create entertainment and raffle for three consecutive days.
