Many butchers have been protesting and asking for talks with CP for about a year since the company started slaughtering pigs for distribution in the market, but failed to find a solution until a debate. A match was held at the Continental Hotel on the afternoon of November 15, 2018.
In the above meeting, the struggling traders asked three big points to the company to immediately stop cutting pigs themselves, which would cause losses to traders, and if they cut themselves, they would have to stop. Put the same price as the price they distribute in the market.
Ms. Hav Chuy Vong, a business owner, said that CP must immediately stop cutting pigs for meat, dumping properly and request that the pigs be weighed properly because they have lost a lot of kilos in the past. .
She added that the company has a lot of money, so it is a pressure on traders. Vendors praised Mong Rithy's company for its good performance, saying that Mong Rithy's company did not cut pigs for its own meat, but in accordance with the principles set by the Royal Government or the Ministry.
Many traders have urged CP to immediately stop the above case, otherwise they will seek justice from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to help solve.
Separately, a representative of CP Cambodia, Mr. Sophat Chanvong, declined to comment on the interview with the media, while the representative of the veterinary officer did not provide an interview.
According to the traders, after going through interrogation and discussion, the veterinary officer said that they will submit it to the upper level for further settlement. Kampong Cham Provincial Commissioner and ACU Disseminate Anti-Corruption Law and Law Amendment to Anti-Corruption Law to Police Officers
(Kampong Cham): Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham, Mr. Keo Thi Vuth, Assistant of the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), on the afternoon of November 15, 2018, disseminated the Anti-Corruption Law and the Law Amendment Law. Anti-corruption to Kampong Cham provincial police officers.
Speaking on that occasion, Major General Em Kosal opened the program and instructed his subordinates to pay attention to and implement the Anti-Corruption Law and the Law on Amendments to the Anti-Corruption Law. Stay away from these acts.
In addition, Mr. Keo Thivuth, Assistant of the Anti-Corruption Unit, disseminated the skills of corruption, bribery, employee bribery and bribery, illegal bidding, misdemeanor offenses, embezzlement offenses. Illegal gain, abuse of power, non-declaration of assets and liabilities, obstruction and interference with the work of the Anti-Corruption Unit and many other crimes.
During the meeting, Mr. Keo Thi Vuth instructed his subordinates to pay attention to prevention, law enforcement and how to file a complaint to the Anti-Corruption Unit.
Please be informed that the above meeting was also attended by the Deputy Commissioner, Mr. Anu Phen, the Chief of the Office, the Deputy Chief of the Office, the Chiefs of the 10 District Police Offices, the Deputy Inspectors, the Chiefs of the 109 Administrative Police Stations, a total of 323 people.
