Minister of Agriculture inspects a mango processing enterprise in Tbong Khmum province with an investment of over 2 million USD
According to the general manager of the company, informed the Minister Veng Sakhon that the company was launched in May 2018 with an investment of more than 2 million dollars, capable of processing mangoes into dried mangoes 300 tons per Months.
The same manager added that on average per day, the company collects mangoes, turmeric from farmers in Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum about 60-100 tons per day and 1 kg at 1200-1600 riels. Most of the finished products are shipped to the Chinese market at $ 5.3 per kilogram.
After inspecting the production line, Mr. Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the company's efforts to contribute to the market for mangoes to farmers through investment in processing mango products for export.
The Minister stated that this activity has really contributed to solving the mango market problem, increasing income, creating jobs for local people, reducing migration and poverty.
According to the report of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, per hectare of mango, turmeric can produce an average of 10 to 20 tons, sold for 10 to 20 million riels per harvest and can be harvested twice a year. Therefore, one year can earn at least 20 million riels.
The status of this income level, in the case of farmers with one hectare of mango land, can be concluded that can meet the vision of the Royal Government, which wants to turn Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030.
Minister Veng Sakhon also stated that the current visit is to present opportunities for farmers to grow mangoes, turmeric for investors to process to export finished products by implementing contract agriculture and especially to encourage and support the sector. The private sector must work with the state (public-private sector) to promote and bring agricultural products to international markets.
Please note that the company is currently negotiating with Australian companies to process cashew nuts and export in the future. The Minister responded to this news and requested and encouraged to consider processing more agricultural products for export. Fresh News TV via Smart TV, PC and mobile
