Some important issues in the region and the world were raised by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the 21st ASEAN Summit with China, Japan and the Republic of Korea
The leaders noted that over the past two decades, our cooperation has grown stronger, broader and significantly contributed to the promotion of peace, security, stability and prosperity in East Asia.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia presented some interests and ideas in response to regional and global issues that require ASEAN and the three partners to participate in solving. The issues raised by Samdech Techo include:
Second. The world and the region have been experiencing more and more frequent disasters. Therefore, Cambodia would like to encourage ASEAN member countries and all three countries to continue to pay more attention to the protection of the environment and natural resources in order to build a strong, Sustainable development in line with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals 2030.
Third. He appreciated the continued strengthening of the mechanisms put in place in the East Asia Analysts and East Asia Business Group and noted all the recommendations that these mechanisms have put in place to promote ASEAN Plus Three cooperation. Better.
Fourth. I am pleased to see that our cooperation in the field of health has improved significantly, especially the launch of the ASEAN Plus Three Leaders' Declaration on Cooperation in Combating Immunity. Will give antibiotics.
In this area of government, I would like to draw the attention of the leaders of ASEAN + 3 countries to the issue of counterfeit and substandard medicines that are causing serious problems to the health and well-being of the people. Counterfeit and substandard medicines are the most hidden killer for the poor and also hinder economic and social development.
The fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs requires better cooperation between all countries in the region. In this regard, Cambodia has proposed to put the fight against counterfeit and substandard medicines on the agenda of ASEAN + 3 cooperation.
Fifth. With the trend of protectionism as well as trade wars that are weakening the free trade system. In this regard, Samdech requested the Plus Three countries to help promote and complete the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) negotiations in 2019.
At the same time, Samdech Techo also welcomed the joint research project on 10 + 3 cooperation for the improvement of supply chain connectivity, which will boost trade and investment and help connect and plan. Regional economic integration.
At the 21st ASEAN Plus Three Summit, ASEAN and Plus Three leaders agreed to issue the 21st ASEAN Plus Three Summit.
ASEAN Plus Three Leaders' Declaration on Cooperation in Combating Immunity to Antibiotics Progress Report on the Implementation of the ASEAN Plus Three Cooperation Plan 2018-2022. Project proposal for a joint study on 10 + 3 collaborative work for improving production chain connectivity.
ASEAN Plus Three Economic Cooperation Work Program 2019-2020. Memorandum No. 15 of the East Asia Analysts Network. Policies for the ASEAN Plus Three Leaders' Meeting, ASEAN Plus Three and External Risks "Supporting Development through Cooperation" and the Minutes of the 16th East Asia Forum.
Health minister calls on parents to get their children vaccinated against hepatitis B at nearby hospitals
(Oddar Meanchey): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, called on all parents or guardians in Oddar Meanchey to get their children vaccinated at hospitals in the province near his home. To protect children and prevent hepatitis B.
The appeal of Prof. Mam Bun Heng on the occasion of his visit to the people who came to receive medical services and are being treated at Oddar Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital on November 15, 2018.
