200 Poor Families in Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok Receive Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross
(Phnom Penh): On November 15, 2018, 200 poor families in Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok received donations from the Cambodian Red Cross.
The donations were handed over to the people by Mr. Mov Manit, Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in Sen Sok District, and Mr. Sak Chankanharith, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch Committee, together with the Governor, Deputy Governor, Khan, Sangkat and Village Civil Servants.
Donation brought as a humanitarian gesture of the Cambodian Red Cross under the leadership of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The donations, including food and some funds, were distributed to 200 poor families from 13 villages in Khmuonh commune, Sen Sok district, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Mov Manit donated 2 million Riels and 200 cases of noodles, Mr. Pov Narith, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, Khan Sen Sok donated 2 million Riels, Mr. Kim Chi and Mr. Tang Sopheavuth, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch Khan Sen Sok donated 2 million Riels and Mr. Sak Chankanharith, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Committee, Khan Sen Sok donated 200 cases of pure water.
In order to ensure the supply of electricity for the operation of the main plants planned to be set up in Stung Hav district, Epichean Tien has decided to set up a coal-fired power plant with a capacity of up to 1,200 megawatts. The construction is scheduled to be completed and can supply electricity by 2020. The power plant was inaugurated this morning.
Zhu Zhang Jing, governor of Epicentian, said the establishment of the coal-fired power plant was part of the company's plan to generate electricity to supply its large industries, which are scheduled to be set up next year. 2019. These include steel mills, copper mills, paper mills, glass mills and some rubber mills.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia has expressed the expectation that his company will invest and create more jobs for Cambodians and make Stung Hav district like Shenzhen in China," he added. "We are capable and confident that in 10 years we will be able to turn this area into a jinn."
