This afternoon, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen continued to visit and distribute gifts to nearly 1,000 more vulnerable families in Mondulkiri province
(Mondulkiri): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and the accompanying delegation on the afternoon of November 15, 2018 continued their visit to visit and distribute humanitarian gifts to the homeless elderly. More than 630 widows, orphans, the disabled and people born or born with HIV / AIDS in Mondulkiri province.
There are 50 Cambodian families, 530 Pnong families and 50 Muslim families from two communes, Sen Monorom and Dak Dam communes of Oreang district, Mondulkiri province.
The invitation to visit and distribute gifts of Samdech Kittipritthbandit was made in Phsar village, Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district, Mondulkiri province.
For each family: 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 sarong, 1 scarf, 1 T-shirt, 1 bottle of water and 1 loaf of bread. At the same time, each family still received a piece of white cloth and another 10,000 Riels as a gift from Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
On November 14th, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen visited and distributed humanitarian aid to 1,358 most vulnerable families from 15 villages in 3 communes of Keo Seima district. Mondulkiri province, which took place in Chhneng village, Sre Khtom commune, Keo Seima district.
The Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit, always takes care of and solves all the challenges of people from all walks of life with compassion, consideration and gives hope and confidence to the general population who face difficulties without any problems. Discrimination does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion or political affiliation. Wherever there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross.
