The President of the Constitutional Council of Cambodia stated: "Samdech Techo is not only a hero of national liberation, but also a hero who has built peace and victory for Cambodia [... "Samdech Techo is also a heroic engineer who has left a lot of achievements for the people of Cambodia, especially this win-win monument."
Mr. Im Chhun Lim added that not only that, the Victory Monument is a very important symbol to show to the international community that Cambodia has peace, full political stability, these are due to the merits of Samdech Techo and the CPP. Cambodia, which has sacrificed everything to exchange peace and prosperity in all areas for Cambodia from the dark regime of Pol Pot, which destroyed Cambodian society like ashes.
Please be informed that recently, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has publicly announced that Samdech will hold a New Year celebration for 3 nights and 3 days from December 29 to 31, 2018. At the Victory Monument to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War through a win-win policy with the first territorial unity.
Colonel Chim Sitha said that the suspect was Thach Sour, a 48-year-old Cambodian man living in a house with no number in Borey Kamakor village, Sangkat Cheung Ek, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. The suspect was arrested in Sambo Meas Village, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor on November 15, 2018 at 11:10 AM.
According to the colonel, the reason for stabbing the victim to death was due to a land dispute, and before the incident, the victim attacked the suspect, causing the suspect to defend himself by pulling out a knife. On the victim at once. According to the suspect's confession.
Please be informed that at 11:00 pm on November 13, 2018, Mr. KET Sitha, 53 years old, Chief of People's Protection of Tali Village, Sangkat Cheung Ek, Khan Dangkor, was stabbed with 3 knives, causing the victim to die on the street. When sent to the rescue at the Russian hospital.
The suspect and the victim were drinking together at a shop along Prey Sar Road, and while drunk, there was little argument about land grabbing. Until 11:00 pm, they asked each other to continue drinking at the victim's house, but when riding in the middle of the road, the suspect intercepted a knife and stabbed the victim with three knives, causing his death when he was taken to the hospital. The suspect escaped after the incident.
After this case, the Dangkor district police force, led by Colonel Chim Sitha, deployed its forces to search for and arrest the killer. In less than two days, the police followed the killer and immediately sent him to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to continue the procedure.
In addition, the General Commissioner also instructed all police forces to take control of the situation in the local area and if any situation arises to report to the upper level immediately.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun: The National Police Force must not wear uniforms and threaten innocent people, but must be a good service provider
(Kampong Speu): Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, said that the National Police Force must not wear uniforms and use its power to threaten innocent people, that is, to be a good and effective service provider. Citizens in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The remarks of Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun were made this morning, November 15, 2018, on the occasion of the closing of the Special Intervention Course at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School in Treng Trayeung Commune, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province. Nearly 200 trainees of the National Police participated in the training.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said, "The police force must be moral, ethical and most importantly respect the professional conscience because we were created to save the people at the time of the incident." "Intervention forces have the role of intervening to save people and the environment, the social situation, but not a force acting like a tiger to threaten, without taking to threaten the fear of citizens and society."
As a special intervention force, the General emphasized the need to implement orders to be sharper, more honest and more gentle, more moral, more religious, more lenient, because the policy of the National Police Force is important in the future: "We will "Let the National Police Force be a professional service, serve the people with loyalty, virtue and morality."
In addition, the Deputy Commissioner stressed that for the training of special intervention skills to be more effective during the operation, all police forces must have the highest will and spirit, and at the end of this training must be focused. The highest attention.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Un On, Deputy Chief of Staff and Director of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School also made a report showing that in order to measure the ability of the trainees in this course, the school conducted a final exam in both theory and practice. Practice on the field to give points to each participant, plus the discipline of living ethics.
The principal added that after studying for almost three months, the school organized an exam program to measure the level of ability, found that 134 participants were eligible for the exam, 5 were not eligible for the exam and the participants were removed from the exam. 05 students, of which 25 received good grades, 62 moderately good grades, 44 average grades and 8 weak grades.
(Preah Vihear): A suspect was arrested by the police of Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province and confiscated 36 small and large packages of drugs. The suspect was arrested on November 14, 2018 at Romdeng point in Trapeang Tontum village, Romtom commune, Srok Vieng district, Preah Vihear province.
This morning, November 15, 2018, Lieutenant Colonel Say Det, Police Inspector of Rovieng District, said that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Ly Heng, alias Atom, male, 35 years old, false occupation, living in Khang Khang village. On. Authorities also confiscated 31 small and large packages of drugs.
The district inspector said that before the incident, a woman called him to intervene in the case of her husband abusing her. After receiving a complaint from the woman, the police arrived at the scene, then the perpetrator, her husband, escaped for fear of being arrested.
He added that while the police were working, suddenly one of the suspects, who was a drug addict with a house nearby, shouted Lola without being afraid of the police. Seeing this, he ordered his arrest and called the family to cooperate in searching the suspect's body. At that time, the police found 30 small packages of drugs and 1 large package hidden in the wallet.
