A South Korean fishing boat weighing 48 tons sank shortly after colliding with a Japanese fishing boat at 9:38 a.m. Thursday. Rescuers at the scene have rescued 13 South Korean boat workers and are searching for some of them who are still missing.
The Japanese fishing boat did not sink after the collision, and Japan claimed no one was missing or injured as rescue operations for South Korean fishermen continued. The cause of the accident has not been confirmed.
