(Phnom Penh): Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, former President of the Khmer Rouge Party, on November 15, 2018, announced to ask Mr. Sam Rainsy, former President of the Opposition Party to bet on political life.
In this bet, Mr. Suon Serey Ratha believes that Mr. Sam Rainsy will lose to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and will not dare to enter the country forever unless there is an apology from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In this case, he placed the condition that if Sam Rainsy dared to enter the country without amnesty, Suon Serey Ratha would end his political life, but if he did not, Sam Rainsy would have to end his political life.
Please note that Mr. Suon Serey Ratha's bet came out after Mr. Sam Rainsy on November 9, 2018 took the political life of Mr. Kem Sokha to ask Samdech Techo Hun Sen to bet.
Claiming that foreign pressure would cause Samdech to pardon Kem Sokha, Mr. Sam Rainsy set a bet that "if Kem Sokha is released on December 29, 2018 or at least March 3, 2019 "Samdech Techo must resign, but if not released, Mr. Sam Rainsy volunteered to face the law by the authorities to arrest him to serve his sentence in prison."
National Assembly Holds Plenary Session to Approve 2019 Budget Law and Some Draft Laws
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 15, 2018, the National Assembly convened its first plenary session of the sixth legislature to discuss and approve the draft law on finance for management in 2019 and other draft laws. The session was chaired by National Assembly President Samdech Heng Samrin and attended by 115 members of the National Assembly.
The agenda to be discussed in the session is:
2: Draft law on the payment of the general state budget for management in 2017.
3: Draft Law on the Approval of:
* Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of fiscal evasion with respect to taxes on income.
* Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Indonesia on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of fiscal evasion with respect to taxes on income.
4. Draft Law on the Approval of the Extradition Treaty between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Continues to Lead a Working Group to Inspect the Construction Process of a Win-Win Monument as the Inauguration Day Approaches
(Phnom Penh): With only 45 days left until the inauguration of the Victory Monument, on November 15, 2018, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Committee for the Construction of the Win-Win Monument, continued to lead The Win-Win Monument Construction Team continues to inspect the construction process of the Win-Win Monument in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
Along with the inspection of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, the participation of Mr. Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, led a delegation to visit the Victory Monument to learn more about the meaning and construction. This magnificent monument of the 21st century.
After the construction of the Victory Monument is nearing completion, it is seen that the leaders of some major institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia led their delegations to visit and learn about the meaning of this Victory Monument. No.
As always, Samdech Pichey Sena, the Chairman of the Working Group, always leads inspections to make sure that this monument, which is a symbol of peace and unity of the Khmer nation, is built in all aspects and on time of the celebration day according to the President's schedule. Of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Reverse riders at the Independence Monument roundabout continue to occur almost every day, despite the fact that the authorities and the authorities deployed forces to intercept day and night, in fact, last night, November 14, 2018, law enforcement and Authorities seized five vehicles and sent them to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
Currently, the vehicles have been sent to the Office of Land Traffic of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for further instruction on the procedures. Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended a banquet hosted by the Prime Minister of Singapore.
(Singapore): After several busy meetings on the evening of November 14, 2018, the Prime Minister of Singapore Lee Hsien Loong and his wife held a banquet with the highest honor to the Head of State. Heads of Government of ASEAN and all ASEAN Parties, as well as ASEAN Senior Officials and Delegates
He said that all ASEAN leaders have spent a lot of time together to build an ASEAN community in 2015, and for the future will continue to work together and continue to work together in the future. Addressing all challenges for the glorious future of the region, especially for all of our people.
"Under the theme of building innovation and resilience in ASEAN, we will continue to deepen our discussions on the morning of April 28 for the benefit of our region and our people," he said. The leaders also watched a dance performance by a Singaporean masses.
The meeting was attended by leaders of many Asian and European countries. The ASEAN Heads of State / Government congratulated the Ministers of the Comprehensive Economic Partnerships for achieving significant results in the establishment of a large free trade area in Asia as well as in the world. .
The leaders also considered that the geopolitical and economic changes of the world, the establishment of a comprehensive free trade area is very important to make the Asian economy become a core economic pole, help maintain political stability and Stabilizing the global economy and helping to prevent protectionist policies and the spread of trade wars.
Addressing the leaders of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership, the Prime Minister said that although Cambodia is a least developed country, Cambodia urges the negotiators to overcome obstacles in each sector to complete the mandated negotiations provided by the leadership. Of a wide range of economies, although Cambodia needs to reform some normative documents and provide a lot of coordination with other partner countries.
"Cambodia maintains its position and agreement with the leaders of all major economies that the Comprehensive Economic Agreement must be modern, comprehensive, of high quality and beneficial to all members," he said. "Even though those benefits are not shared equally due to differences in size and economic situation, as well as due to different levels of competitiveness."
All the leaders present at the Summit on the Comprehensive Economic Partnership agreed to issue the Chairman's Statement and the Ministerial Report of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Leaders' Meeting.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's assessment was made at the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit on November 14, 2018 in Singapore. The meeting was attended by 10 ASEAN leaders, including Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe. The ASEAN Heads of State / Government warmly welcomed Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe at this important 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit.
The Heads of State / Government of all ASEAN countries are pleased to see that ASEAN-Japan cooperation has made remarkable progress over the past 45 years. In this spirit, all ASEAN leaders welcomed and supported the release of the Joint Statement on the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit to Celebrate the 45th Anniversary of ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation.
At the same time, ASEAN leaders also supported the continued close work between ASEAN members and Japan to implement the revised implementation plan of the Vision on ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation, which was approved in August 2017, fully and effectively. Effectively aim to strengthen and deepen the cooperation and strategic partnership between ASEAN and Japan.
ASEAN and Japan leaders also expressed satisfaction over the growth of ASEAN-Japan trade volume to 217.9 billion US dollars in 2017. This clearly shows that Japan remains an important economic partner of ASEAN.
Like other ASEAN leaders, the Prime Minister said that in the spirit of increasing the size as well as expanding the scope of ASEAN-Japan trade, Cambodia welcomes the signing of the first protocol to amend the agreement on A comprehensive economic partner between ASEAN and Japan.
In addition, Cambodia appreciates Japan's significant contribution to ASEAN community building and ASEAN integration through the Japan Fund for ASEAN Integration, as well as its continued support for the implementation of the ASEAN 2025 Master Plan and the Work Plan. Third, the Initiative for ASEAN Integration 2016-2020 to reduce the development gap in the region. In particular, support for ASEAN human resource development and the promotion of people-to-people contacts.
At the meeting, ASEAN leaders also praised Japan's support for the ASEAN Middle East and noted Japan's open and open Indo-Pacific strategy, and encouraged continued dialogue to build better understanding. .
At the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit, the leaders of the ASEAN-Japan countries agreed to issue a statement by the President of the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit.
Joint Declaration of the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit to Celebrate the 45th Anniversary of ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation Briefing Report on the Progress of the Implementation of the Vision Statement on ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation and the First Protocol of the ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement.
ASEAN leaders also considered the meeting to be an unprecedented forum under a very important theme for the region and the world in the current economic and trade environment.
ASEAN leaders stressed that in response to the escalation of protectionist tendencies, unilateral trade activities and trade wars, ASEAN is working to deepen regional economic integration by accelerating Free trade.
ASEAN has been working hard to promote a comprehensive economic partnership in the region, which is a testament to ASEAN's commitment to trade liberalization and economic integration. At the meeting, the leaders agreed to issue a statement by the chairman of the luncheon hosted by Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong.
Chinese Foreign Ministry Holds Press Conference on Chinese President Xi Jinping's Visit
In Papua New Guinea, he will meet with leaders of Pacific island nations that have established diplomatic ties with China.
Speaking at a press conference, Chinese Vice Foreign Minister Zheng Zeguang said that Chinese President Xi Jinping's visit to the South Pacific is important to deepen friendly cooperation between the two countries. China and Papua New Guinea enhance the level of relations between China and the Pacific island countries, as well as promote cooperation and solidarity between developing countries.
Speaking at the press conference, Li Chenggang, Vice Minister of the Ministry of Commerce of the People's Republic of China, said that this year's APEC conference is expected to achieve a number of achievements, first of all Divided into two parts, it promotes the construction of a network of electronic border crossings, which is a model area in the Asia-Pacific region for new development.
On the other hand, global value chain cooperation will be a major achievement and will create an APEC trade value database. Second, it will deepen the process of regional economic cooperation and promote the development of the Asia-Pacific Free Trade Area. Third, it will contribute to the economic and trade sectors to achieve the post-2020 co-operation concept.
