Forestry Administration and Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Crack Down on a Luxury Timber Truck
(Stung Treng): A large amount of rosewood was smuggled by a Samsung truck and processed by the Provincial Gendarmerie in cooperation with the Forestry Administration of Dong Kralor Sangkat while transporting rosewood from the district. Siem Pang towards the target province.
The crackdown on Samsung vehicles transporting luxury wood was carried out in the early morning on November 14, 2018 on the road to Sdao commune, in Kilometer 8 village, Sangkat Samaki, Stung Treng city.
Mr. Suon Mengly, Chief of Dong Kra Forestry Administration Sangkat, said that the Samsung car that was seized by the force was a processed vehicle with both bottom and roof stolen from Siem Pang district in all forms and then transported through Samsung to the market. Of the target province.
He said that because the team received information that a Samsung truck transporting luxury wood illegally, the force also cooperated with the provincial military police to crack down, while Tai Kong escaped.
Dong Kralor commune chief said that the Samsung car that was confiscated by professional officers was taken to be stored in the provincial forestry administration. So far, he said, 330 pieces of rosewood, small and large, equal to 4 cubic meters, have been confiscated, along with two large islands, and the Minister of Agriculture told a senior official of the Asian Development Bank about the problem. Some Challenges of Cambodia's Agriculture Sector
He said that the challenges include marketing of agricultural products, technology before and after the harvest, physical infrastructure, processing technology, packaging, use and management of agricultural water, market information, etc.
Mr. Veng Sakhon added that in order to solve all these problems, the Ministry as well as the Royal Government has been making great efforts through the formulation of policies, action plans, infrastructure construction, human resource training, technical dissemination and regulation. Encourage investors to build partnerships between the private sector and farmers, communities or small enterprises, and support the transition from farmers to agribusinesses.
