Good opportunity! The National Employment Agency will hold a job forum tomorrow to provide 935 job opportunities
This November Job Forum is being held at the National Employment Agency (NEA) at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training from 8:00 am to 5:00 pm.
Mr. Aing Phea, President of the Phnom Penh Job Center, stated that "Organizing job forums is an important part of finding jobs for students and job seekers that are most effective. "This program will give participants the opportunity to choose their favorite companies and jobs and apply and interview directly with human resources officers from companies."
Mr. Aing Phea called on companies that are in need of recruitment to cooperate with the National Employment Agency to conduct direct recruitment on a monthly basis.
For students and job seekers, do not forget to prepare a CV to apply for a face-to-face interview with a representative from the company and know the results immediately on the spot.
(China): China's transportation sector is looking at ways to reduce the volume, standardize and commercially recycle paper cartons in order to reduce pollution.
Sunfeng set up the company's first laboratory in 2013 to find environmentally friendly materials for cardboard and scotch production. This year, a new type of reusable case has been developed.
Yao Hongshu, deputy general manager of Sunfeng Express Beijing, said the case saves a lot of paper and the design has a lot of users. In fact, the 10 million boxes in use today can replace the old 500 million cases.
He said SunFeng Express had been using 8,000 electric vehicles instead of conventional gasoline vehicles for the past two years. These electric cars are being used in more than 30 cities such as Beijing, Shanghai and Shenzhen.
He said that in the next few years, the company plans to use 15,000 electric cars for transportation. When using electric cars, they can save about 30,000 tons of gasoline and reduce emissions by more than 100,000 tons.
But these carriers have not yet been able to turn to environmentally friendly raw materials because of their high cost, he said. However, this is still a target for shipping companies in China.
At the moment, it's too expensive for all carriers to switch to environmentally friendly boxes because these new, less environmentally friendly raw materials are expensive, he said. Fees.
