The support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made during the 3rd ASEAN-Russia Summit held on November 14, 2018.
This important meeting was attended by 10 ASEAN leaders and the President of Russia. ASEAN leaders considered that the presence of the Russian President not only reflected Russia's strong interest in ASEAN-Russia relations, but also strengthened the ties.
Addressing ASEAN-Russia leaders, Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung praised the remarkable progress of ASEAN-Russia cooperation. Especially after the successful organization of the ASEAN-Russia Anniversary Summit in 2016 in the Russian Federation in Kyrgyzstan.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged both sides to make more efforts to achieve the ASEAN-Russia Comprehensive Action Plan 2016-2020 to accelerate and deepen bilateral cooperation. The Prime Minister also said that regular summits between ASEAN and Russia should be held to strengthen and deepen ASEAN-Russia cooperation.
At the 3rd ASEAN-Russia Summit, ASEAN and Russia leaders agreed to issue a statement by the Chair of the 3rd ASEAN-Russia Summit. ASEAN-Russia Leaders' Declaration on Cooperation in Information Security, Communication and Technology and in the Use of Information and Communication Technology
