Mr. Suon Serey Ratha expressed his pity for Mr. Kem Sokha who was deceived by Mr. Sam Rainsy as a political tool
(Phnom Penh): While directly insulting Mr. Sam Rainsy as a "political prostitute fleeing the country", Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, former President of the Khmer Rouge Party, on November 14, 2018, expressed his condolences to Mr. Kem Sokha, former The former president of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, who was deceived by his strategic partner, Sam Rainsy, as a political tool until he was imprisoned and suffered alone while Sam Rainsy was living abroad.
With compassion for Kem Sokha, who deprived his wife and children of previous incarceration and physical illness, Suon Serey Ratha, a politician who was imprisoned for insulting the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, lamented that Only those who have been imprisoned understand the feelings of Kem Sokha now.
Suon Serey Ratha said: "Although I am not in the political party with Kem Sokha, but as a former political prisoner who has been imprisoned, I know the feelings of politicians who are living in detention and emotions. Of family, wife, children who want their husbands and fathers to be free. "Only politicians who have been imprisoned in the same way know and understand this feeling."
Immediately responding to this request, on the evening of November 9, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced through Fresh News that he decided to bet with Mr. Sam Rainsy. Samdech determined that if Sam Rainsy loses this bet, he must dare to be arrested to be punished immediately after the bet is over. Is to walk
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, appealed to the owners of truckers who use trucks to enter Phnom Penh on the day of the Royal Water Festival, Ok Ambok, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon, which will be held from November 21-23, 2018, and for those who come to visit, do not drive to the venue to avoid traffic jams.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's appeal was made on the afternoon of November 14, 2018 during the inspection of the lanterns of Phnom Penh Capital Hall on the east side after the meeting to maintain security and good order during the festival. Om Touk, Ok Ambok, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon god.
The Governor of Phnom Penh said, "I would like to inform and inform all people who wish to enjoy the Royal Water Festival, please follow the instructions of the police as well as local authorities to prepare. "Parking and traffic and we will have some areas closed to the public for pedestrians."
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, on November 19, 2018, Phnom Penh Capital Hall will open a test boat race and will hold a Krong Pali ceremony according to the religious tradition to ask for all the people and lead to the celebration of the King. Official ceremonies as well.
