Mr. Khim Bunsong chaired a meeting of the Water Festival Organizing Committee in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Mr. Khim Bunsong, Governor of Siem Reap Province, on November 14, 2018, chaired a meeting of the Water Festival Organizing Committee in Siem Reap Province with the participation of the Board of Governors. Provinces and leaders of departments, units, municipal authorities.
The provincial governor also said that the organization of the Water Festival, floating lanterns to worship the moon and Ok Ambok is to commemorate and respect the heroism of the ancestors of the navy who sacrificed their lives in the war on the water. Defeating invading enemies and winning for our motherland Angkor.
After the report of each sub-committee on the activities and results implemented, in which the Secretariat of the Provincial Water Festival Organizing Committee said that 31 boats have applied to participate in the competition, with a capacity of 22 boats. There are 5 female boats and lanterns from departments, units and companies.
The meeting also focused on security, public order, sanitation, health, environment and electricity, as well as the accommodation of athletes.
During the Water Festival, the Provincial National Festival Committee also set up booths for traders wishing to come and shop during the Water Festival, continuing from the end of the Water Festival with music performances for national and international guests. Also, after the sub-committee and district authorities, the unit raised some points to participate in the Water Festival, focusing on environmental issues, traffic lights and mobile toilets during the festival.
The Governor of Siem Reap Province emphasized on cleaning and sanitizing the environment, especially for electricity, to continue lighting in booths and music venues until November 23, 2018, and asked all departments, units as well as companies without boats to participate in the competition. Please support those boats in order to promote culture, traditions and national participation as well as participate in the development of tourism in this historic land.
