(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chan Chesta, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry, said that in 2018, Cambodia is ranked No. 1 in the rice sector, so farmers in the community must produce high-value rice seeds in accordance. Company introduction: The factory accepts the purchase and requirements of the local market and exports.
A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture said this at the signing ceremony of agricultural contracts for the production and supply of rice between Amru Rice and nine agricultural communities at the Clareus Hotel, Stung Sen, Kampong Thom province this morning, November 14, 2018.
Song Saran, CEO of Amru Rice, said the company had signed contracts with 48 farming communities in the past. Among them, there are 10 cashew communities and today signed contracts with 9 more communities in Kampong Thom province to complete the procurement of 50,000 tons by the company during the end of 2018.
He said that until November 14, the company has signed contracts with 56 rice farming communities in seven provinces with agricultural potential. In addition to the contracts with these 56 communities, the company continues to procure rice from small and medium-sized mills that they have not yet exported, and most importantly, the rice varieties are good in accordance with the techniques and standards of the export market.
At the same time, Mr. Nher Ban Kheng, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, said that the signing ceremony was very important to provide farmers with a clear market opportunity to grow agricultural crops, especially the rice sector, which is not on Merchant lips.
He asked the agricultural community and the buyer to trust each other by respecting the contract. General Department of Taxation reminds people to hurry to pay tax on means of transportation and all kinds of vehicles for 2018 before November 30!
