Samdech Tea Banh Conversation with a group of artists who will sing at the inauguration of the Win-Win Monument
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on the afternoon of November 14, 2018, met with Cambodian artists in order to mobilize famous Cambodian artists to support the inauguration of the Victory Monument. Celebrate the 20th anniversary of the upcoming win-win political day.
The meeting was held at the Friendship Building of the Office of the Council of Ministers, which was attended by a large number of relevant institutions, including the Ministry of National Defense, famous artists in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
This Victory-Day Political Day celebration will be held for 3 days from December 29 to 31, 2018 to be more solemn in line with the achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia in all fields. In the last 20 years, through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 31, announced publicly that he will hold a New Year celebration for 3 nights and 3 days from December 29 to 31, 2018. Coming soon at the Victory Monument to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War in a win-win policy by gaining territorial unity for the first time.
The construction of this Victory Monument is to commemorate the merits of Khmer ancestors of all times who sacrificed their lives in the cause of the motherland. Moreover, this monument is also a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war. In addition, this monument will be a legacy for future generations.
20 Million Riel Prize from 2 Pink Toothpaste to Another Factory Worker in Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): A young woman named Tim Saveth, 32 years old, a worker at Win Star Su shoe factory in Prey Rong village, Pheary Meanchey commune, Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province, was lucky to win a grand prize of 20 million Riels from toothpaste. Two more pink bouquets.
Speaking to the team that handed over the prizes directly to the house, Ms. Tim Saveth, who became the owner of 20 million Riel, said that for a long time, she has always supported and used toothpaste to remove two lotus flowers regularly because It can cure gum disease, whiten teeth and eliminate bad breath.
But recently, after using all the toothpaste, she bought two more pink toothpaste to use at the factory and the sticker in the box also found a prize of 20 million riels. Suddenly, she was very happy and told her family and called the company via the phone number in the box.
Ms. Tim Saveth also stated that after receiving the big prize of 20 million Riel, she will take some to pay off debts and leave some for living in the future.
(Phnom Penh): The Boeung Kak II Administrative Police Station of the Tuol Kork District Police Inspectorate cracked down on and arrested a suspect in the case of stealing pieces of wood in a Vietnamese wood shop, which was closed by a court in 2016. The arrest took place on November 13, 2018 at 11:40 AM at 4C, Street 616, Group 85, Village 18, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
According to the report of the district police inspector, Mr. Sok Heng, the suspect, Sem Pov, male, 24 years old, Khmer, unspecified occupation, unspecified residence, was sleeping on a tricycle. The suspect was born in Doung Thom village, Kork Prich commune, Kirivong district, Takeo province.
The house was closed by the court in the afternoon in connection with drug offenses during 2016. The owner of the house is John Khun En, male, about 40 years old, Vietnamese, wood carpenter, 4C, Street 616, Group 85, Village 18, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, who escaped with his family. Forces from the Anti-Drug Department of the Ministry of Interior conducted a crackdown operation.
Currently, the suspect has been sent to the Tuol Kork Police Inspectorate for legal action.
