(Banteay Meanchey): This morning, November 14, 2018, Mr. San Vichea Saravuth, President of CamControl Banteay Meanchey Branch, led several relevant officials to continue the inspection of various goods that can easily affect everyone's health. At the markets on the Cambodian-Thai border, at Tumnup K5 Market, Sangkat Poipet and Prey Kob Market, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet City.
Mr. San Vichea Saravuth stated that no matter how remote or distant the place, as long as there is a variety of stalls, stalls, markets, and houses in Banteay Meanchey province, it is strictly forbidden by professional officials this morning. Collected and confiscated: 447 small packets of noodles, 8 bottles of rabbit acetic acid, 1 can of condensed milk, and 5 bottles of orange juice to be burned.
The president continued, "The problem of crushed noodles is a problem. Our professional officers always chase and strictly ban the display and consumption, because the crushed noodles are collected by corrupt traders and processed from the good noodles and they fall on the ground." "And the other is unhygienic, but all these traders think it is useful not to think about health, harm to human health, even knowing that the noodles are unhygienic."
(Phnom Penh): The mastermind of an armed robbery, a former military officer and his wife, who had been involved in many cases, was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Bureau of Serious Crimes in cooperation with the Kampong Speu Provincial Police under the coordination of Mr. Oum Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor. Phnom Penh was first arrested on a warrant issued by the Kampong Speu Provincial Court.
The arrest of the two suspects, the couple, took place this morning, November 14, 2018, on Beto Street 93z, Phsar Touch Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The suspect, Hat Chhay alias Hak Chhay, a 42-year-old former military officer, lives at 369, Street 93z, Samaki Village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, his hometown is Kampong Kdei Village, Kampong Reap Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
Authorities told Fresh News that the arrest of the two suspects was made in accordance with the arrest warrant No. 4221 dated November 9, 2018, issued by Mr. Ou Phat, a representative of the Kampong Speu Provincial Prosecutor's Office. There is a serious case of theft in Kampong Speu province.
The arrest was made while the suspect was driving a CRV with a couple on Beto Street 93z, Phsar Touch Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke 1, Khan Russey Keo. Police found a PCX motorcycle, a K54 handgun, several bullets, a credit card and 14 motorcycles, a license plate and some related items.
After detaining the two suspects, the couple sent their wives home because there was no involvement in the arrest warrant, and the suspects were sent back to the Kampong Speu Provincial Police, which is the owner of the case.
On behalf of the Royal Government and on behalf of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, through the Ambassador, the Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the United States Government for its excellent support in the development process of Cambodia.
In fact, the United States Agency for International Development (USAID) has provided technical and financial support to implement projects related to agricultural development, including:
First, the Horticultural Project (2017-2022) with a total value of 17.5 million USD, focusing on building capacity to find agricultural markets, improving markets for horticulture, improving good governance.
Second, the project to build a partnership between USAID and the Royal University of Agriculture with $ 1 million in order to build institutional capacity and develop human resources, the participation of students, government officials and the private sector.
Fourth, the project on fish farming in the field (2016-2021) has more than 6 million dollars to be implemented in Pursat, Battambang, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom. In order to improve the fish farming system in the field, increase the scope of sustainable fish production.
The Minister stated that through the results obtained from the implementation of various projects, the agricultural sector has continued to grow remarkably, and this growth has greatly contributed to raising living standards, increasing incomes, improving and maintaining Preserve the environment, get new technologies to apply to increase production productivity, ensure food security, nutrition, reduce migration and reduce total dependence on natural resources, etc.
Through the Ambassador, the Minister hopes and believes that the US Government will continue to fully support the Royal Government of Cambodia in developing the country for sustainable development, especially the US private sector will invest in agriculture. More and more in the future to achieve the vision of 2030 is a high middle income country.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo and the Heads of State / Government of ASEAN countries on November 14, 2018 attended the opening ceremony of the 20th ASEAN-Republic of Korea Summit. .
At the summit, the ASEAN Heads of State / Government warmly welcomed the President of the Republic of Korea, Moon Jae-in, to attend the ASEAN Annual Summit.
The 20th ASEAN-ROK Summit was held under the theme "Review of ASEAN-ROK Cooperation and Future Directions". Interventions and perspectives on ASEAN-Republic of Korea relations on three key points, including:
* First, Cambodia welcomes the proposal to hold a meeting to commemorate the 30th anniversary of the ASEAN Dialogue Partnership in the Republic of Korea in 2019 in the Republic of Korea. Cambodia also noted with pleasure the intention to upgrade the Mekong-Republic of Korea Summit to the Summit and host the 1st Mekong-Republic of Korea Summit in conjunction with the 30th Anniversary Meeting of the Partnership. ASEAN-Republic of Korea Dialogue
Cambodia will continue to work closely with ASEAN member countries and the Republic of Korea to achieve fruitful summits to further boost our cooperation.
* Second, Cambodia welcomes the new South Korean policy of the Republic of Korea, which aims to enhance relations between ASEAN and the Republic of Korea and establish a community based on three pillars: people, prosperity and peace. Cambodia also hopes that this policy will complement other policies in the region and serve the interests of our two regions as well as the people as a whole.
The implementation of the Joint Statement of the United States Summit, the Democratic People's Republic of Korea and the Panmunjom Statement, as well as the Pyongyang Joint Declaration requires patience. Recent developments are encouraging and unprecedented in the history of the Korean Peninsula.
