80% of people in the world have back pain that occurs in people who work long hours in the office.
(Phnom Penh): A specialist doctor from Vietnam, Professor Jin Minh Chi, a neurosurgeon at Ho Chi Minh City Choray Hospital, confirmed that according to a study by chiropractors in 2018, it is clear that people in the world About 80 percent of them have back pain for sure, and a high percentage of these conditions occur in people who work long hours in the office.
The statement from the Vietnamese doctor was made during a free screening and treatment program for 50 chiropractors at Choray Hospital in Phnom Penh on the morning of November 14. 2018, in collaboration with pharmaceutical company DHG Pharma, moreover, the collaboration between the two institutions will be done for up to 1,000 patients.
He added that spinal diseases are divided into two types: the first type of spinal disease and the second type of gonorrhea. For type 1 disease, there are more patients than type 2.
Please be informed that this free screening and treatment program for chronically ill patients is a meaningful humanitarian program of Choray Hospital Phnom Penh and DHG Pharma to contribute to the well-being of Cambodians. Opportunity to receive quality health care from highly experienced Vietnamese specialists along with modern medical equipment at Choray Hospital Phnom Penh.
The chiropractor added that the cause of the patient's risk or risk of back pain is due to the patient's daily activities or behaviors, such as daily sitting, especially on heavy objects. In addition to resting in a position that makes the back bend, such as resting in the hammock, etc., which leads to patients at risk and this type of disease.
At the same time, the doctor from Vietnam also advised all staff working in the office who spend a lot of time every day should behave properly, especially sitting upright if you have to sit a lot. Hours should be adjusted several times in the daily work.
