17 years after US invasion: Afghanistan remains a chaotic, corrupt and genocidal country ...
(Afghanistan): 17 years after the US invasion, Afghanistan continues to be in chaos, corruption and violence almost across the country, which has led some Afghans to change their mindset that the United States is an aggressor. And bring Afghanistan back to where it is today. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Wednesday morning, November 14, 2018.
The United States invaded Afghanistan in 2001 to overthrow the Taliban government, and NATO has so far reduced its troop numbers from 150,000 to 15,000. But as military presence was reduced, the United States stepped up airstrikes.
As of the end of September 2018, the US Air Force under Donald Trump dropped 4,943 bombs on Afghanistan, while in 2011 the US dropped 4,266 bombs during the same period under the campaign. Fight the Taliban and ISIS.
