The Supreme Advisory Council will debate three draft laws and national policies before the Royal Government approves them (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Supreme Advisory Council this morning, November 13, 2018. It took almost six hours to review and debate the three draft laws and national policies before the draft laws and policies were submitted to the Royal Government for review and approval.
According to the alphabet, which is the law of the Supreme Advisory Council, in today's meeting, Mr. Seng Sok Kheng, President of the Cambodian Nationality Party, is in charge of chairing the meeting. These three draft laws and policies include: Draft Law on Public Administration, 2. Draft Framework for Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia 2016-2030 and 3rd. Draft National Ecotourism Policy 2019-2030.
The review and debate on the three draft laws and national policies was also attended by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, Senior Minister Chhay Thorn, Minister of Planning and senior officials from the Ministry of Tourism.
Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Secretariat of the Supreme Advisory Council, informed Fresh News that the review and discussion meeting on the draft law and policy was held from 08:30. Morning to 1:10 pm, lasting up to 6 hours. According to Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, the discussion was interpreted by the Ministry and there was also a lot of debate from the Supreme Council.
Kong Monika, President of the Khmer Will Party, highlighted on his Facebook page that in these three draft laws and national policies, he expressed concern about money laundering, migrant workers, poverty rates and the vulnerable. Come below the poor line. He also called for greater attention to tourism to avoid concerns about the removal of tariff preferences from rich countries.
According to Mr. Chhim Phalvarun, the meeting to review and consult on these three draft laws and policies is the second work of the Supreme Advisory Council, while the first work is to review and advise on The draft law on the 2019 national budget, which was recently approved by the Royal Government. Ministry of Commerce opens polling station to elect members of Pursat Chamber of Commerce
