This morning, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen visited and distributed gifts to nearly 2,000 vulnerable families in Keo Seima District, Mondulkiri Province.
(Mondulkiri): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, and his accompanying delegation this morning, November 14, 2018, visited and distributed humanitarian gifts to the elderly, homeless, widows and children. Most of the 1,358 orphans, the disabled and those born or infected with HIV came from 15 villages in 3 communes of Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
The invitation to visit and distribute gifts of Samdech Kittipritthbandit took place in Chhneng village, Sre Khtom commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
At the same time, the people also received a piece of white cloth and an additional 10,000 Riels as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Samdech always takes care of and solves all the challenges of people from all walks of life with compassion, consideration and gives hope and confidence to the general people who are facing difficulties. Without discrimination, regardless of caste, race, color, religion or political affiliation, wherever there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross.
Cambodia Injures Four In Suicide Bombing At UN Location In Mali (Video inside) (Mali): At least four Cambodians were seriously injured in a suicide bombing. At a UN location in Gao, Mali. This is according to the announcement of the spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense on the morning of November 14, 2018.
A statement from General Chhum Socheat, spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, stated that the case occurred on the night of November 12, 2018 (Mali time) and on the morning of November 13, 2018 (at Cambodia) Terrorists drive a car into a UN operational base in Gao, Mali.
The bomber struck shortly after noon in front of a crowd of mourners, killing two Malians and wounding 14 others, including a Cambodian national working for the United Nations, the statement said. Four nations, with one seriously injured and three lightly injured.
The General confirmed that the Cambodian peacekeepers (Blue Hat soldiers) who were on a mission in this area were not harmed by the above incident and that the four Cambodians were mercenaries working for the United Nations. There are also translators.
