Sandan district authorities call on people to dispose of garbage properly and to clean up the environment together
(Kampong Thom): Sandan District Authority, in cooperation with ADA in Kampong Thom Province, on November 13, 2018, organized an awareness program on hygiene and the environment in the presence of Mr. HER Sara, Deputy District Governor, with the support of ADA. Cambodia Hugging Project (Promoting Maternal and Baby Health) at Omean Resort, Meanchey Commune, Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province, with the participation of the Armed Forces, Village, Commune, People and more than 300 students.
Mr. Ken Chamroeun, Vice President of Adra Hug Project in Sandan District, said that the program to understand hygiene and the environment has three objectives, including:
1: Provide knowledge by showing the problems caused by poor hygiene and environment in the target community of Sandan district, Kampong Thom province.
2: Encourage the community to change attitudes, be healthy and prosper in the future.
3. Identify and manage waste to prevent various infections.
4: Participants clearly understand how to wash their hands properly before cooking, before and after feeding the baby, and after washing the anus or after going to the toilet.
Mr. Hee Sara said that participating in improving sanitation and the environment in the community is very important, especially the collection of garbage in schools, at home, on public roads, as well as resorts and other places. He said that a lot of garbage and waste can be a source of disease and affect human health, animals and plant growth.
He added that if the house is clean, the village is clean and healthy, to avoid various diseases. On the other hand, in the resort areas can also help attract tourists to visit and can improve people's lives to some extent.
He urged people to wash their hands thoroughly before eating and after using the toilet. Must drink safe water at all times and everywhere, clean the environment around the village house and participate in cleaning the environment in public houses, such as helping to reduce littering in the open.
Nationwide anti-drug campaign for November 13 Result: 16 cases cracked, 39 people arrested
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for November 13, 2018 shows that law enforcement forces have cracked down on:
1: 8 drug trafficking cases, 23 people were arrested (2 females). 2: 8 drug use cases, 16 people were arrested (3 females). Minister of Agriculture Receives ADB and World Bank Officials
As a result of the discussions, the two sides agreed on the following principles:
First, the development of agriculture and food security in Cambodia in accordance with the fourth rectangular strategy of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
Second, the development of the agricultural sector must be done according to the feasibility and potential of the quality of soil and water and the type of crops, along with the construction of adequate support infrastructure to support production.
Third, building partnerships between the private sector and farmers through contract farming.
Fourth, modernization of agriculture through the introduction of new technologies of cultivation, crop management and agricultural mechanization.
Sixth, support for rice and crop research, refining and management in response to market demand.
7th. Helping to build market information systems for farmers and traders and building warehouses before releasing them to markets in the vegetable and fruit growing communities.
8th. Study the possibility of increasing the attractiveness of the private sector to increase investment in the processing of agricultural products in Cambodia with the experience of two countries in the region, especially neighboring countries.
After the meeting between the Minister and the ADB delegation, the Minister allowed Ms. Chamroeun Mutita, Chairperson of the Third World Bank Mission to Cambodia, and her colleagues to pay a courtesy call and discuss the project implementation activities. Land Allocation for Social and Economic Development Phase 2 (LASED II).
According to Ms. Chamroeun Mutita, the third World Bank Mission to Cambodia visited from October 30 to November 14, 2018 to examine the feasibility of conducting basic data surveys and conducting assessments. Mid-term of the project: Selection of subjects to receive social land concessions and review the living conditions of farmers who have received social land concessions in the past.
According to the facts, she confirmed that the project has been doing well, with the income and family life of the concessionaire has improved significantly. At the same time, she would like to thank the Minister and the Ministry's professional officers for their continued cooperation in implementing this project.
Welcoming the Minister, he expressed his deep gratitude to the World Bank for its continued support to the Royal Government of Cambodia in developing the country. At the same time, the Minister also praised the progress and achievements that the project has achieved with this achievement, which has helped improve the livelihood of families in rural areas and reduce poverty effectively.
In response, she promised to take the minister's recommendations and check as much as possible to ensure the development of the concessionaire's family life. And fined 1,294 units
