Ministry of Health distributes donations to 360 families affected by floods during last rainy season
(Stung Treng): The working group of the Ministry of Health led by Mrs. O Vandin, Director General of Health Technology of the Ministry of Health, on behalf of Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on November 13, 2018, distributed gifts to 360 families. Affected by floods during the previous rainy season in Teak Taem village, Santepheap commune, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province.
Mrs. O Vandin brought a message from the Minister, who always pays high attention to the health of the people who have been living in the water for a long time. She said that while the water was flooding, the minister visited homes to find out the health of the people, who also vaccinated hundreds of children and distributed various medicines. More.
She continued to remind all people to consider the health of daily life according to the three medical rules: live clean, eat clean and drink clean.
