SINGAPORE: Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the 33rd ASEAN Summit in Singapore this afternoon. On November 13, 2018, the strategic trends of the superpowers and the opposition to multilateralism pushed the ASEAN member countries to have different goals.
Li Xianlong said the presence of freedom, openness and the legal basis of the multilateral system, which has supported ASEAN's growth and stability, is in a worrying state. Many countries, including the two great powers, have been developing unilateral actions and bilateral agreements and have indirectly rejected the idea of multilateralism.
Li Xianlong, chair of ASEAN, said that ASEAN member states have their own political strategies and national interests, but he still hopes that ASEAN will continue to work together and find common ground.
"Through our economic integration, we have helped our people benefit from the regional employment sector and strengthened the value of ASEAN proposals to investors. Today, ASEAN is a major economic player in the world. "With the growth of middle-aged and working-age youth, ASEAN will become the world's fourth largest economy by 2030." The Prime Minister of Singapore further confirmed.
