Pailin CamControl officers also continued to inspect various goods and confiscated a total of 17P'ksg (2.36 kg) of defective goods that were harmful to consumers' health and stored them at the office for disposal. Procedures.
Taking the opportunity, the team also distributed posters and advertisements to vendors, vendors and consumers in the market and at home to make them aware of the consequences of eating out of date, use and placement. Add chemicals in food.
The team also instructed all vendors on hygiene and how to properly display the goods in accordance with each type of goods to avoid bacterial contamination, and also advised the vendors in the market. To help inspect the goods themselves for the date of the goods and also prohibit the display of goods that have expired.
