The following is the full text of the Royal Decree: The Ministry of Social Affairs signs MoUs with three major organizations for more than $ 2 million for a three-year project to help vulnerable children, women and vulnerable people in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on November 13, 2018 signed an agreement (MoU) with three major organizations in the amount of more than 2 million dollars for a three-year project to help children and women. Dangerous and vulnerable in Cambodia, both in Phnom Penh and in the provinces.
The three organizations that signed an agreement with the Ministry of Social Affairs this morning are: Holt for Welfare with a budget of $ 360,000 for three years, Ponleu Kampuchea with a budget of $ 791,168 for Three years and First Step Cambodia has a budget of $ 854,831 for three years.
The signing ceremony was attended by Mr. Hach Hean, Undersecretary of State, Representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, relevant officials of the Ministry, as well as representatives of the three organizations and officials-working groups in many provinces.
Mr. Hach Hean requested the current working group of ministries and organizations to work together to support the education, education and development of vulnerable children in remote Cambodia and to help orphans, poor children and children affected by crime. Violence. For the Ministry of Social Affairs is always welcome with relevant partners and organizations to help victims in Cambodia to have a better life and life to another level.
The Undersecretary of State stated that the main purpose of the signing of the agreement with the three organizations is to support the education, welfare and livelihood of children, victims and vulnerable people. He asked all working groups to do this work honestly to help the Cambodian society to be better.
At the same time, he suggested that the three organizations should use these funds to target the victims and the vulnerable more than the administrative costs. He asked the three organizations to abide by the agreement and be honest in helping Cambodian society.
In response, the representatives of the three organizations that signed the MoU with the Ministry of Social Affairs now expressed their pleasure and pleasure in cooperating to help children and vulnerable women in Cambodia through the signing of this agreement.
The three organizations expect to continue to work with the ministry as best they can and use the funds most effectively.
