Bulgaria is located in Eastern Europe, a country in the European Union (since 2007) that has had good relations with Cambodia. In 2017, Bulgaria received more than 9 million international tourists, an increase of 7.6% (mostly Greek, Romanian, Turkish, German, Russian) and more than 6 million Bulgarian tourists (mostly to Greece, Turkey, Romania).
Following the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation, relations between the two countries will be further strengthened and expanded, and Cambodia hopes to receive more tourists from Bulgaria and Europe.
