People's Bank of China (PBOC) Governor Yi Kang has vowed to launch a series of policies to expand private sector financing, including the issuance of bank loans and capital financing. Original.
The central bank has increased lending quotas and additional discounts to $ 43 billion this year, the highest ever and cut interest rates by 0.5 percent. % For small borrowers.
The governor said the central bank has also taken steps to support the provision of capital financing for private companies. "We should implement this measure and dare to accept this burden," he said. As President Xi Jinping has already said, preparation requires 10% and implementation is 90%. "I think we can work hard to follow this formula."
"We should implement at all levels, from financial and management oversight to small and medium-sized financial institutions," Yi Kang added. He said financing difficulties for private companies, especially small and medium-sized enterprises, had become a global problem and that the Chinese government would do more to combat "market failures".
The central bank has reduced its reserve requirement ratio, which is the amount of money banks should have in reserve, and this has helped bring about $ 331 billion in cash flows into the currency market this year.
