Roy, a farmer living in Pochar village, Busra commune, Pichreada district, said that his family has 8 hectares of coffee plantations and is currently harvesting. He said that coffee is a crop that is easy to grow and maintain is not as difficult as pepper, while the harvest period is two and a half years from the date of planting.
The same farmer stated that the price of coffee in 2017 was only 6,000 to 7,000 riel, but this year he can sell up to 10,000 riel per kilogram for dry coffee beans and fresh coffee beans per kilogram. The price of 4,000 riel, which made him and other farmers get a lot of profit from this crop.
