(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, confirmed that currently, the provincial authorities have rescued 6,000 hectares of rice farmers affected by the drought to date and the remaining 12,000 hectares The province is eager to continue the rescue.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun's confirmation was made on November 13, 2018, during a meeting with 40 representatives of the "E" boat committee from 6 districts in Kampong Cham province.
The provincial governor said: "The rice crop of farmers in Kampong Cham province, which is facing the threat of drought, 18,000 hectares as of the evening of November 12, 2018, but the provincial authorities. "We have helped pump 6,000 hectares of water, and the remaining 12,000 hectares, which the provincial authorities, together with professional officials, are still working to help."
At the same time, the provincial governor said that it is true that the people who live next to the river are less likely to have problems with drought. But farmers living far from the river are facing a shortage of water to pump water into their fields, almost turning into a water war because the water supply is not enough to meet their needs.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun also urged the provincial authorities to make efforts to provide sufficient water to farmers, as in some areas there are insufficient water sources and some areas are far away and some canals are old canals. It is difficult to provide enough water to meet the needs of our farmers.
However, the provincial authorities are still doing their best to help find water to pump water to our farmers, no matter how difficult it is, because at least our farmers can get Some of the results, in particular, can not allow their rice to be completely damaged.
