A thief who hit a motorcycle, causing the death of a victim, leaving his wife and children, faces up to 15-30 years in prison
(Phnom Penh): Two thieves who shocked and kicked the victim's motorbike, causing his death at the scene, leaving his wife and two children facing 15 to 30 years in prison according to the provisions of Article 360 of the Penal Code.
This morning, November 13, 2018, the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Ky Manera, issued an order to detain two thieves in prison pending trial.
The judge's decision comes after prosecutors Sin Virak decided to charge the two defendants with aggravated theft due to the death of the victim under Article 360 of the Penal Code.
Article 360 aggravated by the death of the victim states that "Theft is punishable by 15 (fifteen) to 30 (thirty) years imprisonment if committed before, during or after the violence. "Let the victim die because there was no intention to kill."
According to Colonel Kheng Meng Chheang, director of the Bureau of Minor Offenses of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior, Fresh News reported that the assailant, who was the one who shocked and kicked the victim, was named Moeung Bun Veasna. Abo, 21, a resident of Mittapheap Village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, was arrested on Koh Pich, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Morn.
Another faction member, Khieu Phalla, alias Khla, male, 21 years old, occupation: bag snatching, current address, house for rent, no road, Phum Doeum Chan, Sangkat Chbar Ampov 2, Khan Chbar Ampov, was also caught by the police at 4:30 p.m. November 6, 2018 at a point in Wat Thmey, Preah Theat village, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province.
As for the other two fugitives, the competent authorities are looking to arrest them to take legal action.
