(Prey Veng): The European Union (EU) is an important partner of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for a project to promote sustainable and inclusive economic growth in agriculture, fisheries and animal husbandry with the support and support of the European Union. Preventing illegal fishing has made the people in the fishing community in Babong village, Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province, have a better life due to the increase in income from the sale of fish products.
Pan Sodivi, President of the Social Action Organization, said the EU Foundation has benefited many communities by setting up community patrols to stop illegal fishing and teaching them how to grow mushrooms for extra income. Their income from selling fish after receiving assistance from the European Union also increased due to increased fish production.
"Their income from fishing is still limited, so we encourage them to grow more vegetables," she said. The EU provides 80% of the funding for these activities and we provide the rest. She noted that about $ 500,000 has been spent on the project since 2016, of which $ 100,000 came from the organization.
Sreng Limsong, Deputy Director of the Fisheries Administration, said: "This EU assistance is very important to help prevent illegal fishing, and without the cooperation of the community, the commune will be addicted to illegal fishing. The project also benefits the fishing community. ”
The main activities of the project implemented in Babong commune are to increase the leadership and management skills of the leaders and members of the Fisheries Community Committees, as well as to raise awareness of their roles and responsibilities in order to promote fisheries conservation and combat. And illegal fishing, as well as increasing the income from the sale of fish left over from eating.
