(Tbong Khmum): On the occasion of the upcoming Water Festival to ensure the health of the people who eat, Mr. Meas Mora, President of CamControl Branch in Tbong Khmum Province, on November 12, 2018, led the CamControl officials in cooperation. With the Provincial Department of Commerce, continue to inspect and improve the quality and safety of goods by testing some food kits at Memot Market in Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Meas Mora said that under the guidance of the General Department of CamControl, all CamControl branches across the country follow its action plan to ensure the quality of food safety and health of the people, especially during the festival. Water, floating lanterns, chanting and worshiping the moon, he, along with the provincial CamControl officials and relevant authorities always inspect regularly.
In fact, today we continued to inspect and test immediately on some foods, such as prahok and pickles are not found to contain chemicals that cause harm to the health of consumers.
At the same time, they also tested two types of iodized salt, the type of stone and mat, which was packaged in Phnom Penh and Kampong Speu province to contain real iodine. After testing, it was found that a total of 10 packages of iodized salt packaged in Phnom Penh did not contain iodine as specified on its packaging.
At the same time, CamControl officials advised traders before buying iodized salt from distributors to test whether the salt actually contains iodine or not, and take further steps to find a source to confirm the problem.
Please note that iodine on salt is important to prevent various diseases, especially gout, which the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Health always calls for all people to consume salt containing iodine.
