(Phnom Penh): Dr. Bumi Pediatrics J. Ganathan, Caritas Consultant Pediatric Psychiatrist in Cambodia, said that most mental illnesses occur in adolescents when they know and understand the root causes. With mental health problems, they can know and find ways to prevent, treat or help themselves when mental health problems occur.
This is what the psychiatrist said on the occasion of his participation as a speaker in a seminar organized by the team of Phka Chhouk radio station on mental illness under the theme "Current state of adolescent mental illness". Ascended last weekend with more than 500 participants in the hall of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center (CJCC).
He said that according to the documents of the American Psychological Association, there are three main factors that lead people to mental problems, social factors, biological factors and psychological factors. First, social factors such as love, economy and so on. Second, biological factors, including drug use, alcohol, and third, psychological factors are factors that determine the growth of an individual, the mode of upbringing of the family to each child.
