(Tbong Khmum): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, called on the people affected by the floods to be very careful about health problems when the floods recede and during the winter (winter) will be Some epidemics occur such as diarrhea, dengue fever, scabies, pneumonia, colds and respiratory infections.
This statement was made on the occasion of the Minister accompanied by officials of the Provincial Health Department and the Deputy Governors of the provinces and districts to distribute medicines, sanitary ware with the support of Direct Relief and treat people after the impact. Affected 647 families in Koh Treng village, Koh Pei commune, Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province on December 12, 2018.
The Minister stated that in order to prevent all these health problems, the people must take part in implementing health protection measures consistently. Health protection measures include:
* Continue to eat clean food - well cooked, drink and use clean water as well as personal hygiene and diligently wash your hands with soap every time you cook before eating and after defecation.
Sleep under mosquito nets to prevent dengue fever, malaria and other mosquito-borne diseases, even if the disease does not occur this season.
* Check the house carefully to see if there are any snakes or other venomous animals that can bite or bite.
* Clean the environment around the house and indoors, because after the water recedes, leaving a lot of dirt, waste and germs.
* Need to restore and clean the well before use.
* Repair and rebuild toilets by always defecating in the toilet at all times
* Dry wet floors or appliances and open all windows and doors to allow adequate ventilation in the house to prevent mold from growing, which can cause diarrhea and respiratory illnesses.
The minister also said that if there is a health problem, people must go to the health center or hospital near their home. In addition, the Ministry of Health encourages the general public to follow the above simple advice to protect you and your family from various diseases.
