The Ministry of Justice's dismissal came after prisoner Sam Rainsy escaped from Cambodia's legal trap in an interview with Cambodian National Radio on the night of November 9. That Mr. Kem Sokha will be released no later than March 3, 2019, the court proceedings because Mr. Kem Sokha has not been convicted.
In a statement issued by the Ministry of Justice on Sunday, November 11, 2018, it stated that the provision of legal arguments is distorted and misleading, which could confuse the public about the procedures and practices. Law by the courts as an independent institution.
Through this statement, the Ministry of Justice claimed that the accused Kem Sokha was charged with conspiracy with a foreigner as a type of treason under Article 443 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, where he was convicted. Imprisonment from 15 to 30 years.
On the other hand, Mr. Kem Sokha was detained by the Investigating Judge on September 5, 2017 and released on bail and placed under judicial supervision on September 9, 2018. .
The ministry further stated that the criminal case involving the accused Kem Sokha is currently under the jurisdiction of the investigating judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. The investigating judge shall decide on the actions in this case at its sole discretion and based on the facts, evidence and laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia without any pressure from foreigners or individuals.
The statement also reacted to Sam Rainsy's claim that French law provides for detention for only two days. The ministry confirmed that this claim was a hoax and a misrepresentation of Sam Rainsy, a French prisoner who did not know French law at all.
The ministry expects the public to be aware of this and not believe in the manipulation and incitement of Sam Rainsy.
