(Japan): The Ambassador of Cambodia to Japan held a celebration of the 65th Anniversary of National Independence Day on November 9 and the 65th Anniversary of Cambodia-Japan Diplomatic Relations in Tokyo, Japan on the evening of November 08, 2018 .
Mr. Ung Rachana, Cambodian Ambassador to Japan, confirmed that the historic day was held with the support of many students and Cambodians living in Japan, representatives of the Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, representatives of Japanese private organizations and organizations. Ambassadors of some countries also attended.
The Ambassador expressed his happiness to the larger-than-expected participants, which showed the support of the Cambodian people, the people of Japan, and Norikazu SUZUKI, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, as well as friends and relatives. Other countries' ambassadors to Cambodia.
Mr. Ung Rachana reminded that the celebration of the Independence Day on November 9 is a reminder of the great crusade, the great achievements of the country until the full independence in 1953 to the motherland of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. Preah Borom Ratanakoth.
He hopes that from now on, after Cambodia has achieved full peace from 1998 until today, Cambodia has progressed in all areas, and in the future, Cambodia will strengthen its development and progress than now. In Tokyo, Japan, with the celebration of the National Independence Day, the Cambodian Embassy also celebrated the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan diplomatic relations.
According to the Japanese Deputy Foreign Minister, about 200,000 Japanese people visit Cambodia each year, so the Cambodian economy is growing and the relationship between the two countries is getting stronger.
Mr. Kan Phannarith, President of the Cambodian Students Association in Japan, said that today's program provides an opportunity for the Cambodian people to meet, as well as the people of Cambodia and Japan to discuss the strengthening of cooperation.
In particular, Mr. Meng Phalkun, a master's degree student in Engineering and Civil Engineering at the University of Tokyo, Japan, confirmed that this is the first time to attend the Independence Day event in Japan, especially the participants have met and established good relations. Learn about Japanese companies and organizations that wish to contribute to the strengthening and expansion of Cambodia-Japan relations.
In Cambodia, the National Independence Day is also held on November 9, 2018 under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and led by government officials, students and troops. The armed forces, tens of thousands of people participated.
According to history, November 9, 2018 marks the 65th anniversary of the complete liberation of the entire Cambodian nation from French colonial rule under the ferocious crusade of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty the King. King Samdech Norodom Sihanouk on November 9, 1953.
France colonized Sovannaphumi for almost a century from August 11, 1863 to November 9, 1953, before Cambodia gained independence under the crusade of the former King, King Norodom. Sihanouk.
The following is a speech by the Cambodian Ambassador to Japan
Today, I am very honored to have Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs and all the distinguished guests in this evening to celebrate the 65th Anniversary of the National Independence Day of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the 65th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between Cambodia and Japan. . I am very excited about the noble presence of Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, all distinguished guests.
Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, all distinguished guests
In these 65 years, Cambodia and Japan have not only endured time and regional and international political changes, but we have also seen the growth and deepening of bilateral relations. The two countries enjoy warm relations as well as multi-sectoral cooperation, which enhances our friendship to become a strategic partnership in December 2013.
Cambodia and Japan have common interests in regional and global affairs through close cooperation and coordination. The two countries have worked closely for the sake of regional and global peace and stability.
