Watch the video: Royal Speech of the King of Cambodia and Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the Occasion of National Independence Day, November 9:
In the meaningful speech, the King of Cambodia commemorated the deeds and crusades of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty the King Father of the Khmer Nation, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk in the struggle for national independence and the rights of the people. Khmer from the yoke of French colonization.
Satisfied with the progress of Cambodia, the King of Cambodia also called on the Cambodian people to unite to protect peace and build the motherland of Cambodia going forward. "I would like to call on all Cambodians from all walks of life to unite as one under the umbrella of the Constitution and state law to contribute to the protection and construction of the motherland in all areas."
In the presence of the King of Cambodia, civil servants, the armed forces and the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, also announced his commitment to continue to work hard to promote national development and bring prosperity. For the Cambodian nation, based on the four main principles and principles, including:
1. Continue to build the nation to progress in all fields, have strong national unity, social morality, equality, freedom and justice, democracy and human rights for the prosperous life, prosperity of the people and harmony in the family, community and society as a whole.
2. Defend national independence, peace, sovereignty and territorial integrity, protect national social achievements, enhance national prestige, prevent interference in Cambodia's internal affairs and absolutely oppose any activities related to the color revolution or any incitement that causes political instability or unrest in Cambodian society.
3. Continue to resolve land and water borders with neighboring countries on the basis of international law and promote the implementation of border development strategies to become a border of peace, peace and cooperation and not allow foreigners to use Cambodian territory to oppose neighboring countries.
4. Prevent and suppress all kinds of crimes, including: financing, terrorism, money laundering, human trafficking, sex trafficking, all kinds of transnational crime, and continue to promote the effective implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes.
