(Ratanakkiri): 203 people living in 2 villages in O'Chum district, Ratanakkiri province, suffered from diarrhea and vomiting, were sent to the hospital for emergency treatment the same day, then returned and recovered. Go home.
This incident happened on the evening of November 8, 2018 at Loeun Kreun village, Loeun Chong village, Samaki commune, O'Chum district, Ratanakkiri province.
According to Dr. Ung Ratana, director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department, the reason people vomit is because they eat unhygienic food.
Dr. Ung Ratana said that out of 203 people, only 40 had to be suspended from the serum, however, in this case, no one was in danger.
