(Phnom Penh): A 23-member high-level delegation from Colombia's mine sector has successfully completed demining skills training in Cambodia and gained a lot of experience from CMAC over the past two weeks.
The Closing Ceremony of the Training Course was presided over by Mr. Heng Ratana, General Director of CMAC on the morning of November 9, 2018 at CMAC Headquarters in Phnom Penh.
The two-week course focuses on "General Management, Planning and Prioritization of Demining" at the Peace Museum, Demining Activities at the 2nd Mine Action Unit and the Mine Action Training Institute (TIMA). In addition to learning about demining skills from Cambodia, the Cambodian and Colombian sides shared good experiences and cultures with each other.
