In addition, to find out the end of the war and peace building through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Colombia has gone through 50 years of war and has only had a two-year peace agreement. Colombia has a population of about 50 million in South America.
During the meeting, Colombian mine officials were interested in and appreciated CMAC's work, especially exploring the Royal Government's win-win policy, claiming to apply Cambodia's good experience in their own country.
It should be recalled that on March 1, 2017, CMAC, Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and Colombia signed a cooperation agreement on demining and unexploded ordnance (UXO) training. The eruption for the second phase lasted for five years under the support and sponsorship of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) under the South-South Cooperation Project.
