In the meeting with Prince Sar Kheng, Ms. Rona Smith discussed three main issues, but did not mention Kem Sokha.
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of November 7, 2018, for more than two hours, Ms. Rona Smith, UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, discussed Three important tasks, but did not mention the story of Kem Sokha, former president of the CNRP.
Deputy Spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Phat Sophanit, told reporters after the meeting that the three main tasks that Ms. Rona Smith discussed with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng are: Sustainability 2016 and civil society organizations, second: related to accountability issues and third: related to overcrowding in prisons.
Speaking at the meeting, Prince Sar Kheng told Ms. Rona Smith that in order to solve various challenges as well as link partnerships and work together for society, the Royal Government has set up a working group to address various issues. Concerns or opinions raised by civil society related to the implementation of their activities and when there is a problem can be asked questions and opinions.
Ms. Rona Smith expressed appreciation for the Royal Government of Cambodia's initiative to increase partnerships with civil society organizations and NGOs through the establishment of a forum as well as the issuance of a new notice in October to clarify And give civil society and NGOs the confidence to take action to participate in the development of Cambodian society.
Regarding the issue of accountability, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Interior as its staff, has made efforts to eliminate various inactive points that Cambodia strives to establish a one-stop-shop mechanism in all capitals. Provinces, while aiming to reach all districts to provide services closer to the people faster and more transparently.
Samdech Sar Kheng stressed that the OWSO also has a place to receive complaints from people to address what is inactive in providing services to people at the local level.
At this point, Ms. Rona Smith also expressed her congratulations and encouraged the government as well as the Ministry of Interior to continue to work hard to strengthen the establishment of this OWSO to serve the people more easily and Closer to the people.
In addition, regarding the drug crackdown campaign and overcrowding in prisons, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng informed that the drug problem is a problem that is a challenge of Cambodian society because if the authorities do not crack down on drugs, this problem will expand. Spread in society and also a big responsibility of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
For the operation to crack down on drugs, Sar Kheng added that the authorities could not avoid the arrest and detention of suspects, which led to overcrowding in prisons. But to solve this problem, the Royal Government and the Ministry of Interior are working hard and are building additional prison infrastructure in the provinces to help share the prisons in Phnom Penh as well as in the overcrowded prisons.
In this regard, Prince Sar Kheng also wants to have a meeting to work together to resolve the pre-trial detention of some detainees, which is also part of the overcrowding. In prison as well.
At the same time, Ms. Rona Smith also supported what the Royal Government has done in the past regarding the construction of infrastructure in the prison, and she said that if there is a meeting between the Ministry of Interior or relevant institutions to try to speed up the trial. As a solution for detainees awaiting trial, this is a good thing.
It should be noted that during Ms. Rona Smith's visit to Cambodia this time, it seems that Soth did not mention and raise the issue of political parties, especially in relation to the case of Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party, which is under the jurisdiction of the judiciary. Groundbreaking Ceremony for Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Headquarters
On that occasion, Mr. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General, Representative of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, praised the past leadership and successful work of Tbong Khmum Provincial Commissioner and all forces working hard. Do not be afraid to get tired, especially a big thank you to all the donors who donated money and equipment for the construction of this staff building.
Labor Minister Asks Association to Send-Receive Workers to Help Prepare Temporary Accommodation for Cambodian Workers in Thailand
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, requested the relevant associations working on sending and receiving Cambodian workers to work in Thailand to help arrange temporary accommodation for Cambodian workers in key areas where possible. They can stay temporarily during a change of job or wait for a dispute to be resolved with the employer.
The Minister's request was made during the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation for the Protection and Management of Cambodian Workers in Thailand between the Cambodian Labor Agency Association and the Cambodian Recruitment Association. Cambodia-Thailand Relations at The Credit Duk Hotel, Phnom Penh on November 7, 2018.
"Through the experience of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in the management of Cambodian workers in the Republic of Korea, I would like to ask the association to consider arranging temporary housing for Cambodian workers in areas in Thailand that can "Cambodian workers stay temporarily during job changes or wait for disputes with employers."
Regarding the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that before the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation for the Protection and Management of Cambodian Workers in the Kingdom of Thailand, the Association The Cambodian Labor Agency (MAC), the Cambodian Recruitment Association (ACRA) and the Cambodian-Thai Relations Association (TCRA) have worked together responsibly.
He added that the MoU is a step forward and a new mechanism for the protection of Cambodian workers going to work in Thailand, in addition to the existing protections and contributing to a better Thailand. Improved efficiency and effectiveness.
(Phnom Penh): The Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on November 7, 2018, issued a statement confirming and explaining the legal action and charges of Deputy Prosecutor Heng Bunthon in the case of the burglars. Phone on the street recently. This is according to the statement of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, which was received by Fresh News this evening.
The statement came after a series of criticisms of Deputy Prosecutor Heng Bunthon's allegations of altering the burglary charges from heavy to light. Justice that seeks to catch thieves and build a case to send to court.
The statement explained that Deputy Prosecutor Heng Bunthon charged the two thieves under Articles 353 and 356 of the Penal Code, in strict accordance with the provisions of the law in order to achieve Law enforcement and the elimination of impunity.
However, according to some reports obtained by Fresh News in late October 2018, Deputy Prosecutor Hung Bunthon also decided to release a number of suspects, including: Israelis involved in defamation and posting photos. Pornography, suspects as car warehouse owners involved in cases of theft and buying cars from thieves, suspects in traffic accidents and so on.
Samdech Heng Samrin Requests the Chinese Parliament to Meet with the National Assembly of Cambodia to Strengthen the Deep Cooperation between the Two Parliamentary Expert Committees
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Committee and the Law of the National People's Congress (NPC) met this morning, November 8, 2018, with Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, to strengthen the cooperation between the two parliaments. The Chinese National People's Congress (NPC) visited Cambodia to strengthen cooperation between the two parliaments, especially in the field of law.
During the visit, a delegation from the Constitution and Law Committee of the National People's Congress, led by Li Fei, a member of the committee and chairman of the delegation, paid a courtesy call and held a hearing with the National Assembly President on the morning of November 8. 2018, held at the National Assembly.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin considers that Mr. Li Fei's visit has contributed to the strengthening of Cambodia-China friendly relations and cooperation, especially between the two parliaments to understand and share experiences on construction legislation. Law.
Samdech Heng Samrin emphasized that "cooperation in all-round strategic partnership" is bearing fruit in all fields.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and the delegation said that Cambodia-China diplomatic relations have reached its 60th anniversary this year, and the leaders of the two countries' legislatures and executive branches have exchanged visits with each other.
On behalf of the National Assembly, Samdech Heng Samrin praised and fully supported China's initiative on the One Belt One Road policy. Samdech stated that this global economic project has played an important role in socio-economic development, helping to attract more investors and the development of trade, industry and tourism in Cambodia.
In recent years, bilateral trade from China to Cambodia has grown significantly. China has become an important trading partner and the first major investor in Cambodia.
As for Cambodia, the National Bank of Cambodia recently announced the introduction of the Chinese yuan in the Cambodian banking system. This is a mechanism to facilitate bilateral trade, investment and tourism more effectively. Li Fei informed that the Constitution and Law Committee of the Chinese National People's Congress was established in March 2018.
"Cambodia is the first country that the selection committee will visit to study and exchange experiences on legal issues, which is an important part of encouraging Chinese investors to understand Cambodian law," he said. They will come to invest more in Cambodia.
Regarding the cooperation between the two parliaments, the President of the National Assembly requested the delegation to discuss with Dr. Pen Panha, Chairman of the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia on in-depth cooperation between the two parliamentary expert committees for the benefit of both. All together. Do not forget! Cambodia vs. Malaysia to open Suzuki Cup at 6:30 pm
