(Ratanakkiri): Four roads were badly damaged by floods for more than three consecutive months recently in Ratanakkiri province, with two paved national roads in O'Yadao and Lumphat districts. Including two other Red Family Roads in Vern Sai and Ta Veng districts will be rehabilitated by the end of November 2018.
This was confirmed by Mr. Va Savun, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Ratanakkiri Province, who gave a telephone interview to Fresh News Agency in Ratanakkiri Province on November 8.
He said that the four domestic roads that were badly damaged were in three districts, which the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport had almost completely repaired, including O'Yadao, Vern Sai and Lumphat districts. Separately, another road, Provincial Road No. 3RK1, a red gravel road in Ta Veng district, is 7 km long, has just been repaired by more than 50% and is still undergoing further repairs, which will take about 3 months. More is ready.
In addition to repairing the roads damaged by the floods, Mr. Savavun also mentioned the project to build 5 DBST paved roads in Banlung with a total length of 6,000 meters, 6-7 meters wide and 1 red pavement. Both meters will be completed by the end of 2018 as well.
