International analysis: Can Iran continue to live under the weight of new US sanctions?
However, Trump has allowed eight states to continue importing imports from Iran as temporary concessions. At this point, it seems that Trump has acknowledged that blocking Iran's oil exports to zero is easy.
For many states, it is impossible to cut off energy supply ties with Tehran in the short term, which is why Washington has allowed some countries to continue importing oil and gas. From Iran, but they need to cut imports in large quantities or stop importing completely in the future.
Obviously, like Turkey, which receives energy from Iran, it is impossible for Turkey to follow the intentions of the US superpower by cutting off imports from Iran in the near future because the Ankara government is difficult to find. Find new sources of energy supply from other states and make the country's economy weak and fragile.
Not only Turkey, but many other close allies of the United States are facing similar problems. As of October 28, just days before the new US sanctions take effect, Iranian oil companies could sell up to 280,000 barrels of crude oil at $ 74.85 a barrel, signaling demand. Oil from Iran strongly.
If the United States does not grant exemptions to countries that are heavily dependent on Iranian oil, they will inevitably violate the principles of Washington's sanctions on Tehran.
European countries have expressed confidence that Iran will remain committed to the JCOPA principles and have made it clear that they will not follow in the footsteps of the United States by imposing sanctions on Iran. At the same time, the leaders of European countries have decided to implement payment mechanisms as a special way to support European companies to avoid losses due to US sanctions.
(Svay Rieng): A man died in a traffic accident between a truck and a motorcycle, colliding head-on on National Road No. 1 at Samaki Village, Sangkat Svay Toeur, Svay Rieng City on the afternoon of November 7, 2018. This caused the motorcycle to die immediately, while the car hit and dragged more than 30 meters to get stuck.
