In 10 months, the General Department of Taxation collected more than $ 1.87 billion in tax revenue for the national budget, an increase of 18%
(Phnom Penh): In the first 10 months of 2018, the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance collected 7,494.85 billion Riels for the national budget, equivalent to approximately 1,873.71 million US dollars, an increase of 18 .83% compared to the same period in 2017. This is according to the press release of the General Department of Taxation on the results of the October 2018 tax revenue collection meeting on November 7.
The meeting to review the results of tax collection for October 2018 was chaired by Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, with the participation of the Deputy Director General, the Deputy Director of the Provincial-Khan Tax Branch. And all relevant tax officials under the jurisdiction of the General Department of Taxation.
At the same time, the General Department of Taxation expects that all types of tax revenue for 2018 can be collected in accordance with the plan set by law.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Kong Vibol further instructed all units to continue to work hard to enforce the labor law and to be gentle but firm based on the legal aspect in responding to taxpayers to make them happy to accept and volunteer. Everyone is willing to pay taxes, minimize the taxpayers' grievances and provide good cooperation in paying taxes to the people.
For 2018, in order to ensure the effective implementation of tax collection in accordance with the legal plan of 7,693.50 billion riels (approximately 1,923.38 million US dollars), the General Department of Taxation will continue to strictly implement and More effectively implement the Royal Government's in-depth reform policy and set out some measures as follows:
* Prepare to adjust the value of real estate, which is the basis for real estate tax in accordance with the recommendations of the Prime Minister.
* Continue to push for deeper implementation of key reforms to increase the efficiency of providing public services to taxpayers to have a higher quality, faster, easier to make the tax administration a more trusted state institution. From the public from all walks of life.
* Continue to modernize the information technology system by continuing to develop tax management software based on information technology.
* Inform and remind people to fulfill the obligation to declare and pay taxes, means of transportation and all types of vehicles, which will expire at the end of November 2018.
* Continue to survey and update real estate.
