64 Poor Farmers in Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province Receive Cattle for Raising, Minister of Agriculture Urges Department to Provide Animal Health Care Techniques to Farmers
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on November 7, 2018, requested the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Chhnang Province to continue to pay high attention to providing technical services on Animal health care and artificial insemination to farmers to improve farmers' incomes.
The report added that today's cattle distribution program is a new program for 3 years, 2018-2021, which will be implemented in 30 villages in Kampong Tralach Nong district, Rolea Bier district and Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province, which has poor farmers. 605 families will directly and indirectly benefit from the project, about 49,150 families.
The first program was held on September 28, 2018, which distributed 112 cows to 56 poor farmers from 12 villages in 4 communes in Kampong Tralach district under the chairmanship of Ms. Hor Malin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. Hunting and fishing. During December, the organization will distribute 40 more families, for a total of 160 families in all three cases.
According to the organization's conditions, the distribution of cattle to farmers is given priority to:
1: Women heads of households have limited access to wealth 2: Families with disabilities and registered as poor 3: Indigenous families 4: Indigenous families with limited wealth Khmer Islam.
According to the director of the organization, before distributing cows for raising, the organization has provided basic technical training to farmers to ensure that they know how to take good care of animals, including feeding, protection and treatment. Disease.
At the same time, Mr. Veng Sakhon also requested the organization to examine the possibility of expanding the project program more in the areas or provinces where there are many Muslims living to reduce poverty and requested the farmers who receive cows. Today, take care to maintain and get better growth for the benefit of increasing family income.
The Minister requested the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture to continue to pay close attention to providing technical services on animal health care and artificial breeding to farmers who receive cows today to improve. He also asked the organization to examine the possibility of expanding the project program to other areas.
