The Senior Minister confirmed that on December 3, 2018, the construction company will open the bidding package and speed up the procedures to open the construction site in January 2019.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also pointed to the delays in the construction. According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, this delay is due to the fact that the construction cost is more than the budget that the Royal Government of Cambodia borrowed from the South Korean government four years ago up to 13 million US dollars, which is why it can not be auctioned. Yes.
In response, the Cambodian Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has submitted a request to the South Korean side for a loan, and the South Korean side has recently agreed.
Please note that National Road No. 2, which is planned to be rebuilt, is approximately 57 kilometers long from the roundabout in Takhmao City, Kandal Province to the roundabout of O Chambok (approximately 3 kilometers from the roundabout in Takeo Province). The project also includes the construction of a 9-kilometer stretch of National Road 22.
The project will implement AC paving, build a new bridge and widen the road to 13 meters. Separately, at the roundabout of Ku Srov to the south, a length of 8 km will be built in 4 lanes.
It should be noted that all road projects funded by loans from the South Korean government are always slower than in other countries. Roads planned to be built under the loan from South Korea include National Road, National Road 2 and National Road 48 (from Sre Ampil district to Koh Kong provincial town).
