Ballot counting begins in states across the United States after midterm elections
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - More than half of the 50 polling stations in the United States began closing ballot counts on Tuesday (US time) amid speculation that Democrats could control Congress and Republicans will continue to control the Senate. Same. This was released by CNN on Wednesday morning, November 7, 2018.
In the U.S. midterm elections (Senate and House of Representatives), the American people must elect all 435 members of Congress and 30 senators out of 100 candidates, and governors will be elected in 36 of the states. 50 states as well.
Remarkably, however, this election will not only determine whether Democrats or Republicans control the US Congress, but it will also determine whether Donald Trump will have more power or not. Reduce power.
Moreover, if the Democrats win this election, Donald Trump's US presidency could be revised, as some Democrats have promised to take steps to oust Donald Trump. .
According to the results gradually released, the Democrat Party is leading in the National Assembly and the Republican Party is leading in the Senate.
