Siem Reap Mayor Aims to Transform Siem Reap into a Smoke-Free City
(Siem Reap): "It's time for Siem Reap to become a smoke-free city, because Siem Reap is one of the most famous cities in Southeast Asia, especially in the areas of tourism, culture, history and heritage. "Smoke completely."
This is the statement of Mr. So Platon, Governor of Siem Reap City, on the morning of November 6, 2018, the Siem Reap Municipal Administration was announced as a smoke-free workplace with the participation of Dr. Lak Leang, Representative of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia, Dr. Do. Domilin Vilaraz and a total of 100 members of the Armed Forces, Sangkat Councils.
The Governor of Siem Reap stated that Siem Reap has been selected by the Royal Government of Cambodia to develop as a Smart City to continue its efforts to develop Siem Reap as a smart city among ASEAN smart cities.
"Today we begin to declare the Siem Reap Municipality a smoke-free place and we will continue to do so in all public and private institutions, public places, and smoke-free public places," So Platon said.
The organizers added that this is the face of Cambodia, which is obviously increasing the number of tourists, both national and international from year to year. Turning this historic tourist city into a smoke-free city is another important part of boosting tourism.
In addition, it is actively involved in the implementation of the International Convention on the Control of Tobacco Products of the World Health Organization, which is the effort of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay attention to the health of the people. Death due to tobacco use, as well as the health of national and international guests who come to Cambodia, especially Siem Reap to escape the dangers caused by tobacco.
Please be informed that the implementation of a smoke-free environment is a global trend and in line with 99% of the people support the city of Siem Reap to be a smoke-free city October 2017 in Siem Reap).
Cigarette-free cities are: 1-No smoking in the building of the workplace and public places, 2-No smoking inside the public transport, 3-Smoking outside the building 5 meters from the entrance, 4. Smoking is prohibited on the premises of educational institutions, health facilities, nurseries, playgrounds, public parks, religious institutions, museums, cultural and historical sites, gyms, gas stations and flammable places.
In ASEAN countries, some of their cities have already been declared smoke-free.
