WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Scientists around the world have been amazed since a strange space object named Oumuamua orbited the Sun in late 2017. Due to its fast speed and erratic orbit, this mysterious object, the size of an international sports stadium, clearly originates from outside our solar system.
But the elongated, flat shape and speed at which it travels through the solar system makes it very different from ordinary asteroids or comets, as astronomers and scientists have been observing for decades. . This is according to a quote from NBC News on Tuesday morning, November 6, 2018.
Two researchers from Harvard University are raising the possibility that Oumuamua could be an alien spacecraft. The two scientists described in their research papers that the mysterious space object was probably a fully operational spacecraft deliberately sent to the solar system by aliens.
