23 senior Colombian mine officials to study demining skills from Cambodia
(Siem Reap): Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), confirmed that on November 5, 2018, a high-level delegation of the Ministry of Mines of Colombia 23 arrived in the territory. Angkor to receive training with CMAC for 2 weeks.
He added that the delegation included advisers to the President of Colombia and leaders of relevant ministries and institutions. This project supports the Japanese government through JICA. Colombia has been at war for about 50 years and has just achieved peace, so it needs to clear landmines and explosive remnants of war to ensure the full implementation of the peace process.
The course focuses on "General Management, Demining and Prioritization of Demining" at the Peace Museum, Demining Activities at the 2nd Mine Action Unit and the Sima Mine Action Institute (TIMA).
It should be recalled that on March 1, 2017, CMAC, Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and Colombia signed a cooperation agreement on demining and unexploded ordnance (UXO) training. Explosion for the second phase under the support and sponsorship of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) under the South-South Cooperation Project.
Under this agreement, CMAC will provide seven training sessions to Colombian trainees, from the military and from relevant institutions, for a period of five years from 2017 to 2022, with a total of 158 trainees, focusing on seven topics:
1: Explosive Ordnance Disposal Level 32: Training of dog trainers 3: General management, planning and prioritization of demining 4: Reduction of minefields (technical and non-technical research) 5: Training of machine cleaners 6: Quality control and standards 7: Information management
