After traveling to seven cities in two provinces, Guangxi and Jiangsu, which are China's most prosperous provinces and have strong political, economic, tourism and investment ties with Cambodia. All Cambodian journalists were amazed at China's economic, trade, and technological growth in these two provinces.
As 2018 marks the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations, and while the topic of Chinese friendship and investment in Cambodia is a hot topic in Cambodian society, Mr. Van Saray and Mr. Powy raised This issue is discussed and answered sharply.
During the talks, Van Saray said that China, Asia's economic powerhouse and the world's second-largest economy, is becoming the world's rising sun and could become It also ruled the world economy in the new era under the "Belt and Road" policy, Xi Jinping's sharp policy of building allies and boosting its trade economy.
Mr. Van Saray's remarks are also due to his three visits to China, which have seen him expand on China's sharp economic and technological warfare. In particular, China has a lot of natural resources to support its efforts.
Mr. Van Saray saw China's progress as a good opportunity for Cambodia as an ally today. For Mr. Povi also sees the current alliance between Cambodia and China is a good thing for Cambodia, because the progress of China today will push Cambodia to grow.
Mr. Povi affirmed and expressed confidence that Cambodia today will not slip into the abyss of misery as in the past, because the political situation of Cambodia as well as the problems of the world today is not the same as in the past. That. Cambodia, as well as the world, has focused on building its economy, not on war, expanding its influence as it once did.
On the other hand, the number of ASEAN tourists to China as a whole has also increased steadily, with more than 10 million in 2016, an increase of 57.8% compared to 2015.
Based on this investment and tourism data, it shows that Cambodia and other ASEAN member countries are competing to seize opportunities through China's growth.
At the same time, Mr. Van Saray and Mr. Povi both want to see the Cambodian people change their attitude from being greedy to Chinese investment in Cambodia, change from fearing China to be Cambodia's owner through investment, and strive to strengthen their capacity to create An opportunity to take advantage of Chinese investment to improve their lives.
During the 1990s, Cambodians worked hard to learn English in order to seize job opportunities in Western-majority civil society organizations, the two journalists said. So if young Cambodians embrace learning Chinese, it could also create their own job opportunities.
Mr. Povi said that when Westerners come to Cambodia, we know how to learn English to seize job opportunities, so why refuse to learn Chinese when Chinese come to do business in Cambodia? Mr. Vitha, whether they want to or not, young Cambodians, Cambodians must recognize the changes in the world today and must strengthen their capacity to seize the opportunity of this change.
