(China): The Chinese government has raised the minimum level of the national social security system as the government continues to work to raise the living standards of people across the country. According to the Chinese Ministry of Civil Affairs.
As of the end of September, urban and rural areas across China had more than 46 million low-income people. The poorest families in urban areas receive $ 52 a month in social security, while the poorest families in rural areas receive $ 682 a year.
China has nearly 5 million people living in extreme poverty, and the central government has spent $ 3.4 billion to help them from January to September, the ministry said. 2018, an increase of 20 percent compared to the same period last year.
A total of 1.888 million people have registered for assistance and financial assistance. Of those, 928 million have officially crossed the poverty line. According to the Chinese government.
