On the occasion of presiding over the opening of the Regional International Conference on "Combating Counterfeit and Substandard Medicines" held at Sofitel Phuket this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended that the perpetrators be severely punished. Counterfeit medicine traffic.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said, "Currently, the problem of counterfeit and substandard medicines is spreading alarmingly, with some pharmaceutical products being marketed online as counterfeit and similar drugs. "That really makes it difficult for the authorities to control."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted that the spread of counterfeit medicines could be caused by many factors, including high prices of real and accurate medicines, ineffective mechanisms for drug control during production and market circulation. , Training of health officials on drug quality control skills, as well as public awareness of counterfeit drugs and limited drug control by the authorities.
According to the Prime Minister, all these factors provide opportunities for criminals to exploit society and pose a serious threat to the well-being and lives of the people.
He stressed that the scope of these accidents and negative impacts has prompted Cambodia to pay more attention to and develop mechanisms and measures to maintain the well-being of the people and reduce traffic accidents. This fake medicine.
(Preah Vihear): Under the guidance of the Senior Minister, Mr. Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport has been actively repairing and paving red and paved roads throughout Provinces to facilitate the traffic of the people easily.
Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, said that the repair work of the red gravel and rubber road team was divided into several groups, one group has been repairing and maintaining the red gravel road. A line in the geography of Choam Ksan district, which is a road in the confrontation area between the Cambodian army and the Thai army during 2008.
He said that this section of road needs to be repaired and maintained by pouring red stones to fill the chicken coop and grind it well so that people can travel easily. Meanwhile, another group at the same time has also been doing maintenance work, that is, National Road No. 62 at 176 + 800 km in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, by watering rubber, removing cracks and leveling the road surface.
"For the damaged road, if we do not hurry to repair it, it will be more damaged," he said. That is why the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the provincial governor require regular maintenance.
It should be noted that National Road No. 62 is more than 100 kilometers long, from the temple of Preah Vihear to the provincial town of Preah Vihear and continue to Kampong Thom.
CNN: South Koreans have a habit of working overtime to the point of death, and this is a challenge that is difficult to solve! (Video inside) (Seoul): Deaths due to overwork of the South Korean people remain an issue for the government of South Korean President Moon Jae-in, despite his current government trying to change habits. This is bad by reducing working hours for the weekly population.
