(Phnom Penh): After a two-week study visit to the Faculty of Chinese Language and Culture of Jinan University, a delegation of 11 students from the University of Indochina successfully returned with some experience and knowledge. Tourism and economic development.
The student delegation also gained knowledge of the culture, traditions, customs and history of relations between the two countries, Cambodia and China, dating back to the third century AD.
During the visit, the student delegation visited the 600-meter-high Guangzhou Tower, the third tallest building in the world. Visit the amusement park and take photos of Guangzhou, visit the Pearl River and see the colorful lights at night. Visit pagodas and ancient pottery sites, museums of the famous kung fu masters Luo Feng Feihong and Bruce Lee alias Li Xiaolong in Fushan.
Visit the third largest city in China, founded by the father of economic model Teng Xiaoping during the early decades, Shenzhen.
The tour allows students to learn more about the history of Chinese hijabs from the Chinese eating customs in each region. Some areas like spicy, some areas like salty, some areas like sweet.
Speaking at the closing ceremony, Shao Yi, Director General of the Faculty of Chinese Language and Culture, praised the students, who, despite the difficulties of learning different languages, still strive to succeed. Mr. Choeun assured that all participants will bring the achievements of this workshop to share and disseminate the traditional and good relations between Cambodia and China.
In response, Major General Seng Dilin, a representative of the participants, thanked the Chinese government through Jinan University for providing the opportunity for a delegation of students from the University of Indiana to pay a warm visit.
The student representative promised to take this knowledge and experience to share and disseminate more widely. Especially about the historical relationship on the Silk Road between Cambodia and China that has existed for a long time.
Mr. Dilin stated that with the success is also the merit of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which provides opportunities and ease of communication between Cambodia and China.
It should be reminded that at the opening of the seminar on October 10, 2018, Mr. Shao Yi (Director) of the Faculty of Chinese Language and Culture said that Cambodia is a country that can not be forgotten and he said that he has It is a great honor to have the permission of the Rector of Jinan to meet with 11 students from the University of Indochina, Cambodia, especially to meet with the Rector of the University of Indochina.
He said that since he was born, he has known Cambodia and knew that Cambodia and China have an inseparable friendship. Between Cambodia and China, there are more than a thousand years ago, before the Angkorian period or so-called Funan period.
Dr. Lach Samrong said that once again, Cambodia-China relations were connected by former King Norodom Sihanouk. Especially for now, Cambodia and China are firmly connected by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen.
Professor Dr. stated that due to this good relationship, the collaboration between the University of Indochina and Jinan University and this study tour.
The Rector said that the University of Indochina is honored to receive the invitation of Jinan University, and he hoped that Jinan University, especially the university leadership, will provide more opportunities for Cambodian students to study here. In addition, the professor stated that the University of Indochina will also welcome Chinese students to visit, explore and study here.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on November 3: 2,097 illegal vehicles found and 1,880 fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for November 3, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 7,070 vehicles and found 2,097 vehicles violating the law (81% motorcycles), 217 education vehicles and park 1,880 fines, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,471 helmets and goggles were inspected on November 3, 156 education helmets and 1,132 glasses were fined.
For the results of the three-day inspection from November 1 to 3, the police inspected 13,666 vehicles and found 3,016 offending vehicles (79% motorcycles), including 575 educational vehicles. And fined 2,441 units.
Actors facilitating Paris peace talks marvel at Cambodia's progress
(Phnom Penh): Jean-David, a former adviser to the French president in the 1990s and facilitator of the Paris Peace Talks (October 23, 1991) to end the flames of war and conflict by Cambodian politicians on This trip to Phnom Penh also showed surprise and amazement at Cambodia's progress.
During a courtesy call and meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of November 4, 2018, Mr. Jean David reminded of the bitter memories of Cambodia from the past and also reminded of the process of seeking negotiations. The Paris Peace Corps, of which he is a person, also played a mediating role in the negotiations.
During his visit to Phnom Penh 27 years after the Paris Peace Talks, Mr. Jean-David expressed his surprise and admiration for the progress and prosperity of Phnom Penh, which used to be a quiet city, as well as in Cambodia as a whole. .
Jean-David also expressed his happiness at seeing Cambodia progress and strengthen peace and stability.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also described the memories of peace talks in Cambodia, which Mr. Jean David acted as a facilitator. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked Mr. David for continuing to support Cambodia because he knew exactly where Cambodia came from and where it was going.
Samdech Techo Tha, His Majesty Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech himself are the most important characters that led to this peace talks. Car race event through Khmer Rally Red Conservation Area 2018 "Together to protect and conserve natural resources in Cambodia" is over
Please be informed that this motor racing event through the protected area has the participation of athletes from 5 countries, including Cambodia, Thailand, Australia, Wales, Scotland, a total of 16 motorcycles and 9 cars. For the past four days, the race has been running smoothly and without any accidents.
As for the people living in the communities around the protected areas and national parks with passing cars, they are surprised and happy that they did not expect this kind of motor racing that they used to see in other countries, but now it has arrived. Cambodia.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment believes that through the promotion of car racing through protected areas in Cambodia, this will make people aware of the potential of eco-tourism, the livelihood of the communities around the protected area, the beautiful scenery of forests, plantations and Biodiversity of all kinds.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that counterfeit medicine is a hidden killer that is facing a lot of people in remote areas. Samdech Techo said that this fake medicine not only can not help the treatment effectively, it also causes harm to users.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this while allowing Mr. Jean-David, Chairman of the Board of the Research Institute of Counterfeit Medicine of France on Sunday afternoon, November 4, 2018. Jean-David is in Cambodia for the first regional conference on "Fighting Counterfeit and Substandard Medicines" from November 5 to 6, hosted by Cambodia.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Jean-David discussed a lot about the fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs. This is according to Mr. Srey Thamrong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, speaking to the media after the meeting.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his concern about the circulation of counterfeit medicines in Cambodia and some other developing countries. The Prime Minister considered counterfeit medicine to be a worrying masked killer.
According to Srey Thamrong, during the meeting, Mr. Jean-David also mentioned the history leading up to the regional international conference on "the fight against counterfeit and substandard medicines". Mr. Jean David confirmed that the conference was held after the initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with him in 2016.
Mr. David said that the Commission and the working group are reviewing the Phnom Penh Declaration and moving forward on the circulation of counterfeit and substandard drugs to prevent and fight more effectively.
David also expressed consideration for expanding the scope of this regional international conference forum, not only for the Mekong region, but also for other countries to participate in the conference.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has agreed to expand the scope of the regional conference on the fight against counterfeit and substandard medicines in the future so that other countries can understand and enable some major countries to support this conference. More revival.
