Cambodia Hosts the 31st Conference of the Law Society for Asia and the Pacific in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Law Society for Asia and the Pacific (LAWASIA) in collaboration with the Bar Association of Cambodia and the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia held its 31st Conference under the chairmanship of Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Prime Minister of Cambodia, which took place in Siem Reap from November 2 to 5, 2018.
The conference was also attended by Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Court of Appeal, Representative of the President of the Supreme Court, Representative of the Anti-Corruption Unit, Mr. Suon Visal, President of the Bar Association of Cambodia, Mr. Christopher Long, President of the Law Association for Asia and Pacific (LAWASIA), Mr. Khim Bunsong, Governor of Siem Reap, and Mr. Prohm Vichet, Attorney General, Secretary General of the Bar Association of Cambodia.
Mr. Suon Visal, President of the Bar Association of Cambodia and President of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia, emphasized that the 31st Conference of the Law Society for Asia and the Pacific (LAWASIA) was possible with the support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director The Minister of Cambodia and it is historic that Cambodia was chosen to host this conference.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice, told the conference that Cambodia is on the right track with economic growth of more than 7% for 3 consecutive years, which is the result of political stability, social security and security. The law that Cambodia is having.
The 31st conference will address a wide range of topics, including economic issues, domestic investment, human rights protection, environmental protection, strengthening of non-judicial dispute resolution mechanisms, resolving land issues, especially strengthening international trade mechanisms, and Strive for the harmonization of laws within the regional and global framework.
