The first day of the 2018 Rally Red Race Car Race under the theme "Together to protect and conserve natural resources in Cambodia" ended and continued the second day this Saturday
(Phnom Penh): The first race through the protected area was completed almost 100% successfully, without any motorists encountering any problems, they arrived safely. The people in the area where the vehicles have to race through are very knowledgeable about motor racing and they are happy and supportive of the race.
On the first day of the race, all motorists started their journey from Phnom Penh to Kampong Speu province, with a distance of 137 km through Chbar Morn town, Oral district and Phnom Sruoch through the sanctuary area. Oral Mountain Wildlife and Kirirom National Park. Athletes saw the beautiful scenery of the fields and the lush greenery, passing through the villages, communities and across the vast sugar cane fields.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment believes that through the promotion of car racing through protected areas in Cambodia, this will make people aware of the potential of eco-tourism, the livelihood of the communities around the protected area, the beautiful scenery of the plantation forest. And biodiversity of all kinds, and also through difficult sections of roads, including mountain roads, mud roads, red dirt roads, sand roads, and obstacles.
