(Phnom Penh): More than 1.5 tons of chicken, knees, legs and chicken wings were burnt in Boeung Choeung Ek, Dangkor district after the Anti-Economic Crime Police Department and the General Department of CamControl searched a car in Chbar Ampov district. .
After the inspection, the joint police searched and found about 1 and a half tons of defective chicken meat, chicken knees, chicken legs and chicken wings.
For all of the above exhibits, Deputy Prosecutor Kham Sophary ordered the police to burn the damaged chicken wings and chicken wings at the Boeung Jing Ek landfill and bring two drivers to the department to Continue the procedure. Six short films will be ready to receive awards on the day of the 2nd National Short Film Festival
(Phnom Penh): Six short films will be shortlisted for the finals on the opening day of the 2nd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia at Chaktomuk Film Festival on November 10-15. 2018.
All films will go through two stages of evaluation by the festival's judging panel. In the first stage, the jury will review and evaluate all the works to take 6 works to be screened at Chaktomuk Theater on the closing day of the festival, while in the second stage, the committee will review and evaluate the last 6 works to select the award.
Speaking at the press conference on the 2nd National Short Film Festival of Cambodia, Mr. Pok Borak, Director of the Department of Film and Cultural Arts and Cultural Promotion, said that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts organized the second film festival in order to encourage young people to develop their abilities and Develop creative ideas to contribute to the development of the national film industry.
He added that the works to be competed must focus on cultural content, social development and focus on knowledge, attitudes and behaviors related to the daily life and experiences of young people.
(Phnom Penh): Police in Po Sen Chey district launched an operation to crack down on active drug traffickers by arresting two suspects and confiscating 19 packages of ice drugs on the afternoon of November 3, 2018. At the point of house no., Road Lum, Chung Ruk Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasang.
Colonel Yim Saran, police inspector of Por Senchey district, told Fresh News that the operation was carried out under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy National Police Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner.
Colonel Yim Saran confirmed that the first suspect: Ros Rithy, 28 years old, false occupation, living in Chung Ruk village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Sen Chey, and the second suspect: Uon Sithy, 39 years old, living in Chung Ruk village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Sen Chey. Addicted to 19 packs of transparent gram.
The suspects are now being brought along with exhibits to the district anti-drug unit to build a case to be sent to court for legal action.
Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy: We need both hardware and software infrastructure to prepare for the digital economy and the Fourth Industrial Revolution
In this regard, the Royal Government is preparing policies in line with this new trend to seize opportunities, promote technological progress in the business market, manage the business environment, as well as reduce any potential risks arising from the development of both technologies. Here via:
* Improve hard and soft infrastructure to support digital development, focusing on expanding the fiber optic distribution network, backbone infrastructure of fiber optic and submarine fiber, in line with the modernization of mobile networks and Establishment of a data center.
* Improving the logistics system for the development of the digital economy to support e-commerce with better logistics systems to transport goods from one country to another and developing platforms for financial payments.
* Update and implement telecommunications and ICT development policies, such as the Master Plan for Information and Communication Technology, the Telecommunications Law, and other relevant regulations, along with the development and implementation of ICT strategies and legal frameworks for the period Long time to support digital development.
* Develop education and training programs by expanding the use of digital technology and integrating digital technology awareness into the curriculum to ensure that our youth can benefit from new technologies.
* Promote the development of ecosystems that support research and innovation in the region, as well as the development of human resources and skills in line with the new development context, in order to reduce economic inequality by increasing the capacity of entrepreneurship to create new business models. , Create jobs and set new directions for the future economy that incorporate new ways of doing business.
At the same time, the Royal Government is currently preparing to establish a bank for small and medium enterprises, the Skills Development Fund and the Entrepreneurship Development Fund in order to support the establishment of new businesses and the promotion of entrepreneurship and small and medium enterprises, which are the backbone of the Cambodian economy. Siem Reap Authorities Celebrate International Day of Remembrance for Traffic Accident Victims
(Siem Reap): On November 3, 2018, the Siem Reap Provincial Authority celebrated the 13th International Day of Remembrance for the Victims of Road Traffic in Puok District, Siem Reap Province to commemorate the victims of traffic accidents.
The event was attended by Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, Mr. Kim Bonna, Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport and Director of the Provincial Road Safety Secretariat, Mr. Teng Channath, Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner. Monks, ladies and gentlemen, government officials, competent authorities, the armed forces, teachers, students, students, a total of more than 500 people.
On this occasion, Mr. Pin Prak said that our committee has actively implemented its work and achieved good results in disseminating the land traffic law, inspecting garages, repairing and repairing garages, assembling vehicles, inspecting vehicles for technical defects and Improvement of road equipment for traffic safety.
He added that the remarkable point of the Department of Public Works and Transport is to strive to achieve the priority points of the policy of the Royal Government in the construction, maintenance, repair of roads, bridges, providing services closer to the people, especially registration. And the issuance of driver's licenses, transportation management, technical inspections, inspections of overdue shipments, and proud results.
He added that at present, our transport infrastructure, including roads, railways, airways, waterways, ports and transportation management systems, have been restored and developed to promote and promote national and family economic growth. To the people from day to day as well.
On this occasion, the delegation and the team visited 10 patients who were injured in traffic accidents and are being treated at the referral hospital, providing them with money and drinks.
