Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Presides Over the 13th International Day of Remembrance for Traffic Accident Victims in Pursat Province
(Pursat): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, this morning, November 3, 2018, presided over the International Day of Remembrance for Traffic Accident Victims. The 13th is located in Svay Ath village, Snam Preah commune, Bakan district, Pursat province.
The National Committee for Road Safety organizes this day in order to mourn the families and victims of traffic accidents to help raise awareness of the effects of traffic accidents caused by driving illegally. Motorcycles without helmets, speeding, overtaking in dangerous situations, overweight and driving under the influence of alcohol.
It should be noted that the International Day of Remembrance for Traffic Accident Victims has been encouraged by the Royal Government to organize the National Road Safety Committee since 2006, which was first held in Phnom Penh on Sunday, November 19, 2006. Koh Kong Governor Urges Traffic Police to Strictly Enforce Laws to Protect Passengers on Public Roads
