Cambodian Cardiologists Meet to Share Experiences to Strengthen Knowledge Capacity
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Association of Cardiologists this morning, November 3, 2018, organized its 5th Annual Medical Conference to discuss and hone the knowledge and ability of the Cambodian team of doctors for one purpose: Keep patients healthy and professional.
The 5th Annual Medical Conference of the Cambodian Cardiologists Association was held at the Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh with the participation of Mr. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Prof. Sok Chuor, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Cardiologists Association.
He added that the future goal of the Cambodian Heart Association is to strengthen the capacity of all doctors in Cambodia to be as high as the local and international doctors and to make sure that all Cambodian doctors are competent and Professional enough to serve as a good doctor for all patients.
Mr. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, praised and appreciated the efforts of the Cambodian Heart Association and called on the doctors of the Medical Association to continue to pay more attention to this effort.
