Minister Delegates to the Prime Minister: Authorities and Courts Should Find Effective Measures to Suppress Thieves (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Minister Delegates to the Prime Minister and Royal Government Spokesman Phay Siphan Effective measures should be taken to crack down on street thieves, which is a chronic problem in Phnom Penh and cause fear for people every time they travel on the streets.
Mr. Phay Siphan's remarks came after a series of street robberies in Phnom Penh caused widespread harm to residents, including foreign tourists. Especially after a burglary incident that occurred at 5:40 am on November 3, 2018 in front of the English School on Street 302 in Village 7, Sangkat Beng Keng Kang 1, Khan Chamkar Morn.
The thieves shocked and kicked the victim's motorcycle, causing the victim's wife to be seriously injured and her husband to die tragically.
Mr. Phay Siphan said that this issue should not be allowed to continue. Mr. Phay Siphan said on social media on the morning of November 3, 2018, so "authorities and courts should find any effective measures to crack down on this crime. "It should not be allowed."
Please note that the incident of burglary on the streets is seen to occur in Phnom Penh almost never that day and is also a concern of the people in Phnom Penh every time they travel on the streets. . Thieves on the streets sometimes cause serious injuries and even loss of life. The activities of the thieves are not only against the people, sometimes also against foreign tourists.
The action against foreigners has been expressed as a matter of concern for foreign tourists who are afraid to visit Phnom Penh.
However, in the past, it has been observed that the authorities have often cracked down on these young thieves. But there are also reports that some of the thieves are the same targets that the authorities have arrested and cracked down on 2-3 times.
