ASEAN Recognizes Cambodia's Success in Arms Control and Sharing Experiences with Other Countries (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): ASEAN countries and ASEAN partners highly value and recognize Cambodia as A country that has had great success in controlling arms and combating illegal cross-border arms trade, and is ready to share this experience with other countries.
This is according to General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, speaking at a press conference on the night of November 2, 2018, after leading the delegation back to Cambodia after the 12th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Crime. Crossing the border in Nay Pyi Taw, Myanmar, where the General was assigned to represent Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
General Miech Sophanna stated, "ASEAN countries, as well as countries in the region and representatives of ASEAN partners, highly commend Cambodia for its great achievements in the field of arms control, especially the policy of collection and destruction. Weapons that the Royal Government of Cambodia has done successfully in the past.
General Miech Sophanna affirmed that at the 12th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting, the whole meeting also assigned Cambodia, one of the leading countries in the preparation of documents as well as action plans related to the fight against arms trafficking. Cross the border illegally to share this successful experience with other countries.
Recognizing the experience as well as what Cambodia has successfully achieved in calling on the people and consumers to illegally collect and collect weapons for destruction, ASEAN countries have initiated this idea by defining Cambodia as a leading country. Face in the security sector, focusing on the control of illegal traffic, illegal ownership of weapons. This is according to General Miech Sophanna.
The general also added that Cambodia will have to contribute to other member countries as well as partner countries, which is to share knowledge, participate in the preparation of documents, participate in the formulation of participation in the proposed law (convention) of ASEAN. Control the arms trade, combat illegal cross-border arms trade, and so on.
