During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister congratulated Mr. Tahama Pheakson on his appointment and conferred his credentials as Ambassador to Cambodia on July 11, 2018.
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his pleasure at the development of relations and cooperation between the two countries and thanked New Zealand for its continued assistance to Cambodia in human resource training, agricultural development and past contributions to the Khmer Rouge Tribunal. .
The two dignitaries also discussed the current complex and rapidly changing political and economic situation in the world, as well as regional issues such as the positive developments on the Korean Peninsula and regional innovation initiatives.
During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister spoke about the political situation in Cambodia, especially the results of the July 2018 general election, which shows the Cambodian people's desire for peace, stability and continued development and development. Develop a positive situation after the election.
The Ambassador of New Zealand thanked for this explanation and stated that although the two countries have some differences on the political situation, Cambodia and New Zealand still have other major interests and cooperation. Cooperation in the fields of education, agriculture and trade, which the Ambassador pledged to continue to push for further progress.
The Ambassador emphasized that New Zealand will continue to work with Cambodia to promote cooperation in various fields for the long-term benefit of the two nations.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador agreed to assign the relevant officials to continue discussions in the future to find ways to further promote cooperation. China and Vietnam strengthen border ties by exchanging their national currencies for the first time (Video inside)
Chinese yuan and Vietnamese dong are used on both sides of the border to facilitate trade and cooperation. And a ceremony held last week was aimed at highlighting the close ties between the people of the two countries along the border.
"When Chinese tourists are planning to visit Vietnam and want to exchange Vietnamese dong first, banks on the Chinese side of the border can Give them dong. "Also, when Vietnamese tourists want to visit or do business in China, they can exchange yuan in advance from Vietnamese banks."
