This morning, Cambodia is preparing to send another 216 Blue Hat troops to a peacekeeping mission in the Central African Republic.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 2, 2018, Cambodia sent another 216 engineers from the 594th Brigade to join a peacekeeping mission under the auspices of the United Nations in the Central African Republic. Of the 216 members of the 594th Engineering Corps, 10 were women.
The farewell ceremony for the 216th 594th Engineer Brigade was presided over by General Pol Saroeun, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions at Pochentong Air Force Base in Phnom Penh.
In addition to the farewell ceremony for the 594th Engineer Corps, Cambodia also hosted the repatriation of 216 954th Engineers from the Central African Republic and 73 618th Gendarmerie from the Republic of South Sudan.
The Repatriation Ceremony will be presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at 08:00 am on November 5, 2018. At Pochentong Air Force Base, Phnom Penh.
