The father, surnamed Li, took police and doctors to a ravine near the hospital, where they began their search at 11 a.m. the same day. According to the father, the baby was placed in a nylon bag before being thrown into a ravine.
Finally, because of her crying, the baby was found by rescuers at 1 pm, 12 hours after her father abandoned her. Rescuers told local Chinese media that the twigs helped prevent the fall and the nylon sack also protected the little girl.
Mr. Li said that Ty's family was very poor and after having two daughters and a son, he hoped to have another son, but instead had a daughter. After the incident, the black father was detained by the police.
