The vehicle race through the Khmer Rally Red Conservation Area 2018 under the theme "Together to protect and conserve natural resources in Cambodia" has started!
(Phnom Penh): The motor racing event through Khmer Rally Red Conservation Area 2018 under the theme "Together to protect and conserve natural resources in Cambodia" officially started on November 2, 2018, with a group of athletes starting to race on Road section in Kampong Speu province, passing through Kirirom National Park and Phnom Oral Wildlife Sanctuary.
Prior to the start of the race, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, presided over the flag-raising ceremony to officially start the race on the evening of November 1, 2018 at Boeung Kak Lake Park, Phnom Penh.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment believes that through the promotion of car racing through protected areas in Cambodia, people will be made aware of the potential for eco-tourism, the livelihood of the communities around the protected area, and the beautiful scenery of the plantation forest. And biodiversity of all kinds, and also through difficult sections of roads, including mountain roads, mud roads, red dirt roads, sand roads, and obstacle roads.
