(Tbong Khmum): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, confirmed that he has taken immediate action to the Tbong Khmum provincial leaders to prevent the illegal export of rubber trees to Vietnam after the complaint. And subsequent reports on this issue, which is still occurring.
On the evening of November 1, 2018, Mr. Veng Sakhon claimed that he convened an emergency meeting with the leaders and officials of the Forestry Administration to prevent the export of rubber trees, including cashew trees and illegal willow trees to Vietnam. In Tbong Khmum province, especially in Da and some other corridors.
It should be noted that the action of the Minister of Agriculture in response to the letter of intervention from local rubber wood processing business in Tbong Khmum province mentioned the difficulties and losses due to the Vietnamese traders to collect trees. Round rubber, cashew trees and acacia trees in Tbong Khmum province, with dozens of trucks being released every day without paying proper taxes to the state.
After the Minister's action to the leaders of Tbong Khmum, on the afternoon of November 2, 2018, Fresh News contacted Mr. Long Theam, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum, who is in charge of this work can not be confirmed. He is busy with meetings, waiting to be answered later.
At the same time, the local rubber wood processing business also submitted another letter requesting the intervention to the Tbong Khmum provincial governor to take action, but it has not yet been effective.
According to local traders, Vietnamese traders who rush to transport no less than 100 trucks a day are exempted from paying taxes to the state, which is very profitable. Those who do business ask for the right law have to pay taxes to many states that are unable to compete with those Vietnamese traders.
