Senior Minister Pol Saroeun's statement was made on November 2, 2018, on the occasion of the Senior Minister and Ms. Pauline Thames, United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, presiding over the ceremony to send 216 594 engineers. Peacekeeping mission under the auspices of the United Nations in the Central African Republic at the Pochentong Air Force Base in Phnom Penh.
The Senior Minister in charge of the Special Mission affirmed that Cambodia is a unified supporter of the United Nations peace and security framework. In fact, for the 12 years (2006-2018) that Cambodia has sent 5,579 Blue Hat troops (267 women) and is currently completing 811 missions (66 women) to participate in peace missions under the umbrella. United Nations.
These arguments make it clear that Cambodia loves peace, and Cambodia is committed to actively contributing to the United Nations peacekeeping operations. The Cambodian flag continues to fly high with the countries participating in the peacekeeping mission and has made Cambodia famous all over the world.
Senior Minister Pol Saroeun added that in the field of peacekeeping, the Royal Government of Cambodia has expressed its vision to ensure the sustainability of the deployment of peacekeepers, with a strong commitment to continue to contribute to the UN mission to contribute to the international community. In an effort to find peace for other countries in the world at the practical request of the United Nations.
On this occasion, Ms. PaulineTamesis, UN Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, mentioned that Cambodia is one of the largest donors in the ASEAN Community and currently has 811 Cambodian troops, of which 66 are on missions. In countries in Africa and the Middle East.
UN envoy says 594th peacekeeping force will step into its mission to become a UN family and that the mission in the Central African Republic has been under investigation for years. This is because the mission has received many reports of violence and sex trafficking by peacekeepers from some countries. The United Nations has a policy of absolute exemption for these activities.
Qatar plans to invest in agriculture in Cambodia, focusing on the production of fertilizers and pesticides!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, November 2, 2018, received Dr. Ben Yahia, Senior Executive Advisor for Strategy and Development of the Oil, Gas and Energy Sector from Qatar. Meet courtesy at the Ministry.
On that occasion, Dr. Ben Yahia, Senior Executive Advisor for Strategy and Development, thanked the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for allowing him and his delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
Dr. confirmed that he visited Cambodia for the first time to explore the potential for investment in agriculture in Cambodia, especially in the production of fertilizers and pesticides, because Cambodia is an agricultural country and Qatar has raw materials. Many can be recycled, supplied and distributed in countries and regions.
Taking that opportunity, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his welcome and support for agricultural investment projects in Cambodia.
The Minister stated that Cambodia has the potential of the agricultural sector compared to other countries in the region, especially Cambodia has the need for agro-industry, especially the processing of fertilizers and pesticides as an important raw material that can contribute to support Cambodian farmers in reducing Production costs because Cambodia currently has many fertilizer and drug companies that have been importing fertilizer products from neighboring countries.
Minister Veng Sakhon hopes that Dr. will look into the possibility of cooperating with local companies to invest in fertilizer and pesticide projects in the future. At the same time, the Minister also instructed Dr. to help promote cooperation in exporting agricultural products from Cambodia to Qatar market.
