The assassination of Khashoggi has tarnished relations between Saudi Arabia and the West, and even the United States has been reluctant to address its strategic relationship with Riyadh. A large US arms buyer.
In fact, despite claims that Khashoggi's assassination was in violation of international norms and laws, US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo did not name Saudi Arabia, but instead took the case of the Yemeni war. One to put pressure on Riyadh to stop bombing towns in Yemen.
So far, no Western country has taken any action against Saudi Arabia, while France, Germany, Britain and the United States have all warned against imposing sanctions on oil tycoons and arms buyers. If one of them is involved in the assassination of Khashoggi.
Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, who has been accused by some US lawmakers of killing Khashoggi, an outspoken critic of his leadership, has denied the allegations, while Saudi officials have warned of action. Retaliation measures and sanctions.
