Senior Minister Meas Sophea and Mr. Hun Manet Inaugurate a Building Worth More Than $ 300,000 Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Army Engineering Command in Takeo Province
(Takeo): The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Army Engineering Command, based in Bati District, Takeo Province, has officially inaugurated a two-story headquarters building donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. To the Army Engineering Command Unit this morning, November 1, 2018.
The ceremony was presided over by General Meas Sophea, Senior Minister in charge of the Special Mission of the Prime Minister of Cambodia on Mines, Unexploded Ordnance and Engineering Work of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, with the participation of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Armed Forces. The infantry and the leadership of the infantry command.
Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the Army Engineering Command, said that the 1,488.08-square-meter building was designed in the Khmer style with more than four halls. Representing the four temples and the first floor has eight rooms equal to eight offices and a meeting hall that can explode 65 people.
Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha further stated that the second floor has 8 offices, commander's room, deputy commander's office, office and hospitality room that can accommodate 65 people at a cost of approximately 319,937.2 USD. America.
The Deputy Commander of the Army said that the inauguration of the building at this time, as the leaders, officers, deputies and soldiers of all units under the command of the Army Command across the country are celebrating the anniversary. 65th Anniversary of National Independence Day and Birthday of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, November 9, 1962 - November 9, 2018 and to participate in the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Army Command 24 January 1999-24 January 2019.
