Ministry of Social Affairs signs MoU with two Japanese funds and organizations to supply used bicycles and bicycle parts to help poor people in the community
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the Bicycle Parking Fund and KJO International Organization signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the supply of used bicycles and bicycle parts on October 31, 2018 at the Ministry of Social Affairs. .
Speaking at the signing ceremony, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that this is a positive sign for the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Japan to cooperate better step by step.
Minister Vong Soth thanked the two partner organizations that have always supported and assisted Cambodia in the past, especially the activities to provide bicycle assistance to the poor people in Cambodia until now.
Mr. Maszisano, President of KJO International, also expressed his satisfaction with the cooperation with the Ministry of Social Affairs in providing bicycle assistance in the past, so far, there has been a lot of bicycle assistance from the organization to poor students in the community.
