(Preah Vihear): Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, urged farmers to grow all kinds of crops to meet the current market demand.
Such encouragement as he participated in the distribution of agricultural materials to farmers, production groups for planting and raising animals to supply the local market on October 30, 2018 in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Peng Trida said that for the Royal Government of the sixth mandate under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech has paid close attention to the market price of agricultural products of the people, the Royal Government has dropped the budget. More than 100 million dollars to buy agricultural products from the people.
He said that the Ministry of Agriculture, with Mr. Veng Sakhon as the Minister, has taken great care of farmers 'issues, in which the Minister has mobilized large foreign investors to buy farmers' crops and plans to set up agricultural processing plants. Fruits in our province as well.
In this case, Mr. Peng Trida also urged farmers to work hard to grow mixed crops as well as animal husbandry for market demand and to improve our livelihoods.
He added that with the encouragement of the people to grow other crops and raise animals, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, which supports the two ASPIRE programs, distributed agricultural materials to 42 families, including farmers. 25 families and 17 vegetable farmers.
(South Korea): Representative of the National Chemical Weapons Authority of Cambodia, Lt. Gen. Chhum Chakrya, Deputy Secretary General of the National Chemical Weapons Authority, has been attending an international seminar on the peaceful development and use of chemicals for member states of the Organization for the Prohibition of Weapons. Chemistry held for 3 days from October 30 to November 1, 2018 in Seoul, South Korea.
The international workshop was attended by representatives of 29 professional government institutions from 16 countries and an international organization around the world.
According to Lt. Gen. Chhum Chakrya, the purpose of the workshop was to improve communication between stakeholders in the region, with a particular focus on small and medium-sized sectors and the kimchi industry community. Use chemicals (chemicals specified in the Chemical Weapons Convention (CWC)) and build national capacity for regional development based on Korea's experience.
Prey Veng, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces to hold joint annual meeting 2018 this weekend
(Phnom Penh): According to the press release of the working group of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Prey Veng, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey Provinces, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in these three provinces will hold a joint meeting in 2018 on the 3rd and 3rd. November 4, 2018 at the Huangshan Hotel in front of the Australian Embassy in Phnom Penh.
On the morning of November 3, Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Vice President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in charge of Prey Veng, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces will preside over the opening ceremony. On the morning of November 4, Mr. Hun Many, Member of the National Assembly and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia will preside over the closing ceremony.
This conference was attended by the working group of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in the three provinces and more than 250 guests, and this is the second time after the first time was held in Sihanoukville in early December 2017. This morning, the National Assembly convened a meeting of the Standing Committee to review some agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 1, 2018, the National Assembly Standing Committee held a meeting chaired by National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin to review a number of agendas, including the draft law on finance. For the management of 2019 as well.
The agenda that the Standing Committee of the National Assembly discussed and approved was as follows:
1. The meeting approved the handover of the draft law on finance for the year 2019 to the Committee on Economy, Finance, Banking and Auditing of the National Assembly for review and study and report to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
2. The meeting approved the handing over of the draft law on the payment of the general state budget for the year 2017 to the Economic, Finance, Banking and Auditing Committee of the National Assembly for review and study and report to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
3. The Meeting approved the submission of the draft law on the ratification of the Extradition Treaty between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation to the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly in cooperation with the National Assembly Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information. And study and report back to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
4: The meeting approved and handed over the draft law on the approval of:
* Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax.
Senior Minister Kun Kim inspected the actual land location and handed over the houses to two families of veterans as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association, handed over two houses in O'Ambel village, O'Tameng commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, President of the Veterans Association. Cambodia provides two members of the Cambodian Veterans Association from Phnom Penh who are poor and homeless.
Speaking on that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also conveyed Samdech Techo Hun Sen's greetings to the members, who always consider the members' health and well-being according to the current report of the provincial association and at his own request. Decided to build two more houses and handed over today.
Please be informed that the two houses, each measuring 5 meters by 6 meters, made of wood, zinc, tiles and wooden walls, were handed over to the families of two veterans' associations. Village 12, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh, and 2nd: Mr. Chhay Sarath, a disabled soldier in Village 12, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh.
