Ministry of Health and related partners to strengthen health services for poor patients at the local level to be more high quality and effective
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health and relevant partners held a workshop on the role and responsibilities of the Health Finance Committee of the Equity Fund for Poor Patients to provide guidelines for the implementation of this equity fund to provide quality services to poor patients at the local level. Effectiveness, safety, equity and accountability of the Ministry of Health.
The event was held on October 31, 2018 at Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel with the participation of Prof. Eng Huot, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Special Authority, Representative of the Board of Governors of the Capital-Province, District / Khan, Director of the Capital-Provincial Health Department and Chiefs of OD offices, as well as relevant institutions, including development partners.
Prof. Eng Huot said, "The Health Equity Fund is the only large-scale financial risk mobilization mechanism that demonstrates the effectiveness of state investment in financial resources to improve the health of the poor." "Reducing out-of-pocket spending on health care and increasing the provision of financial support can help people escape the dangers of health care costs and prevent them from falling into poverty."
"Strengthening the role of the National Capital-Provincial-Executive Committees and ODs, which requires high commitment and support from stakeholders, especially Capital-provincial, district / Khan authorities and health officials at all levels." .
She hopes to strengthen some of the governance work and help raise awareness of the benefits of access to health services by using equity cards to increase access to services by strengthening the role and function of the Board of Directors. Financing national, provincial and district hospitals for the implementation of health equity fund.
