Prek Pnov District Governor Temporarily Suspends Construction in Sangkat Ponhea Ponn for Violating State Public Roads
(Phnom Penh): The construction site of a strong house with the brand name "Ros Rathaya" located in Thom Cheung village, Sangkat Ponhea Pon, Khan Prek Pnov, which was reported by the villagers to be completely encroaching on the public road. Almost half of the state has been temporarily suspended by Prek Pnov district governor Sok Sambath because the construction was claimed by officials to have violated the road.
On the afternoon of October 31, 2018, Mr. Khon Veasna, Director of Prek Pnov District Inter-Sector Office, told Fresh News that this case was ordered by Mr. Sok Sambath, District Governor and Mr. Chea Khema, Deputy District Governor, and other relevant officials. To make a record of the temporary suspension of construction because it affects the master plan contained in the data of Phnom Penh Capital Hall in the project to open the road up to 12 meters.
However, after the Prek Pnov district authorities suspended the construction, Ms. Ros Rathaya, the owner of the construction, came out to explain that she did not build in violation of the state's public road, instead she had a valid construction permit. From the Sangkat authorities and are preparing to take the permit to continue to ask the law to the district to be legal.
Ms. Ros Rathaya claims that this time there will be no more concessions for the authorities to open the road because her residential land is getting smaller and smaller.
It should be noted that the construction site of a strong house with the brand name "Ros Rathaya" is reported by the people that it has been completely encroaching on the public land of the state, almost half the length of the road. 10 meters left only 5 to 6 meters, but did not see the presence of village, sangkat or Khan authorities came down to prevent it, suspecting a large cable pool or a blue light from any official.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the rise of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, was based on respect for human rights and democracy.
He said this on October 31, 2018, on the occasion of the International Relations Institute of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, under the cooperation and support of the Konrad Adenauer Foundation in Cambodia, held an international conference on "40 years of ASEAN cooperation. EU: Achievements and the Way Forward "at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Dr. Sok Touch stated that "Democracy has a clear definition: the people are the masters, and the power of the people, the power of the rise of Prime Minister Hun Sen is not because of the coup, but because of the election of the Cambodian people. More than 83 percent. "This is the definition of democracy that originated in prehistoric Greece."
Addressing Ambassadors, Ambassadors to Cambodia, national and international dignitaries, especially national and international speakers from the European Union and other ASEAN member countries, Dr. Sok Touch After decades of chronic war, the bitter and dark pages of Cambodia's history are completely over.
According to Dr. Cambodia, there is now peace, political stability and economic development. With the high commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia, many achievements have been made.
In fact, GDP growth has been steady and annual economic growth has been around 7%. The growth of exports of finished products from Cambodia, the growth of agricultural production and the growth of tourists have increased significantly, which is a sign of harmony and security situation, stability, good security in Cambodia. Cambodia's cities and rural areas are undergoing a new face, highlighting the potential for advancement.
Ms. Rona Smith arrived in Cambodia on October 28, 2018 for an 11-day visit from October 29 to November 8, 2018 at the invitation of the Royal Government of Cambodia. During the 11-day visit, the expert is scheduled to meet with senior government officials, civil society representatives and members of the diplomatic community.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen explained that the fulfillment of Samdech's mission abroad has brought benefits to the nation, such as seeking scholarships to train Cambodian students, gaining international cooperation in economics, politics, security, as well as national defense. . On the other hand, hosting the upcoming Asia-Europe Summit in 2020 is Cambodia's face on the international stage. Samdech considers this a success in the field of diplomacy.
Along with harsh criticism of analysts, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed skepticism about the failure of opposition groups attempting to organize anti-Samdech demonstrations in Switzerland. Samdech considers this a strange thing.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the opposition group if they act against it is not strange, but if they do not oppose it is strange. At the same time, Samdech concluded that the reason why there were no anti-Samdech demonstrations in Switzerland and no demonstrators in New York was because the opposition group was incapable of mobilizing people to participate in the demonstration.
At the same time, many Cambodians abroad began to support Samdech's policies and leadership, which led to Cambodia's continued development with a 7% economic growth rate. USGS staff use the computer of the institution to watch hot movies and spread the virus all over the place!
