In the third quarter of this year, there were 745 traffic accidents, resulting in 383 deaths and more than 1,000 injuries, both the number of deaths and injuries decreased!
This is according to the report summarizing the traffic safety work results for the third quarter of 2018 of the Second Sub-Committee of the National Road Safety Committee (NRCC) presented at the law enforcement meeting. Road traffic in the third quarter of 2018 under the presidency of General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police this morning, October 31, 2018.
The meeting to monitor the implementation of the road traffic law in the third quarter of 2018 was also attended by representatives of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the Ministry of Justice, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Health, the National Gendarmerie and Leaders of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department and the Deputy Commissioner in charge of traffic order in the capital-province, a total of 50 people.
During the meeting, General Him Yan also stated that "With the joint efforts to maintain good order and traffic safety, the road traffic police force and officials of relevant institutions have reduced traffic accidents. In the first nine months of 2018, there were 353 road accidents, equal to 13%, reducing the number of fatalities by 44, equal to 3%, and reducing the number of injuries by 795, equal to 19% compared to the same period of 2017.
(Xinhua) - A Cambodian delegation visiting China led by Mr. Chuon Chanparun, Minister of Information of the Ministry of Information of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 31, 2018, visited Xinghua, Jiangsu Province.
During the visit in Singhor, the Cambodian delegation was invited to visit the production chain at three factories and public service facilities in the city.
The factories visited include factories that install and manufacture generators, pumps and tractors. The plant assembles about 1,500 machines a day and exports to about 50 countries around the world, including Cambodia.
Noodle production enterprise. The enterprise produces about 100 million packages of noodles a year and about 500 million packages of domestic and foreign orders. For sale, a pack costs 10 yuan ($ 1.5).
After visiting the noodle factory, the Cambodian delegation also visited the meat factory. The enterprise produces about 600 tons of various kinds of meat and meatballs per day.
At the end of the short and short visit of the Cambodian media delegation in the city, they were invited to explore the city's public service, which in Cambodia is called "One Stop". That.
At the public service center, there are service offices from 28 institutions, such as business registration, identity card, passport, land title, etc. Many people have come to this public service center and public service officials are also smiling at providing services to the people.
The Cambodian delegation visited many Chinese government institutions, factories, enterprises and hospitals to learn about the services, production chain and development of those institutions and also disseminated information to Cambodia. CamControl Officers Find Meatballs, Beef, Fish, Riel, Pickles and Pickles Containing Chemicals for Sale at Happy Market and Chhouk Meas Market in Sen Sok District
(Phnom Penh): Camcontrol Branch, Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, this morning, October 31, 2018, in cooperation with the Laboratory Department of the General Department of CamControl, brought the mobile test vehicle of the General Department of CamControl to inspect the quality of goods at Happy Market and Chhouk Market. Gold in Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, with the participation of the Department of Commerce and the Market Commission.
Officials from the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone (Camcontrol) branch said that during the inspection, 69 samples of high-risk food items were suspected, including: beans, sausage, trout, dried fish, beef, meatballs, noodles. Banh Kanh Noodles, a variety of fresh vegetables, pickles, fresh seafood, blueberries, crisps and more. The team analyzed the banned chemicals in the mobile simulator.
During the inspection of the quality of the goods, the CamControl officer also distributed the posters to the producers as well as the food vendors, please participate in maintaining good hygiene, please do not produce, distribute or take goods that do not have quality or chemicals. Selling because it affects the health of consumers.
For buyers, please buy food that is safe, hygienic, please consider before deciding to buy goods that are unusual, goods that are beautiful, attractive.
