Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Calls on Students to Stay Away from Drugs
(Preah Vihear): Addressing teachers as well as students on the occasion of the opening day of the new school year 2018-2019 and the inauguration ceremony of Pong Teuk Primary School this morning, October 31, 2018, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province called All students should stay away from all kinds of drugs, do not try to try, which leads to damage to their own future and loss of family honor.
He said that today, the drug problem is a problem that is happening almost everywhere and has penetrated the masses, especially the youth in this high school, and a small number of students are playing the role of distributing drugs. This addiction is being monitored by the authorities.
"Students must stay away from all kinds of drugs without trying, which leads to loss of time to study, damage the future and damage the reputation of our family," said the governor.
Regarding the opening day of the new school year 2018-2019, Mr. Un Chanda said that the opening ceremony of the new school year is the 38th anniversary of the revival of the education sector after being devastated by the war, especially the destruction of The roots of the Democratic Kampuchea regime, which ruled the country for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days.
As a result of the war and the crimes of democracy, the scars left behind and the conscience of the people fell on the people almost irreparably. Thanks to the great merits of the Cambodian People's Party, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the country has achieved complete peace, political stability, and development in almost all areas, including the education sector, which has made significant progress in both quantity and quality. Quality.
At the same time, Mr. Un Chanda advised teachers to strengthen the management leadership of educational structures at all levels, especially the management of schools, because schools are the front lines that have to fight directly with education.
Mr. Cheng Lim Hean, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, said that in 2018-2019, Preah Vihear Province has 6 educational institutions, 227 primary schools, 48 secondary schools, And 16 high schools. There are 2,475 academic staff, including 128 females.
