The tallest statue in the world officially inaugurated under the presidency of the Prime Minister of India
Sardar Patel played a key role in India's liberation struggle and was a popular leader who was deeply concerned about the well-being of Indian farmers. This huge statue has a total construction cost of more than 400 million US dollars.
Patel's 143rd birthday was also marked on the day the statue was unveiled. This tall statue is claimed to be able to withstand wind speeds of up to 60 meters per second and can withstand earthquakes and vibrations. The public will be able to visit the statue from November 3.
