This is the third time that a delegation of CVEA leaders and members has attended the NAR Annual Meeting, which will be attended by more than 20,000 members from 65 countries. The mission lasts for two weeks, and according to the plan, in addition to attending the meeting, CVEA leaders will also visit some states to learn more about land technology, as well as to visit the Cambodian people living there.
During a ceremony held at a factory in Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, which was attended by more than 6,700 workers, Samdech Techo Prime Minister revealed the three lies of the opposition group, including: Second, Samdech Techo Hun Sen could not attend the UN General Assembly.
However, the deception of the people by the opposition politicians never helped the nation and the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that the three lies of the opposition were completely eliminated in New York City. When the prince steps on the red carpet at a UN meeting.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "If we talk about their lies, the lies at the United Nations lie to three stories, the first lie: that the United States can not land, but in the end, US security must provide Full support for Prime Minister Hun Sen to the United Nations, because it is the territory of the United States, the United States does not forget its duty to protect the leaders who go to the United Nations.
Myth 2: Cambodia's seat at the United Nations has already been stripped of its seat at the United Nations. Myth 3: Seats were not plowed, but Prime Minister Hun Sen's meeting was not attended. "These three lies have been dispelled in New York City through the presence and statement of the United Nations."
The head of the Royal Government claimed that a series of lies by the opposition that were false and that these lies were daily, weekly or hourly lies, but many of them were self-defeating and stressed that Samdech's presence abroad is the most important thing for the nation.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also took to the mass demonstrations that the opposition, organizers and rallies were very small compared to those who came to receive and welcome the presence of Samdech. For this situation shows the character of leaders who like to deceive the people and their children.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has organized a two-day job fair. This job fair provides many job opportunities for the public who want to work in companies that they like with their knowledge and skills.
The job fair is organized with the participation of seven major ministries, including 156 local and foreign companies from key sectors such as manufacturing, finance and real estate.
The big fair was also attended by six subsidiaries of Prince Realty who participated in this job fair. The company has announced a lot of jobs for students and the general public.
Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, spoke about the changes and growth in the industry, leading job seekers to focus on increasing their ability to get good jobs.
He added that the current economic development in Cambodia has achieved remarkable results, being recognized as "the new tiger of the Asian economy." With the growth of society and industry, the market demand for human resources is also gradually changing.
Dr. Ith Sam Heng and Mr. Ly Minh, Chief Executive Officer of Prince Real Estate Group, encouraged the candidates to apply for the job and work hard when they get the job. On that occasion, Dr. Ith Sam Heng also handed over a letter of thanks to Prince Real Estate Group.
During the two-day job fair, the company received about 3,500 applicants. The company welcomes people with experience and ability to work.
(Kampot): Asia-Europe athletes collect medals in almost all disciplines from the 5th International Half Marathon 2018 on Bokor Mountain, Kampot Province, to raise funds for Kantha Bopha Hospital.
This day is designed to give participants the perfect opportunity to create unforgettable memories with family and friends in the sense of promoting health, happiness and charity.
This international event attracted 1,459 runners as it is a sport, tourism and charity event, so national and international runners have shown a willingness to participate and unite in a spirit of high solidarity in charity work.
Mr. Pov Hok, Sports Coach, Asia-Europe University Sports Club, who led his team of more than 30 athletes to the competition, expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Duong Leang, President of the Asia-Europe Council for supporting and encouraging the athletes to participate. Run and participate in this charity work.
The winners of all disciplines include: Men's 21km Runner-up: Ma Viro from Asia Europe University, Women's First place: British Jiu Hamill.
In the men's 10km race, the first place went to Cambodian Vann Pheara, while the first place in the women's event was won by Cambodian athlete from Asia Europe University Bou Samnang. In the 5km race, the first place went to Phat Sophot, while in the women's section, Nguon Jaronai Yi and the 3km race went to Phan Phan Chi. In addition, there are also the 2nd and 3rd place in the men's and women's categories in all disciplines.
The beauty of the people and the country of Cambodia will be revealed through the photo contest of Cambodia Angkor Air 2018
(Phnom Penh): The amazing scenery and life of the Cambodian people has been revealed by Cambodia Angkor Air in collaboration with the Ministry of Tourism through a photo contest called Cambodia Angkor Air 2018 Photo Contest, which will Open to the participation of all Cambodians.
