Police in Bakan district, Pursat province, cracked down on a suspect using, storing and trafficking drugs along with some exhibits
(Pursat): The police force of Bakan district, Pursat province, in cooperation with the Khnar Toteung police force, continued its search activities until the arrest and arrest of a suspect who used, stored and traded drugs, and confiscated 6 small packages of drugs. Exhibits.
Colonel Yem Yoeun, Deputy Police Inspector of Bakan District, said that the operation took place at 12:15 at the home of 36-year-old Hu Hom, a suspect living in Phteah Sla Village, Khnar Toteung Commune, Bakan District. Pursat.
According to the Deputy Inspector, in the operation to crack down on the suspects using, storing and trafficking drugs, the police force confiscated 6 small packages of white gram powder, 1 pack of cigarettes, 1 Nokia mobile phone, 1 pack of Paris, 1 trigger and Khmer money 52,000 riels.
Currently, the suspects who were apprehended above, together with the relevant exhibits, must be brought into temporary detention at the Krakor District Police Inspectorate to build a case file for further proceedings. Very symphonic! Boy kills himself with arrow
(Koh Kong): A boy made an arrow to shoot fish, but accidentally ran through his ribs, causing his death in Preah Ang Keo village, Dong Peng commune, Sre Ambel district at 2:30 on October 30. 2018.
According to the police report, the body of the victim, 13-year-old Sieng An, a resident of the above-mentioned village-commune, was shot in the right rib and pierced to one side, causing his death on the spot.
According to the victim's parents, when his son went fishing in the river, he dived to catch fish, but did not see the fish, came back to the shore and took the fishing gear. The crutch touches the key, causing the sharp arrow to pierce the body to the right rib, pierce to one side, and die instantly.
After receiving the information, the Sre Ambel District Police Inspectorate, in cooperation with the administrative police force, conducted an autopsy. After examination, the expert force confirmed that the victim really died due to the self-inflicted fishing gear.
At present, the body has been handed over to the guardians for a traditional ceremony.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Chairs an Inter-Ministerial Meeting on Drugs
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 31, 2018, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, chaired an inter-ministerial meeting to disseminate information on drug issues.
The meeting was attended by representatives of 27 relevant ministries and institutions, including the leaders of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, which was held at the Ministry of Interior.
4,020 drug users were receiving treatment at public health facilities, accounting for 23.94%.
If something goes wrong, the rocket launch will not be possible and will result in huge losses. Therefore, great care is required to check for any mistakes, even the smallest ones.
It combines the development of manual devices for fuel quality testing.
"The standard thickness of the bulb shell should be thinner than 0.1 mm, but too thick or too thin is also a problem," said Wei Sufeng, a laboratory technician at the five-branch launch test station at the Taiyuan Satellite Launch Center. Blowing air into a bulb is also not easy. "Every time we blow air into each bulb, the air force must be thick and smooth, not too strong or too weak."
Once the bulb is ready, the next step is to analyze the rocket fuel. Because fuels are flammable, explosive and easily cut, laboratory technicians are required to wear a suit and face mask when entering the sample for analysis.
Liu Dongseng, director of the five-branch launch test station, said: "Suits and face masks can avoid us from danger, but wearing this suit is not easy. For example, in the summer, when the temperature rises, we work long hours, and at the end of the day, water flows out of the suit. ”
Even after the first test is over, we have to wait for the fuel to cool down before launching the rocket to ensure the safety of the mission.
Wu Jinsheng, a technician in the laboratory of the launch test station of the five branches of the Taiyuan Satellite Launch Center, said: "Four liquid chemical devices are needed, as well as the analysis and testing of 32 identifiers. Times. "To ensure the quality of each liquid chemical device, three consecutive tests must be performed for those markers." (China's CCTV)
Cambodia to Send 216 Blue Hat Troops to Peacekeeping Mission in Central African Republic in Early November (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Nation in the Central African Republic on the morning of November 2, 2018. This is according to the announcement of the spokesperson of the Ministry of National Defense on October 31, 2018.
