This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets Nearly 7,000 Workers in Muk Kampul District
(Phnom Penh): After a long absence in meeting with Cambodian workers due to a series of missions abroad, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to meet with more than 6,700 workers in Prek Anchanh commune. Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, this morning, October 31, 2018. The workers are from four factories in Muk Kampul district.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, so far, Kandal province has 464 factories, enterprises and establishments with 155,138 workers with a total wage of $ 372 million. There are 170 garment and footwear factories with 137,664 workers, earning more than $ 330 million a year.
The Minister of Labor also highlighted that this is the success of the policy of attracting investment, the national policy on employment and employment, the policy of industrial development in Cambodia, the policy on education, technical and vocational training and the national protection policy framework. Society of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced a campaign to meet with workers in factories in Cambodia every week since mid-2017 to find out about the well-being of workers and solve problems for them.
