(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation on October 30, 2018 organized a meeting between the tax department and the private sector to find solutions to market challenges and tax issues.
The meeting was organized by Mr. Kong Vibol, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Co-Chair of the Partnership Mechanism, General Department of Taxation - Private Sector and Private and many other tax officials.
Today's meeting achieved important results, including: 1. Discussing and providing solutions to 11 tax-related challenges in addition to the challenges addressed at the level of this partnership mechanism. In particular, the remaining issues will continue to be resolved in a spirit of mutual cooperation.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that through careful implementation of administrative reform and fiscal policy, as well as tax modernization in accordance with the medium-term revenue collection strategy 2014-2018 as a result of tax revenue management. And all types of taxes in 2017 achieved 115.2% of the legal plan.
He added that as of October 26, 2018, the General Department of Taxation has collected 97.44% of the total tax and tax revenue (online) of the plan set by the Financial Law for 2018.
He added that new progress related to taxation is the goal of implementation for 2019, in which the General Department of Taxation is studying to adjust the value of real estate as a basis for taxation, stamping on the transfer of ownership - ownership of real estate, improvement. Special taxes on certain goods and services, public comment tax, and amendments to some articles necessary for the implementation of tax revenue collection.
