Inter-ministerial plan to develop tourism master plan in Siem Reap to develop new tourism products and extend stay of international tourists in Cambodia
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government has decided to establish an "Inter-Ministerial Commission and to study and prepare a master plan for the development of tourism in Siem Reap" in order to prepare a master plan for the development of tourism in Siem Reap to study and develop tourism products. Recently in Siem Reap aims to extend the stay of international tourists.
This is a new policy of the Royal Government to develop the tourism sector in Cambodia to grow, especially to promote the sustainable development of tourism in Siem Reap.
The first meeting was held for the purpose of announcing the composition of the inter-ministerial commission and the secretariat to discuss the preparation of the master plan for the development of Siem Reap city and Siem Reap province, as well as the work plan of the inter-ministerial commission.
Mr. Khim Bunsong informed about the development in Siem Reap, including strengthening security and public order, preparing the master plan and land use plan of Siam, improving the quality of food and hygiene, promoting the attraction of private investment, especially investment in tourism products. Recently.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona highlighted the need for zoning between heritage sites and recreation areas to ensure that heritage sites do not fall victim to the development index, in particular, she advocated a master plan for tourism development. In Siem Reap, sustainable.
The meeting discussed and agreed on some important points:
* Siem Reap City Development Master Plan: To promote the development of Siem Reap City Master Plan to be developed as a tourist city, a heritage city and an environmentally conscious city by integrating the economic, social, cultural, environmental and architectural aspects to support The increase in tourists visiting Siem Reap, both national and international, especially in line with the concept of "conservation for development, while development supports conservation."
* Infrastructure development in the province: To study and prepare adequate water and electricity supply systems and to set up solid and liquid waste management systems in accordance with environmental standards. At the same time, it must be well-organized and orderly, have enough traffic lights, light the city of Siem Reap, beautify the Siem Reap River, widen the city streets, especially pedestrian and bicycle lanes.
* Development of tourist areas around Siem Reap and support the "Siem Reap: Beyond Temples" campaign, especially in Prek Toal, Chong Khneas, Tonle Sap Lake, Phnom Kulen and community tourism areas, agro-tourism, rural tourism, various tourism products and special sports tourism events to increase Competitive advantage of Siem Reap tourism and prolong the stay of tourists.
Improving the quality of tourism services and human resources in the tourism sector in response to the growth of tourists by strengthening the quality of tourism vocational training schools, internal training and promoting the implementation of ASEAN standards in tourism.
* Reducing the leakage of tourism caused by the import of vegetables, fruits and meat from abroad: To promote the development of the green belt around Siem Reap by promoting the cultivation of vegetables, fruits and livestock to meet the needs of tourists.
* Chinese Tourism Preparation: Promote the implementation of the China Ready Handbook for Cambodian Tourism and the Cambodian Assessment Standards for Chinese Tourist Preparedness Services prepared by the Ministry of Tourism to facilitate the travel and accommodation of Chinese tourists. Holds Siem Reap Province.
It should be noted that for the first nine months of 2018, Siem Reap received about 1.9 million international tourists, an increase of 8.47%, of which about 830,000 Chinese tourists. Educate young children through the first reading program in Kampong Cham
(Phnom Penh): Prudential Cambodia has promoted and improved access to education for young children in poor communities by distributing educational materials to more than 50 families in Kampong Cham province.
Last week, Prudential Cambodia volunteers distributed children's books and organized a number of activities to improve children's reading skills and learning ability. Through some fun games and activities organized, parents are encouraged to pay more attention to their children's development in childhood.
"Education is at the core of talent development for the country and it starts with educating young children," said Heng Vuthy, director of customer and marketing at Prudential Cambodia. Encouraging young children to read and play with educational materials can help keep them healthy. I believe that the first reading program will help our children realize their full potential and strengthen Cambodia's long-term development. ”
Launched in Cambodia in 2013, the first reading program aims to provide parents and guardians with skills to help teach their children to read and to enable more children to succeed in their studies and to Get a better quality of life.
The first reading program was implemented in 425 villages in Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Prey Veng and Kratie provinces. It is one of the highlights of the Prudential Foundation Community Investment Initiative for Cambodia, focusing on education, health and safety.
