(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, said that for the past five years, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has been achieving great success in the securities sector. That is why the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has prepared a report that would like to compile a 100-page book on the five-year achievements of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia.
This report details the achievements of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia over the past five years, as well as many major achievements to further promote the development of the Cambodian Securities Market.
Mr. Sou Socheat said, "The preparation of the securities sector has been carried out by a clear development strategy by the Securities and Exchange Commission called the Financial Sector Development Strategy. So far, it has been updated to the Financial Sector Development Strategy 2016-2025, which is a strategy. Planned for 10 years.
He stated that currently, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has achieved many major achievements, including: 1, the launch of the market, the preparation of all regulations to be the backbone for the securities sector, the diversification of various products in the securities market. , Market Diversification as well as the Integration of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia into the region and the world.
"Currently, there are five issuers in the stock market, while the sixth and seventh companies are also preparing to enter gradually and may complete the listing around the end of this year or early next year," he said. The Securities and Exchange Commission has also diversified its products. Currently, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has only one type of trading: stock, which is a type of securities.
He added that the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has recently developed a new procedure to allow companies to issue bonds to public securities as well. The bond issuer will list the securities on the market.
He said that in a few weeks, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia will have a new type of securities traded on the market, bonds or bonds. This is product diversification to expand the number of listed companies, diversification of products to get the applause of investors, as well as market diversification to expand the securities market.
(Phnom Penh): Currently, banking and microfinance institutions have been entering the Cambodian securities market. Recently, Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution announced its issuance of 120 billion riels worth of corporate bonds (about 30 million US dollars) while ASA, Plc. Holding 25% of ACLEDA Bank, it is also preparing to issue shares.
This step into the securities market was confirmed by Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, which will help make the securities sector more attractive and active in the future.
He said that the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia is currently expanding the number of products in the market by encouraging companies to enter the market. Of course, every investor is always looking for stocks that are attractive, have a lot of momentum, a lot of evolution.
The visit of the Chinese high-level parliamentary delegation was made at the invitation of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia. The delegation was led by Zhang Chunxian, vice chairman of the National People's Congress. During the visit, high-level delegations from the Chinese National People's Congress (NPC) are expected to pay a courtesy call on key Cambodian leaders, including:
* Pay a courtesy call and hold a hearing with Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia
* Courtesy call and hearing with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia
