(Phnom Penh): The case of fire in the case of foam handicraft on Street 371 near Wat Po Nhean, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun II, Khan Meanchey, on the afternoon of October 30, 2018, was completely extinguished after careful intervention. From the police and local authorities quickly.
According to a report from Fresh News Agency from the scene, around the rescue operation, the police sent 28 water trucks to rescue, but only 22 water cannons, including the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. Phnom Penh fired 12, the Ministry of Interior fired 5, the Phnom Penh Military Police fired 4 and Cambodian Beer fired 1.
Mr. Prohm Yot, Director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed that the fire was caused by a welder on the roof of the handicraft and that the fire broke out and caused a huge fire. But this case does not cause any citizens to suffer.
(Kampong Speu): The business of clearing the gas station is still popular, despite the authorities and Camcontrol officials with educational guidance. In fact, CamControl officials in Kampong Speu province on October 30, 2018, continued to find 4 gas stations and depots in Samrong Tong and Kong Pisey districts of Kampong Speu province, selling low quality oil and falsifying quality.
According to Nhung Wen, the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as a caliper tank with a specific volume for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, with a capacity of 05 liters 10 liters and 20 liters. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles. Retail prices at stations and depots are based on the notification of the Ministry of Commerce.
He said that as a result of the inspection of fuel at nine stations at the above location, there are five petrol stations in compliance with both quantity and quality. However, there is one non-compliance with the quantity and three non-compliance with the quality and quantity.
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese government is planning to implement a series of measures to boost private sector investment. This is according to a spokesman for China's top economic planning body on Wednesday last week in Beijing.
Meng Wei, a spokeswoman for the National Development and Reform Commission of China, said that since the beginning of this year, China has seen an increase in private investment. And as this growth rate continues to outpace the overall investment rate, private sector investment has become an important driving force for maintaining stable investment.
The committee will encourage investment from private companies through updated working mechanisms, reducing unexpected barriers and making investment easier. According to Ms. Moeng.
At the same time, the committee will promote for many years for private companies to invest in various projects, as well as regularly publish a list of projects that private companies are encouraged to invest. The list is compiled based on the approval and online monitoring system of the National Investment Project. According to Ms. Moeng.
Recent projects that the committee has encouraged private companies to invest in include transportation, energy, ecology, environmental protection and social sectors. To date, private companies have invested $ 360 billion in these areas. (China's CCTV)
