Angela Merkel on Monday told the CDU that she would not run in the next presidential election in December, especially as she would step down as chancellor. Germany in 2021.
Merkel's decision comes after her party failed a regional election that severely damaged the stability of the current German coalition coalition. Merkel has been chairing the CDU since 2000 and is one of the longest-serving leaders in Europe.
