(Bangkok): Mr. Yin Vannak, Governor of Kratie Municipality, Representative of the Voice of Cambodia, was invited to attend the "World Forum on Human Settlements 2018", which will be held for two days from October 30-31. In Bangkok, Thailand, there were about 350 participants from 40 countries, from the United Nations (UN), senior government officials of Thailand and other countries, mayors and civil society organizations.
Mr. Yin Vannak was invited to participate in this important forum through the coordination between the organizers and the National League of Associations, Associations, Municipal, District, Khan, Commune and Sangkat Councils of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
On the first day, the forum celebrated World Urban Day 2018, focusing on the topic "Promoting innovation in urban development to achieve the 11 sustainable development goals and the new urban development agenda."
At the same time, the forum will also hold a ceremony to "award the Sustainable Settlement of Humans and Cities 2018" to recognize good practices in sustainable development.
Kampong Thom Provincial Administration Celebrates the 14th Anniversary of the King's Reign
The blessing ceremony for the 14th anniversary of the accession to the throne of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni was presided over by Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Sok Loo, Provincial Governor, Monks, Ladies and Gentlemen of the three Armed Forces. Ladies and Gentlemen, Heads of Departments, Units and Government Officials around many provinces.
It should also be noted that on October 29, 2004, Samdech Preah Boromneath Norodom Sihamoni was elected by the Royal Council of Thirteen and unanimously elected as the King to succeed His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej. King Norodom Sihanouk, the royal father, abdicated on October 7, 2004.
Russey Keo District Police Force Continues to Crack Down on 4 Suspects in Drug Use and Storage
(Phnom Penh): Russey Keo District Police Force under the direct command of Colonel Koul Yi, District Police Inspector, continues to search until the arrest of 4 more suspects using and storing drugs. Also confiscated 3 packs of drugs and 1 motorcycle.
Russey Keo District Police Inspector continued that in the operation to crack down on the suspects using and storing the above four drugs, it was carried out during the inspection of the land traffic law and the substance of alcohol along National Road 5. In the fourth group, Khleang Saing village, Russey Keo commune, and another location along National Road 5 in the same group 5, Lokambor village, Svay Pak commune, on October 29, 2018.
According to the inspector, the arrested suspects are: Chan Kolap, 33 years old, a construction worker living in a construction site in Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo, and another named Tam Wang, 17 years old, a construction worker, false residence. Sure. During the operation, police confiscated two small packages of white plastic and a silver 125cc motorcycle without a license plate.
Separately, the suspects who were apprehended in the second case of drug use were named May Sambo, 27 years old, a worker living in Trapeang Rong village, Chrey Las commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province (kept) and Song Samnang, 20 years old. Occupation: Worker living in Ta Ling village, Khsem Khsan commune, Oudong district, Kampong Speu province (Use).
Colonel Koul Yi also stated that immediately after the crackdown, the four suspects with relevant exhibits were brought into pretrial detention to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with the procedure.
Specialized University of Cambodia organizes a conference on "Studying at Higher Education for a Prosperous and Successful Future"
(Kampot): The Cambodian University of Specialties, Kampot Branch, organized a conference on "Studying at Higher Education for a Prosperous and Successful Future" with the participation of more than 200 professors and students who had just graduated from high school. .
The conference aims to show participants the purpose of continuing their studies to achieve good and successful results and research, as well as some ideas and traits that lead students to actively participate in the job market after Graduate and lead to success in your career and future life.
The conference on October 28, 2018 was also attended by many distinguished speakers, including university leaders with a lot of experience and knowledge, presented and shared to the ceremony.
In addition to this content, Dr. Keo Chea asserted that students must work hard to study, which is a priority work during their life as a student and research focused on specific skills, as well as to strive to study additional skills such as foreign languages, computers and so on.
Dr. also showed the key to a successful person, such as having a goal in life, try to read a lot, manage time well, study outside of school, gain knowledge, be proficient in work, be creative and act with discipline and good character, virtue, hard work. Work and behave with dignity and responsibility.
Mr. Mang Sokha, Director of Vattanac Asia Bank Limited, Kampot Branch, which is a partner of the University, affirmed that specific skills, hard work and responsibility are the qualities that his institution as well as other institutions want because it is The main resources of the institution.
In closing, Dr. Meas Bora, Rector and on behalf of the chairperson of the conference, summarized the content and encouraged the students to study hard, prepare well to become human resources, virtues, knowledge, skills, abilities and experiences for themselves, their families, their society and Nation.
Please be reminded that CUS University has started training for 17 years and at all levels in 5 colleges, currently the university has 8 locations, 2 locations in Phnom Penh and 6 locations in the provinces, including Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom. Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Kampot provinces, while more than 30,000 graduates and nearly 20,000 current students, this number is increasing every year.
The University has signed memorandums of study and research with more than 500 foreign universities and public and private institutions to find places for internships and internships, and has worked to improve quality through a number of measures, such as the addition of physical materials. .
Recently, the university decided to pay twice the monthly salary for staff and professors, and added an additional 70 LCD projectors to study and research. The university always pays attention to promote research through conferences and seminars.
