Ministry of Social Affairs, UNICEF and World Health Organization Jointly Hold Regional Conference to End Violence Against Children in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, in collaboration with UNICEF and the World Health Organization, has organized a regional conference on the implementation of seven INSPIRE strategies to end violence against children in Cambodia.
The Regional Conference on the Implementation of the INSPIRE Strategy was held at the Cambodia Hotel for three days from October 30 to November 1, 2018, with the aim of introducing and presenting the INSPIRE Strategy and the factors to be considered. And implementation to national stakeholders in countries to support the integration of the seven strategies of the INSPIRE into the national child protection program.
In addition, the conference was organized to support participants in identifying opportunities to expand prevention and response to violence against children in countries at the regional level in order to achieve sustainable development goals.
Regional Conferences Towards the Implementation of Seven INSPIRE Strategies to End Violence against Children with the participation of national and international guests, representatives of ministries, diplomatic missions, UN agencies, NGOs, national and international organizations in Cambodia and from 20 countries. More.
On that occasion, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has made progress in its efforts to address violence against children in a sustainable manner and the ASEAN Action Plan 2015 on the Elimination of Violence against Children.
"Based on past efforts, Cambodia has become one of the leading ASEAN countries in conducting a scientific study of the situation of violence against children to determine the extent, scope and provision of specific evidence of violence," he said. On children, both sexually, physically and mentally, that children have experienced and are facing.
Minister Vong Soth added that the action plan is in line with the goals and objectives of the Global Movement to End Violence against Children, the Sustainable Development Goals and the Global Partnership, the seven strategies for ending violence against children, the response to ASEAN and Cambodia. For violence against children.
In addition, this action plan has strategies and directions in line with the relevant strategic plans of the Royal Government, especially the National Strategic Development Plan, which has been implemented in the field of children in the systematic protection of children.
It should be noted that the seven INSPIRE strategies are: first, the implementation and enforcement of laws, second, standards and values, third, a safe environment, and fourth, parental and child support providers. Strengthening income and economy, the sixth is response and support services, and the seventh is education and life skills. Senior Minister Kun Kim Continues to Distribute Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Donation of Winter Coats to the Armed Forces at the 4th Battlefield of the 5th Army Zone
