Five nuclear powers refuse to sign Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (Video inside) (Moscow): The five permanent members of the UN Security Council, Russia, Britain, China, the United States and France, issued a joint statement on Monday. This is by refusing to sign the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Monday, October 29, 2018.
According to the statement, the five powers noted that the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT) adopted during the UN General Assembly on July 7, 2017 failed to resolve the issue. Major nuclear weapons as well as anti-nuclear issues could undermine the Non-Proliferation Treaty. The Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty has not yet been ratified by major powers.
