Chan Sophal, an independent economist, sees the influx of yuan as a positive sign in boosting the Cambodian economy.
He added that for the economic sector in Cambodia, the payment of the yuan is not a loss, but a benefit to the Cambodian economy to facilitate the exchange of currency in other businesses.
Please be informed that Mr. Sum Sansith, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, recently expressed his support for the use of the yuan in Cambodia through the banking system to facilitate bilateral trade, investment and tourism more effectively.
The announcement of support for the renminbi payment in Cambodia was made at a forum on the renminbi in Cambodia organized by the Bank of China Phnom Penh Branch (BOC).
The forum aims to present and discuss the use of the yuan in ASEAN and Cambodia, as well as the benefits of the yuan to the economy in line with the policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the growing economic and financial relationship between China and Cambodia.
Mr. Sum Sannisit emphasized that in the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has allowed two Chinese banks to be the yuan clearing bank, BOC Bank, ICBC Bank and 13 other commercial banks in Cambodia to operate the yuan.
Through this, investors, traders and recipients in yuan, can pay, borrow and deposit in yuan in the banking system, which allows the National Bank of Cambodia to better manage the circulation of the yuan and contribute to the growth of trade and investment. And tourism from China. Mr. Chan Sophal
