Through this, investors, traders and recipients in yuan, can pay, borrow and deposit in yuan in the banking system, which allows the National Bank of Cambodia to better manage the circulation of the yuan and contribute to the growth of trade and investment. And tourism from China.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, bilateral trade between Cambodia and China in 2017 reached $ 4.8 billion, of which exports from Cambodia amounted to $ 830 million and imports to Cambodia amounted to $ 3.9 billion. As of April 2018, Chinese investment in Cambodia totaled about 17 billion US dollars, the country that invested the most in Cambodia.
