In addition, the joint statement reflected the escalation of extremism and violence, which continue to pose a serious threat to international peace and security. All countries can eliminate this negative trend through sustainable and comprehensive cooperation among political parties and governments.
At the 31st meeting of the ICAPP Standing Committee, the Standing Committee reviewed the ICAPP Activity Report for two years since the ninth General Assembly in Kuala Lumpur. In particular, the Standing Committee commended Cambodia for its efforts to reach a partnership agreement between the Cultural Council (ACC) and UNESCO.
According to Khuon Sodary, the agreement has made ICAPP a partner of UNESCO, and this is a major step forward in establishing ICAPP's values and role in the international arena. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Honorary Chairman of ACC, was also congratulated for this noble achievement. Spokesman Net Pheaktra: In this new mandate, the Ministry of Environment focuses on modern administration to meet the sacred aspirations of the Cambodian people.
