Ruling party spokesman considers civil society officials' criticism of the appointment of court officials to be a clear insult to the King's power (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ruling party spokesman Sok Isan October 28, 2018, reacted to the criticism of senior investigator of the Adhoc Association (ADHOC), Mr. Son Sen Karuna, who criticized the transfer and appointment of officials in the judiciary.
The ruling party spokesman called the criticism of the appointment and replacement of prosecutors and prosecutors of the Supreme Council of the Judiciary of civil society officials a clear insult to the King's power.
Mr. Sok Isan said: "Recently, the Supreme Council of the Magistracy has decided to retire and appoint some court officials. "Based on this decision, some people in civil society organizations say that the decision to retire and appoint court officials is not transparent because they do not know, which leads to some doubts."
"The decision of the Supreme Council of the Judiciary was made in a meeting under the supreme presidency of the King, the President of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy. Why is there no transparency? "Such an insult is a clear insult to the King's power."
The ruling party spokesman's reaction came after Son Senkaruna, a senior ADHOC investigator, expressed concern about the effectiveness of law enforcement and doubts about the transfer and promotion of court officials. Recently.
Mr. Sung Senkaruna observed that in the past, the prosecution did not help advocates, especially human rights activists, environmental activists and land activists. He wants to see prosecutors play an active role in protecting those who have a conscience who are sick of social work. This is according to the broadcast of Radio Free Asia.
