During their visit to China, officials from the Ministry of Information and a group of Cambodian journalists were invited to visit to explore the potential of transport, trade, industry and development in cities bordering Vietnam.
Beijing is bordered by the South China Sea, making it easy to transport goods from China to Cambodia and other ASEAN member countries, as well as from Cambodia to ASEAN to China. Not only that, through this port is also a place to help transfer goods from Cambodia from ASEAN to countries in Europe and other countries.
The portfolio states that the port was originally built not to serve commercial purposes, but to serve as a port of departure in sea transport to support Vietnam in the war against The US invasion, or historically known as the Guangxi Plan "3 · 22".
Currently, the port is being developed continuously to serve trade. According to Su Yuanhui, the port currently covers an area of 17 square kilometers and can accommodate 200,000-tonne ships with a depth of 90 kilometers. The port is also expanding its capacity to accommodate up to 400,000-ton cargo ships.
In addition to a large port for transporting goods, there is also an economic and technical zone in Beijing, which has a number of factories operating power plants, coal, steel, copper, metals and soybean oil. Those companies have investors from Britain, America, India, South Korea, Japan ....
Cambodian officials and journalists have shown great interest in the development of the city of Fujian, as the province has the same geographical location as Sihanoukville. They want to see Sihanoukville use Cambodia's coastal land as a potential for trade, industry and transportation like in this city.
Chuon Chan Phearun, an official from the Ministry of Information and led a Cambodian delegation to visit China, said, "Currently, Cambodia's port is in the development stage with the participation of Japan. We hope to be able to bring good technology and good management of this port to develop the port in Cambodia.
Prak Vanda, a reporter from BTV, said: "What I saw was the connection between the port of Fangjingkang and the port of Cambodia. "I hope that the port of Sihanoukville and the port of Kampot in Cambodia will grow in terms of shipping, as our port and the port of Fangjing have had a good relationship in shipping since the 1990s."
Van Saray, Deputy Editor-in-Chief of Fresh News, expressed his admiration and interest in China's development plan for the coastal region to become a high potential area for the Chinese economy through the use of marine resources. He expressed the hope that by promoting the benefits of urban development, it will become a mirror for Cambodians to consider and accept the current development in Sihanoukville.
Mr. Van Saray emphasized, "Sihanoukville Port and Fangjingkang Port are both seaports, and Fangjingkang Port by finding investors to this area is getting good results. "I hope that through the promotion of the Chinese port, Cambodians will become more aware of the importance of port development and will be more supportive of the development of Sihanoukville."
It should be noted that Beijing has a coastline of 530 km and a border of 230 km, and is the only city connected to ASEAN countries by sea, land and river.
Due to the favorable nature of the sea area of thousands of square kilometers, the city of Beijing is connected to seven countries by sea. As an international port, the city will have a new future of industrial port development and transportation modernization.
