It's not until the story breaks! Crime Checkpoint Conspiracy to Take Money from Timber Traders in Stung Treng Province
(Stung Treng): Two swollen Camry cars were intercepted by the traffic police at the checkpoint on the new National Road 9 in Sralao village, Anlong Chrey commune, Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province at 08:45 pm during the day. October 25, 2018.
During the crackdown, it was reported that three luxury timber trucks of the Camry type were smuggling timber from Preah Vihear province to the target market through Stung Treng province when they reached the checkpoint. During the inspection, only two vehicles were detained by the traffic police force, while the other vehicle broke through the inspection target and proceeded safely.
While the police were cracking down on the timber trucks, a woman who claimed to be the owner of the timber came forward and explained that she should ask the authorities to release her timber because she had already paid for running the road at the checkpoint. They will transport these timber.
In relation to the above case, the traffic police force there said that it was following the role and order of Mr. Ot Sivutha, Deputy Commissioner for Traffic Planning, without affecting the money, taking bribes and oppressing the people. For this, the owner of the tree paid money to the police, who should be responsible.
In front of the police, the owner of the tree mentioned and recorded the names of some of the people at the target who took his money, Mr. Oeur Kimheng, Chief Prey, Mr. Chamnan, a police officer at the provincial police commission. (Not known at any office).
It should be noted that the joint force to monitor the crime there is a professional force of the Forestry Administration as the Chief of the Provincial Police, the military and the military, and also the land traffic police, a total of about 20 people in the target. Each.
Currently, the above two vehicles have been professionally stored at the Forestry Administration in Stung Treng Province for legal proceedings.
