A thief who stole people's property was greeted by the owner with one hand and one foot until he died
(Phnom Penh): A suspect who stole people's property in the early morning was greeted by the owner and the people of Krabouch, one hand and one foot, and handed over to the authorities for legal action.
This incident happened on the morning of October 26, 2018 around a rented house in group 2, Sre Chomrov village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sao Sarith, Deputy Chief of Post Choam Chao 2, said that the suspect was named Cham Ratha, 23 years old, unspecified occupation, currently living in a rented room in Russey Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, his hometown is in Chung Ruk Village, Chung Ruk Commune, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province.
Mr. Sao Sarith continued that before the incident, the house around the house with many rooms was quiet, as the workers went to work immediately, suddenly saw the suspect from the workers' rented room and called to stop the suspect. He refused to stop and ran away, only to be shouted at by the people for help, and only as thieves did they beat each other with one hand and one foot and handed over to the authorities.
The suspect is currently being held at the Chaom Chao 2 police station for further questioning, but due to the seriousness of his injuries, the suspect died.
The Minister of Labor encourages all public and private parties to follow the five recommendations to maintain competition in the textile sector.
(Phnom Penh): Speaking at the National Job and Productivity Fair 2018 on October 27, 2018 at the Koh Pich Exhibition Hall, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, encouraged all public-private parties to follow the five recommendations to continue Maintain competition in the textile, garment and footwear sectors.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that in order to maintain competitiveness, Cambodia must strive to successfully implement the national policies that have been set out in the past, especially the national policy on industrial development, national policy on employment and employment and policy. National Technical and Vocational Education and Training aims to become a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Minister Ith Sam Heng encouraged and requested the participation of all parties:
1. At the national level, the first important task is to create a culture of productivity and learning and to enhance the enduring capacity of the Cambodian people.
2. At the sector level, employers' associations and chambers of commerce play an important role in working together to improve the efficiency of the supply chain, to adopt good standards and practices, and to provide training to improve specific workforce skills in each sector. ⁇.
3: At the enterprise-institution level, each company is a leader in initiating to capture a flexible, fast and consistent mindset, innovate and invest in technology to compete more effectively.
4: At the level of workers, each must adhere to the attitude and mindset to continue to improve and expand skills to be flexible, responsive to rapid technological changes and changes from one employer to another. One life to one career, many employers in the working life in the current job market.
5. Unions also play an important role in helping workers acquire new and higher skills and maintain a harmonious professional relationship to contribute to the productivity of the business.
