Police crack down on money laundering case from Wing agency in Kampong Cham province, cracked down on 6 suspects, the suspect confessed that he had acted almost 10 times
(Phnom Penh-Kampong Cham): Case of impersonating a WING agent working at the head office and calling to swindle money from Wing agents in those provinces, now the criminal police force has cracked down on 6 suspects on October 26, 2012 This 2018, while the suspects confessed that they had already acted almost 10 times.
The operation to hunt down the swindlers was carried out by the Criminal Planning Force of Kampong Cham Provincial Police in collaboration with the Criminal Police Department and the Security Department of the Ministry of Interior under the coordination of the Prosecutor's Office.
Brigadier General Heng Vuthy, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Police Planning of Kampong Cham Provincial Police, told Fresh News that after receiving a complaint from the victim, Major General Em Kosal, the provincial police commissioner, assigned him to lead a specialized force. The investigation and research continued until they cracked down on a group of six suspects.
The suspect is currently being handed over to the Kampong Cham Provincial Police by the Criminal Police Department to build a case to be sent to court for sentencing. An international sports event will be held in Bokor Mountain at the end of October, with 32 Asia-Europe School athletes participating.
(Phnom Penh): Asia Europe University will send 32 athletes, including 6 professional athletes, to compete in the 5th International Half Marathon on Bokor Mountain, Kampot Province on October 29, 2018. Coming to contribute to fundraising for Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Speaking during the training at the National Stadium on October 25, Mr. Pov Hok, Sports Coach of Asia-Europe University, said that Asia-Europe University has trained its athletes to strengthen themselves. Well before you compete for a medal in this international event.
The coach thanked Mr. Duong Leang, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Asia Europe University for giving many staff and athletes the opportunity to participate in the International Half Marathon on Bokor Mountain. Raised by Thansur Bokor Resort to help raise funds for Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Pov Hok added that out of the 32 athletes, 6 were professional athletes at the club, including Ma Viro, Sat Udom, Phan Sophuth, Van Pheara, Heng Meng Chou and Bou Samnang, who had won. In the past.
He added that setting a good time record is a good and enjoyable thing, regardless of the overall result, and he hopes that all athletes will do their best to win global honors. Asia Europe High School.
Please note that there are up to 4 disciplines: 21 km, 10 km, 5 km and 3 km family recreation, which focuses on fundraising for donations to Kantha Bopha Hospital. . Plowing touches a ton of tons, causing an explosion and breaking the wheel while the owner was injured in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): A tractor wheel was damaged and the driver was injured in the case of plowing against Minton, causing an explosion at 11:00 on October 26, 2018 at the forest west of Wat Chi One kilometer in Chi Ork village, Romney commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
Colonel Say Det, Rovieng District Police Inspector, said that before the incident, the victim was plowing while plowing, which may have penetrated deep into the ground, causing a landmine to explode. The wheels were damaged and the driver was injured, but not seriously.
According to the district inspector, the victim was Vik Salim, 55, a resident of Randas village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balang district, Kampong Thom province. He added that the land where the mine exploded was plowed every year and had already exploded once last year, a total of two times.
Residents in the area said that the land where the mine exploded was never cleared by the CMAC unit, and that they were very concerned for their safety. Mr. Leang Nypi, head of the Preah Vihear Mine Action Team, said that he would report to the upper level to ask the upper level to clear mines there for the people this dry season.
Amnesty International: More than 130,000 people are waiting for justice in Turkey
In its report entitled "Non-Return Clearance? There is no solution for the public sector workers who have been fired by the current government, ”the international organization said, adding that thousands of doctors, police, teachers and civil servants were fired because But allegations of involvement in terrorist groups have not yet been resolved or settled.
The commission in charge of reviewing the eviction decision did not fulfill its role of compliance with international standards, as the whole process was a disgrace to the Turkish justice system.
It should be noted that such dismissal proceedings and the lack of appeal proceedings also threaten the right to a fair trial in the civil proceedings enshrined in Article 6 (1) of the Convention. Europe on Human Rights and Articles 14 and 15 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights (ICCPR).
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for October 26, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 5,194 vehicles and found 579 vehicles violating the law (82% motorcycles), 211 education vehicles and 368 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,812 helmets and goggles were inspected on October 26, 142 education helmets were inspected and 1,195 vehicles were fined.
Ministry of Tourism and Asia-Europe University continue to spread knowledge about tourism and clean city to many students-trainees
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and Asia-Europe University on October 26, 2018, held a seminar on public awareness about tourism and clean cities for students and trainees, 5th generation national tour guides and regional tour guides. Phnom Penh, 18-19 generation at Asia Europe University to further strengthen Buddhism in tourism.
The workshop was attended by Mr. Chuon Chey Satya, Director of the Department of Local Tourism Promotion and Public Awareness, and Mr. Saing Chanthou, Associate Dean, Faculty of Business and Tourism Management, Asia-Europe University.
Mr. Chuon Chey Satya said that Cambodia has great potential for the development of tourism based on cultural and natural resources, national unity, political stability, security and complete security. The Royal Government of Cambodia is firmly committed to continuing to actively promote the growth of tourism in order to contribute to strengthening the national economy.
He said that the tourism sector is a priority sector that has been identified in the Rectangular Strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia as green gold, providing job opportunities, income, improve living standards and reduce poverty to the people of Cambodia contribute to growth. Gross domestic product (GDP) and balance trade.
Not only that, tourism has contributed to the preservation, protection and preservation of cultural heritage, history and natural resources, as well as enhanced national prestige on the international stage, expanding friendship, solidarity and good cooperation with countries around the world.
Mr. Saing Chanthou stated that although tourism is one of the fastest growing sectors in Cambodia, it will not be able to benefit Cambodia without public participation from the people and From all stakeholders.
According to Mr. Saing Chanthou, Asia Europe University fully supports the organization of this important workshop and he strongly hopes that the students and trainees of the 5th generation National Tour Guide and 18th Generation Phnom Penh Tour Guide All 19 will get more new knowledge from skilled and experienced speakers from the Ministry of Tourism.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requested the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction to instruct all Capital-Provincial Departments of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs to transfer their services. OWSO, Phnom Penh.
Letter from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stating that this is in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 18 dated February 08, 2017 and Joint Proclamation No. 648 MEF.PrK dated July 7, 2017 of Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Ministry of Economy and Finance.
At the same time, the Ministry of Interior also requested the cooperation of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction to organize technical training on the provision of these services to relevant officials of the OWSO during November 2018.
The following is a letter from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara: Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inaugurates a swimming pool and swimming pool rehabilitation site
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on the afternoon of October 26, 2018, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the renovation and reconstruction of the swimming pool at the National Olympic Stadium of Cambodia. The ceremony was also attended by the leaders of the Ministry and many government officials.
The swimming pool and swimming pool in the National Olympic Stadium have the following history:
First, in 1965, the construction of the National Stadium and swimming pool began.
Second, 1967, the opening of the swimming pool and diving pool in the National Stadium, as well as hosting the first Ganefo Asian Games. The swimming pool in the National Stadium was the first international standard swimming pool in Cambodia at that time, measuring 21 meters by 50 meters, equal to 08 lines, and a diving pool with a pedal. For jumping 10 meters high.
Third: 1967-1973 Swimming pool and diving pool in the National Stadium is a championship competition for swimming, diving, water dance and water ball every year and also international friendly competitions. Swim between the national team of Cambodia and the national team of France. Cambodian diving and swimming are very popular in Southeast Asia because we have an international training ground in the National Stadium.
Fourth: 1975-1979 The swimming pool and diving pool in the National Stadium were damaged by the war during the Democratic Kampuchea era (Pol Pot regime).
Fifth, 1980-1990: Elder Hem Thon and Elder Phat Sam Un, along with a number of officials, rehabilitated and rehabilitated the swimming pool infrastructure.
Sixth: In 1990, the swimming pool and diving pool in the National Stadium were damaged by electricity and drainage system.
Seventh: From 1991 to 2000, the Australian Embassy sponsored generators and repaired some damaged equipment.
