Mukisaki Tuyi, Secretary-General of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development, summarized the background and issues of current global investment policy, especially changes in investment and trade trends and protectionist policies. Serious impact on foreign direct investment flows.
He said the purpose of the roundtable was to discuss solutions to attract more investment, which are key to achieving the SDGs, taking advantage of the Fourth Industrial Revolution for sustainable development and mitigation. Negative impact as a result of protectionist policies.
