(Beijing): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, said, "We can not cooperate in a situation where one hand cooperates and the other hand punishes or threatens. "Of course, only win-win cooperation can bring all countries together in harmony."
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said: "We can not cooperate in a situation where one hand cooperates and the other hand punishes or threatens. "Of course, only win-win cooperation can bring all countries together in harmony."
Through this Sieng San forum, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also highlighted three experiences that Cambodia went through to confirm the meeting, including:
Experience 1: Sometimes it is not possible to use military means alone to solve problems. That is, they can not take the war to end the war. If all parties remain steadfast in their demands for victory or defeat, the war will continue, no matter how small or large, in the form of rebellion or terrorism. Only when there is a win-win situation will the war end easily and we can have a win-win situation as long as there is mutual trust.
Experience 3: Based on the Cambodian experience, the relationship between peacekeeping operations and counter-terrorism. These two things sound unrelated. On the other hand, some people think that peacekeeping operations are useless and waste resources, while terrorism must be suppressed by military force.
At the same time, Samdech Pich Sena stated that without peacekeeping operations, there would be no political stability, and such a situation would create an opportunity for terrorists to use the country as a security base and attack other areas. Also.
