Phnom Penh International Airport CamControl Officer Inspects Quality and Safety of Food Products at Pochentong Market, No Prohibited Chemicals Found
(Phnom Penh): In order to improve the well-being of the people, on October 26, 2018, CamControl officials of Phnom Penh International Airport inspected the quality and safety of food products at Pochentong Market, Phnom Penh, and found no banned chemicals. It is 100% good.
The above quality inspection was led by Mr. Tith Sokhim, Mr. Chan Phea Hoeun, Mr. Chin Chhay Sopheary, Mr. Ton Bora and in collaboration with the laboratory staff of the General Department of CamControl and the mobile laboratory vehicle. , Department of Commerce Officer, Pochentong Market Commission.
On that occasion, CamControl officials also educated and disseminated information on food safety and serious health effects, as well as the legal challenges to traders who bring and sell all kinds of goods with no quality and no clear origin. .
CamControl officers sampled more than ten samples of food products, such as seafood, meatballs, patties, prahok, etc., for preliminary analysis for chemicals that are prohibited by law to harm the health of consumers and you. Consumption.
As a result, after a preliminary on-site analysis by mobile laboratory laboratory officials, no banned chemicals were found in the product. Officials also advise traders on how to store goods properly and understand the legal responsibilities of their food products on display.
Please be informed that in order to fulfill its core roles and responsibilities, the Ministry of Commerce has assigned professional officers of the General Department of CamControl to stand in operation at some of the main target markets in Phnom Penh, including: Central Market, Phsar Orussey, Olympic Market, Doeum Kor Market, Toul Tum Poung Market, Stung Meanchey Market, Champou One Market, Century Plaza Market, Chbar Ampov Market and Prek Eang Market.
