(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Piseth, Chief Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, this morning, October 26, 2018, held a trial of a military officer in connection with the shooting death of Kong Ravin, a 30-year-old male. And Son Vin, alias Srey Leak, a 25-year-old female, who did not die but suffered serious injuries, was adjourned until November 8, 2018.
During the hearing, the accused claimed that the gun he had fired was the legacy of his father, a military officer who had left it for personal use, without a permit.
According to the accused, he did not shoot the victim, but fired five shots before flying to the two victims in the car. The accused also asked the court to drop the charges because he did not shoot, it was different from the gun, it just spread.
However, the court stated during the hearing that the firearms could not have been aimed and exploded up to five bullets, meaning that the accused's claims did not seem to be in line with the facts and the answer given by the suspect. Court. In this case, the victim has demanded $ 50,000 in compensation from the accused.
It should also be reminded that a shooting incident occurred at 12:30 AM on February 26, 2018 in front of a rented house along Street 1974 in Phnom Penh Thmey Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok. The above defendant was driving a white RANGE ROVER. The two victims were injured and their relatives sent them to the hospital for treatment.
Two days after the incident, the accused confessed at the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command and was detained by the competent authorities to build a case to be sent to court for legal decision. The Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Agriculture cooperate with UNIDO to Promoting the development of trade and agriculture in Cambodia
(Geneva, Switzerland): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, received Mr. Li Yong, Secretary-General of the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) at the Mission. Permanent Representative of Cambodia to the World Trade Organization and International Trade and Economic Organizations in Geneva, Switzerland.
In this e-commerce work, the Minister also informed that he has already sought to meet with some e-commerce operators to study and help set up an ecosystem for this sector in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, praised UNIDO for working closely with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and requested that UNIDO meet more in promoting marine fisheries processing and aquaculture training not only for Not only the domestic market, but also refers to more exports.
The Minister of Agriculture also requested UNIDO to study and strengthen the sanitary and phytosanitary system on potential products for export, especially to some Chinese markets, such as rice, corn, mango and other crops that Cambodia has the capacity to produce but has not yet been able to import. Get out.
Mr. Ly Yong agreed on the proposals and initiatives that are all good points for promoting the development of trade and agriculture in Cambodia and accepted the two ministers' proposals and promised to continue cooperation with The two institutions to be more cohesive.
According to the summary of the draft budget of the Ministry of Economy 2019 of the Ministry of Economy, in managing public debt, the Royal Government always adheres to the following four key principles:
1: Must borrow a loan in an appropriate amount that the financial and economic situation can withstand.
2: Borrow only loans with high concessions or favorable terms
3. Borrow only for priority sectors to sustain sustainable growth and sectors to increase economic productivity or productivity.
4: Must use those loans with the highest transparency, accountability, efficiency, and efficiency.
According to the Ministry of Economy, the Royal Government has set the size of loans from development partners for 2019 at 1.4 billion SDR, based on the following key factors:
1: The size of development needs increases
2: The development project that will sign the concession loan agreement in 2019 is a public investment project in priority sectors (physical infrastructure and increasing economic productivity and production productivity) and which has been moving from previous years, but has a strategic nature to support To medium- and long-term sustainable economic growth,
3: High Concession Credit
5: Continue to provide high efficiency on project management and implementation. Overall, increasing the size of the loan will not create a debt burden for Cambodia, as as the economy grows, Cambodia's repayment capacity will be higher.
Indeed, the results of the debt sustainability analysis, based on the assumption of additional new loans for 2019 at 1.4 billion SDR, show that Cambodia's four key debt ratios are below all benchmark ratios.
In this regard, the new borrowing ceiling for 2019 at 1.4 billion SDR is to enable the Royal Government to sign loans for 25 out of a total of 32 projects that are fully qualified. Contains:
* 2 World Bank projects
* International Fund for Agricultural Development 1 project
* Japan 2 projects
* Korea 3 projects
* France 3 projects
In order to sustain the medium- and long-term growth of the economy, promoting competitiveness and economic productivity, including:
Power Sector: 500 kV transmission line project as the backbone for the national grid and sub-regional connection: Rural Power Transmission Expansion Project, Phase 7: Construction of 115 kV power transmission line from Suong district, Tbong Khmum province to Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province.
The project modernizes the transmission and distribution network of solar power applications for electricity connectivity with the aim of expanding the scope of electricity supply and lowering electricity prices in rural areas to help reduce the cost of rural people and cut- Reduce production costs in agriculture and handicrafts / rural industries.
Irrigation Sector: Prek Stung Keo Water Resources Development Project, Kampot Province, Phase 2: Agricultural Irrigation Improvement Project.
Physical Infrastructure Sector: Road Development Project from Samlot-Veal Veng to Koh Kong, Construction of National Road No. 71 (Tbong Khmum-Krouch Chhmar-Chamkar Leu), Construction of National Road No. 60, 116 km long and Mekong Bridge, Kratie, Stung Bot International Gate and Road Project Connect National Road 5, Step 2.
This project will improve National Road No. 5 South and Central Rural Road Improvement Project, Phase 3, River Port Development Project, Phase 1, Rural Infrastructure Development Program for Cambodia and other priority areas: projects in agriculture, health, Water supply, finance, vocational training and education.
