(Hong Kong) - Hong Kong government officials say the opening of the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macau bridge will bring many opportunities for development as well as bring tangible benefits to the three regions.
The 55-kilometer bridge spans the Pearl River Delta, connecting the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region with Zhuhai in mainland China and Macau Special Administrative Region. Construction cost more than $ 18 billion.
Many cross-border infrastructure projects between Hong Kong and mainland China, such as the Guangzhou-Shenzhen-Hong Kong Expressway, the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge and the Lian Thang Heng Yuan Wei border checkpoint, are expected to bring development opportunities. Come to this area.
"We all hope that after the bridge opens, it will definitely enhance our cooperation with mainland China and the United States," said Tam Yao Chung, former chairman of the Hong Kong Democratic Party for Development. Bring more benefits to the people.
Transportation is an important factor in the development of the Pearl River Delta because most of the people on both sides travel by land. In the past, they had to travel by sea. But now that the bridge has been built, it will greatly enhance future development.
Many experts hope that the bridge will promote the scientific and technological development, economy, finance and tourism of the Pearl River Delta, which connects Guangdong with Hong Kong and Macau, and make it a multi-industrial area. Sector.
