Phnom Penh Capital Administration Parade for Solidarity Monks at Wat in Sangkat Teuk Thal, Khan Sen Sok Receives More Than $ 250,000
(Phnom Penh): The Council and the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh Capital City have unanimously agreed to launch a Solidarity Kathina to pay homage to the monks who have been waiting for the rain for a quarter in the Buddha Seima Pagoda at Preah Barami Vong Pagoda Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok, receiving more than $ 250,000 to build a church and annex that are still under construction.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration officials confirmed that the Kathina Donation Parade to Wat Preah Barami Vong Borei Bilpost was fined $ 259,875 to build a church and a school complex that is still under construction.
According to the Royal Golden Gate Ceremony, published by the Buddhist Institute, Buddhists perform the Kathin ceremony in the belief in the Buddhist scriptures that the Kathina is more fruitful than all other alms. Due to this, it is noted that if a pagoda reaches the Kathin season and no one enters the Kathin, the pagoda is not equal to the pagoda that does not receive the Kathin.
According to the Buddha's teachings, a monk who can receive the Kathina mat only if he waits for three full months of rain does not enter the rainy season because he violates any discipline. The pagoda, which does not have monks waiting for the rain, can not receive alms from Buddhists.
SCG announces operating results for the third quarter and 9 months of 2018
(Phnom Penh): The operating results of SCG (SCG) for the third quarter and the first nine months of 2018 showed an increase in revenue, but profits fell due to higher prices. Raw materials and energy, global trade declines and asset losses.
SCG is well aware of the effects of trade wars and the uncertainties of the global economy and has set out six goals for a proactive plan, including expanding export opportunities in line with global market flows, managing spending. Energy The use of digital technology to increase production efficiency and reduce costs, develop high value-added products and services (HVA).
In addition, it is innovative in strengthening the efficiency of operating capital and reviewing its investment programs and investment expenditures in order to maintain the competitiveness of the company's business.
SCG ASEAN business results in the third quarter of 2018, excluding Thailand
This revenue includes sales through local operations of each ASEAN market and imports from Thailand.
SCG in Cambodia: In the Cambodian market, SCG's sales revenue for the third quarter of 2018 amounted to 400 billion riels ($ 98 million), an increase of 17%. Due to the high demand for cement and construction materials.
SCG has always considered the continued growth of the construction sector in Cambodia, so SCG has opened the first roofing consulting and solution service center in Phnom Penh.
This Roofing Consulting and Solving Service Center is a comprehensive service location for homeowners and construction project owners to start designing, selecting materials and finding builders.
Suitable for roofing through consultation with experts. In addition, SCG plans to expand the service to more major cities next year.
Moreover, SCG's construction search service, which was launched last quarter of this year, has successfully matched the first homeowners in Sihanoukville with the right qualified builders. This service is designed to make it easy for clients to find a builder by contacting SCG's contact office by phone: 095 999 500.
Mr. Roongrote said that SCG's operating results for the third quarter of 2018 and for the first nine months of 2018 showed an increase in revenue for all businesses due to the favorable situation for High market demand from the public and private sectors for cement products and construction materials from Thailand and in various foreign investment projects to balance market demand for chemicals and paper business.
Although profits fell due to higher raw material and energy prices, coupled with a slowdown in global trade and losses due to asset losses.
SCG is well aware of the impact of trade wars on the whole business and the uncertainty of the global economy, while at the same time recognizing the potential of new opportunities. Therefore, SCG has set out six directions of a progressive plan for this challenge that will be implemented at all levels to maintain as well as boost the viability of the business. These directions are as follows:
1. Expand export opportunities in line with the changing global market flows after the trade war. For example, exports to China and the United States while trade wars are raging.
In addition to a long-term plan aimed at strengthening its market base in Thailand, SCG is also focusing on the continuous expansion of its market base in other regions.
The first phase will focus on services in southern China, strengthening SCG as well as preparing to expand sourcing and e-commerce business to bring Thai products to the Chinese market.
2: Managing energy costs, for example, ensuring a large supply of coal with competitive prices has helped SCG reduce energy costs in the past nine months by up to $ 12 million. SCG plans) and promote the use of renewable energy in factories to reduce energy costs.
6: Review of investment projects and investment expenditures to focus on projects that can lead to business opportunities, energy reduction projects, for example, the development of floating solar farm farms for solar power generation in order to become As the first comprehensive solution provider in Thailand in 2019, providing services from design, installation and after-sales service to potential customers in both the public and private sectors.
