Two Ministers Ask UNDO Director General to Support Cambodia's Trade and Agriculture Promotion
(Switzerland): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and accompanying delegation on October 25, 2018 met with Mr. Liyong, Director General of UNIDO (UNIDO) in Phnom Penh. The Cambodian Permanent Mission to the World Trade Organization in Geneva, Switzerland.
To begin with, Minister Pan Sosak confirmed that the Ministry of Commerce is currently preparing a draft law on e-commerce and asked the organization to provide some support to speed up the process.
In addition, the Ministry of Commerce is promoting Country Trade Integration System (CTIS) and AIMS programs that can help find agricultural markets for Cambodian farmers and share information between buyers and producers.
The Minister requested UNIDO to consider the possibility of supporting the quality of the car assembly process within the ASEAN framework, to facilitate the access to funding from the Road and Belt Policy Framework through the AIIB China, and to provide support to Establish e-commerce system to help small and medium enterprises to connect Cambodian and international markets, especially China.
At the same time, with the growing number of foreign tourists in Cambodia, the Minister also asked UNIDO to support the management of food quality and safety on the streets in Cambodia, which many guests are interested and asked to help strengthen Ability to inspect the safety of cross-border products at all international ports.
Mr Liyong stated that UNIDO aims to strengthen the country's partnership program with Cambodia, focusing on capacity building, aquaculture development, investment promotion, modern agro-industrial parks linked to the agricultural production chain, and cooperation on supporting infrastructure. To the quality and standard of agricultural products (hygiene and phytosanitary) and to promote Cambodia's light trade to international markets.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Director General of the General Department of Taxation, confirmed on October 25, 2018 that the General Department of Taxation is studying the adjustment of property prices for the basis of taxation, stamping on the transfer of ownership and ownership of real estate. .
He said the revision was due to the fact that the property price list set by the government as a tax base has not been updated since its inception, as the discrepancy differs from the actual market value of the property.
