Street 60 meters in Siem Reap is named "Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street"
(Phnom Penh): The 60-meter road in Siem Reap from the corner of Kantha Bopha Hospital to the APSARA Authority is nicknamed "Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street". The naming comes after authorities requested the Siem Reap provincial administration.
According to the decision of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, the reason for naming this name is to repay the gratitude of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An in the cause of heritage.
Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street used to be called 60 meters by the general population in Siem Reap because it is 60 meters wide, but has not yet been officially determined. Recently, APSARA Authority submitted a request to the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, naming this street Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An.
It should be reminded that Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street was built in 2002 with the support of the French Agency (ADF). In 2006, APSARA Authority spent some money to build a red gravel road on both sides of the road and continue to build the road to the east 4 km beyond the roundabout to celebrate the Angkor Kyung Yu cultural event, which is a cooperation between two heritage sites: Angkor and Kyung Yu.
Later in 2010, APSARA Authority also built 9,679 meters from Tram Neak junction to Siem Reap Provincial Administrative Borey, now the headquarters of APSARA Authority.
So far, Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street has served the benefit of the people and tourists, both through and transporting goods for 16 years.
Good news! Get ready to take a job opportunity from PRASAC in the National Job and Productivity Fair 2018
(Phnom Penh): On October 27-28, 2018, PRASAC, the largest financial institution in Cambodia, will participate in the National Job and Productivity Fair 2018 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center at 8 o'clock. Morning to 8 pm to share experiences and provide job opportunities for students and candidates looking for work.
In this program, all candidates can apply and get career advice with PRASAC Recruitment Team immediately with the most intimacy. For more than 20 years, PRASAC has been recognized as an employer of choice for career development and quality of life of its employees.
As of September 2018, PRASAC has a total of more than 7,000 employees in various positions and skills operating across the country, like a big family that provides support, comfort and growth.
PRASAC provides all employees with important points such as job opportunities, stability and longevity, many benefits, capacity development of staff, evaluation based on work results and opportunities to contribute to society. PRASAC offers salaries, rewards and many benefits to attract, maintain and motivate competent employees.
These benefits include: base salary, role allowance, annual bonus, Khmer New Year allowance, Pchum Ben allowance, uniform loan, health insurance, hospital stay insurance, personal accident insurance, annual accommodation. Marriage leave, paternity leave, family vacation and more.
