The branch vice president and the professional team regularly visit the market in Phnom Penh to inform the market vendors about the health effects of consumers and to spread the word to the distributors about the use of chemicals. This is according to the instructions from the head of the delegation in charge of the General Department of CamControl and the head of the dry port branch at the end of Phnom Penh, including the request from the people.
Mr. Kong Vuthy urged all businesses not to add banned chemicals to vegetables, fruits, food and beverages, as those substances pose a high risk to the health of consumers, on the other hand, may face legal action and must be advertised. Continue to the owner of the distribution site to participate in the prevention together.
