(Kep): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, stated that the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants is a public administration institution that has the obligation to manage and ensure the provision of social security system with 6 staff members: Retirement, loss of professional qualifications, maternity, accident, work, death and dependents in accordance with the principles of good governance, transparency, efficiency and high responsibility.
Mr. Vong Soth highly appreciated the hard work of all members of the Board of Directors, management and staff of the NPC. All those who have performed their duties have achieved excellent results in terms of their roles and functions in providing social security services to the rights of the NCDD. And with the support of ministries, institutions, banks and development partners.
Mr. Vong Soth's speech was made at the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for the first nine months of 2018 and the five-year report of the National Social Security Fund for civil servants on behalf of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation as technical guardians Prepared on October 25, 2018.
Minister Vong Soth introduced the leadership at all levels and the staff of the NPC. All on performing work focusing on the following key points:
