Qin Chengiang, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China (CPC) at the university, confirmed that the Khmer language classes will be taught directly by professors from Cambodia and the university will send Chinese teachers to teach at universities in the country. Cambodia, which has its own cooperation as well.
Guangxi University was established in 1928 and is now 90 years old. The university has become one of the oldest universities in China and is also famous for its training.
This university offers a wide range of bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees in a variety of disciplines. The University Doctoral Degree trains in 17 subjects.
Guangxi University does not only train local students. The university also provides scholarships to about 120 students from ASEAN member countries per year to study at this university. In addition to scholarships, the school also offers tuition fees.
In order to promote education between Cambodia and China in accordance with the policy of relations between the Cambodian and Chinese governments, the University of Quang Ngai has cooperated with many Cambodian universities and also provided scholarships to many Cambodian students.
Currently, there are 70 Cambodian students studying at this university, of which 68 study on scholarships from the Chinese government and two pay tuition.
Cambodian students who have received scholarships to study at Guangxi University highlight the quality of education at this university, helping them to have a clear professional knowledge. They also see that studying at a university in China will help provide higher employment opportunities in the country after graduation, as China is now increasing investment in Cambodia.
Hang Chansambo, a Cambodian doctoral student at Guangxi University, said the school now has modern teaching facilities with high quality. He claimed that although the training here is not as strong as in the United States or Europe, the knowledge is not bad.
Another Cambodian student, 19-year-old Tang Suhuang, who recently graduated from the university, also praised the quality of education at the university. In addition, both Cambodian students are optimistic that studying in China will give them higher job opportunities in Cambodia, as many Chinese companies are now doing business in Cambodia.
Please note that in addition to the training, the school has provided suitable accommodation for foreign students and Chinese students from far away.
