Minister of Education urges Sisowath School Board to strengthen environmental clean-up on campus to improve aesthetics (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, on the afternoon of October 24, 2018 This has prompted the board, executive committee and management of Sisowath Quay to strengthen waste management on campus to enhance aesthetics and improve the environment.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron made the remarks when he announced the composition of the Board of Directors, Executive Committee and Management of Preah Sisowath High School and inspected the teaching and learning of students in the new generation of high school. Preah Sisowath, with the participation of a large number of leaders of the Ministry of Education to learn about the development of teaching and learning in the 21st century and to develop other schools across the country.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that for the past five years, the Ministry of Education has increased the budget to strengthen each school across the country, especially to strengthen the efficiency and effectiveness of leadership and management in terms of progress. Improve the quality of education by creating student learning outcomes.
The minister stated: "The first task is to help clean the school, so since the day of the meeting, I turned through the window to see a lot of garbage in the back, so I asked them to clean, so first I help clean the environment, I do not interfere. Hand in technical work, but I help develop the school further.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron added that it is necessary to check how to make the school clean first and after the announcement of the board, he will ask the school management to inspect the classroom to do. However, to make the students' classrooms comfortable and clean, and where they can learn, they should be repaired, corrected and disciplined so that all students can participate in the maintenance of school facilities.
BEIJING, Oct. 23 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping attended the inauguration ceremony of the Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge in Zhuhai, Guangdong Province, China on Friday. . To date, the "Great Engineering", which has been under construction for 15 years and has a total length of 55 km, has been officially launched.
The Hong Kong-Zhuhai-Macau Bridge is the world's longest and most difficult cross-sea traffic project, jointly built by Guangdong Province, the first Hong Kong-Macao Special Administrative Region. The bridge is the most important transportation infrastructure in Dawan, Guangdong, Hong Kong and Macau. This is the first time that a land connection between Zhuhai and Macau and Hong Kong has been achieved.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) has extended its membership for another three years to nine major companies. This is according to the press release on "Renewal Membership to the Securities Company" of the Cambodia Securities Exchange on October 24, 2018.
These companies meet the qualification requirements of the CSX Membership Rules, which include adequate IT equipment and systems and human resources. The new membership is valid for three years from October 20, 2018. The Colombian army came to Cambodia to learn how to use demining equipment in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): A delegation of nine Colombian demining engineers came to study demining skills in Cambodia from the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC).
During a meeting with a delegation from the Colombian Mine Action Engineering Corps, Heng Ratana, Director General of CMAC, said that in addition to learning the skills of using demining equipment, they also learned about the unit's demining activities. CMAC.
He said the Colombian army's visit lasted five days and was supported by the Japanese government, and the Japanese government decided to provide seven demining equipment to the Colombian government, with the CMAC unit providing support for the training.
During the visit, the trainees learned about the activities of Hitmin dogs, inspected demining operations using machines at the minefield, and visited the CMAC Peace Museum in Siem Reap.
Please be informed that CMAC has always cooperated with many countries, not less than 15 countries, in training demining activities for hundreds of foreign trainees.
Labor Minister: In 2019, Cambodia will send 5,000 workers for the first time to work in Kuwait
During the talks held on October 24, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor, the Heads of the Ministry of Labor of Cambodia and Kuwait agreed to promote closer cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training, and Kuwaiti investors Willing to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia as well.
"Cambodia will organize its first 5,000 qualified men to work in Kuwait, and this workforce will be in all areas of service, industry and agriculture," he said.
Minister Ith Sam Heng said that if the situation in Kuwait improves in line with what Cambodian workers have accepted, good working conditions and decent wages, the Royal Government of Cambodia will push for more repatriation.
Regarding the conditions for recruiting workers to work in a country in the Middle East, the Minister also stated that there must be prior training to know the situation of the country, recognize the culture and skills, especially the conditions of living there. .
He stressed that these are in line with the "Open to the Middle East" policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister.
