According to the municipal forensic examination and Dr. Nong Sovannaroth, the victim died of a heart attack and the body was handed over to his family for a traditional ceremony in his hometown.
(Preah Vihear): An elderly man died after being sent to the hospital, while five others suffered severe symptoms after being poisoned after eating mushrooms together. This incident happened on the evening of October 23, 2018 at Romchek village, Srayong commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province.
On the afternoon of October 24, 2018, Lieutenant Colonel Lahn Ly Siv Leng, Kulen District Police Inspector, said that before the incident, the victim's son had removed the mushrooms from the forest and brought them to his mother to eat. Each. After eating for an hour, the victims, a father and son, who were mushroom pickers, had the most toxic symptoms, including salivation, vomiting and diarrhea.
Seeing this, the two victims were sent to the Kulen District Health Center for treatment, but unfortunately, the victim, the father with the most severe poisoning, died. Meanwhile, the son was sent to the 16th of January Referral Hospital in Preah Vihear province, and the mother and three other children were slightly poisoned.
