(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sok Samnang, Representative of "Kuy Siv Chheng" Company, which is the contractor for cleaning Kampong Chhnang City, urged Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance to intervene after Kampong Chhnang City Hall issued an administrative letter recognizing the contractor for cleaning. Kampong Chhnang Thmey while his company contract has not expired.
Kampong Chhnang City Hall letter dated 19 February 2018, signed by Mr. Yin Saven, Governor of Kampong Chhnang City, states: "Sok Sambath, male, born on 31 January 2018 in Prey Krol Village, Prey Moul Commune, Rolea Bier District. "Kampong Chhnang province is actually a contractor to clean the city of Kampong Chhnang from the administration of Kampong Chhnang for 2 years from January 1, 2018 to December 30, 2019."
Regarding this issue, Mr. Mak Solim, Deputy Director of Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration in charge of Sanitation Services, clarified that the issuance of the letter to Sok Sambath was only to confirm his business and to easily borrow money from the bank to do business. It is a letter to give Sok Sambath the right to be involved in the case of the garbage collection company in the city because the two parties have been suing for a long time.
He pointed out that the owner of "Kuy Siv Chheng" had been convicted of personal offenses, so in order to find a contractor, the city hall had to find a new one to work temporarily. He said that his duties were carried out in accordance with the Royal Government's Sub-Decree No. 113 on Urban Solid Waste Management only, and in early 2019, the City Hall will organize a bid to find more municipal cleaners.
Another letter from Kampong Chhnang Municipality after 4 days, dated February 23, 2018, with the note of the provincial governor confirming to review the unanimous procedure in principle to Mr. Heng Pito, Director of Administration and Director of the Department of Economy and Finance. The provincial hall stamped on March 2, 2018, the request of the mayor to cancel the sanitary business license of Kampong Chhnang city of "Kuy Siv Chheng" which is valid for 2 years.
Separately, Mr. Van Ki Antro, the husband of "Kuy Siv Chheng", the owner of a garbage collection company in the city, which has a license from the provincial authorities and the Department of Economy and Finance in the past, said that his wife was guilty. Who can replace him to get the job done.
Due to this irregularity due to the recognition of the new contractor from the City Hall, while another company has not yet terminated the contract, Mr. Van Ki-An had requested that the intervention was still ineffective, so his company decided to request the intervention of Mr. Minister of Economy. He said that the city hall recognized the new company, but the ministry had just issued a letter requesting the cancellation, leaving him without work for more than five months.
