(China): Video and live broadcasts are helping beekeepers in northwest China sell honey and other related products online, which is helping to reduce poverty in the region. Successfully.
Two years ago, under the leadership of a bee business, beekeepers in Longnan County started selling honey online, which gave them a chance to escape poverty.
"I am raising bees from the east because they provide a thicker honey than regular bees and are more nutritious," said Se Pingse, a member of the Tianlong bee business.
These products used to be sold to older customers. But now customers born in the 80s and 90s are also becoming big buyers as they spend more time watching online videos, live streaming and playing mobile games.
"The younger generation is more inclined to the new media, which has a wide range of coverage," said Qin Shingfu, general manager of Sunriver. We want to improve our brand reputation through this one pattern. ”
