(Switzerland): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has brought peace to the motherland to this day, has announced the protection of the monarchy from being lost. Samdech Techo even used harsh words that if anyone wants to destroy the monarchy in Cambodia, they must first skip Samdech's body.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on the occasion of Samdech meeting with more than 900 Cambodian people living in Europe in Switzerland on the evening of October 23, 2018, which is the 27th anniversary of the agreement. Paris.
Samdech Techo said: "Because he used to live under the monarchy and also because he used to go into the forest at the call of the king, who was then the head of state, but he was the king in the monarchy. I must contribute to the re-establishment of this monarchy. I have said over and over again that if you want to destroy the throne, if you want to destroy the monarchy, you have to go past Hun Sen's body.
Prime Minister Hun Sen reacted to some individuals who were dissatisfied with the monarchy because they criticized the monarchy for not being as developed as the Republic. But around this point, Samdech asked those people to look at Belgium with kings and England, etc., where these monarchies are still highly developed.
Samdech considered the critics of the monarchy to be the same group that overthrew the monarchy in the past and a group that betrayed the king and joined other countries.
Samdech said, "He was the one who ousted our king, and I am the one who came back. I have elected the king twice, the first time, the second father, the current king, as a member of the Throne Council." So I did my duty as a Cambodian, but not the son of a traitor to the king, you know, the son of a traitor to the king.
The son of the traitor to whom the king refers is likely to be none other than Sam Rainsy, the son of Sam Sary, an elite who was condemned by the former king as a traitor during the period. Sangkum Reastr Niyum.
According to documents from the Khmer Documentation Association, during 1956, Sam Sary conspired with the United States to overthrow the Sangkum Reastr Niyum regime of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk. Mr. Mr. Sam Sary's ploy to seize power made the head of state, Prince Norodom Sihanouk, know in advance and announced the removal of all positions and ranks.
Angered by the loss of his position and title, Sam Sary founded a newspaper called "People" in the Khmer-French language, strongly criticizing the leadership of Prince Norodom Sihanouk. This newspaper was first published on December 30, 1958.
By 1959, Sam Sary had formed a party called the "Khmer Democratic Assembly", which proved right-wing and fiercely opposed to the regime of Norodom Sihanouk, and conspired with insurgents along the Cambodian-Thai border. To overthrow the Sangkum Reastr Niyum regime. Sam Sary's conspiracy led to the arrest of the National Assembly and he fled to South Vietnam forever.
Sam Sary's betrayal forced his family, including his wife, father and children, to resign and force them to resign. Ms. NM, after being imprisoned for a while, was released, but it was not until 1965 that her family was allowed to leave Cambodia.
While commemorating the traitor, King Techo Hun Sen, who became his father-in-law during his visit to North Korea, also expressed anger at those who insulted the current King. Also. Samdech believes that these people are not in the country, mostly abroad, and those who insulted the king in the country in the past have also been punished according to the law.
