(Phnom Penh): On October 24, 2018, three provincial councils, Kampot, Stung Treng and Pailin, opened a two-day training course for provincial councilors and their officials on two lessons: 1- Principles Universalization of good governance; and 2- Orientation to the newly elected council.
The training on both lessons was conducted with the technical and financial support of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils in order to raise the awareness of the members of the Provincial Council and relevant officials about the theory, policy, legal documents and reflect on the actual work.
The training course in Kampot province was chaired by Mr. Ung Meng Hour, Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council and Mr. Yim Sokhom, Permanent Vice President of the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils. The trainers from the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils are Mr. Sok Yat, Member of Kampong Speu Provincial Council and Mr. Heng Ser, Member of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Council.
The training course in Stung Treng was organized under the chairmanship of Mr. Chhim Rachana, Chairman of Stung Treng Provincial Council and coordinated by the trainers from the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, Mr. Em Det, Member of Tbong Khmum Council and Mrs. Sok Chanthou, Member of Kampong Thom Provincial Council.
The training course in Pailin was chaired by Mr. Ley Chan Chhay, Chairman of Pailin Provincial Council and coordinated by the trainers from the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, Mr. Suon Sothy, Member of Banteay Meanchey Council and Mr. A Sarum, Member of Battambang Council.
After more than 80 deaths and illnesses in Sambo district, more than 700 wineries across Kratie province have been temporarily suspended.
(Kratie): More than 700 unlicensed wine handicrafts throughout Kratie province have been suspended by the Department of Industry and Handicrafts in collaboration with the relevant authorities out of a total of 761 locations throughout Kratie province. This is according to the director of the Department of Industry and Handicraft of Kratie Province, Mr. Ny Chhon told Fresh News this morning, October 24, 2018.
Mr. Ny Chhon confirmed that the suspension of these handicrafts business based on the cause of wine poisoning and illness in Sambo district, Kratie province a few days ago, but as of this morning, his department and relevant authorities More than 400 businesses have been suspended and the campaign will continue.
However, the director of the department also claimed that the time to issue the permit to reopen has not been set, that is, unless the owners of these handicrafts are recognized and agreed with the technical standards of the department. Pre-made.
Nichon also said that only a handful of the 761 handicrafts were recognized and licensed, and that the suspension was to prevent a recurrence.
It should be noted that the case of alcohol poisoning in Boeung Char commune, Sambo district, Kratie province and Koh Khnhe commune a few days ago caused 5 people to die and 78 others to fall ill. Koch Sokheng, a 31-year-old winery owner, was also remanded in custody by Kratie Provincial Court on charges of "involuntary manslaughter."
Regarding the suspension of the above handicrafts, the Ministry of Health has fully supported the goal of protecting the health of the people and their lives.
Speaking to Fresh News this morning, October 24, 2018, Dr. Ly Sovann, spokesman for the Ministry of Health, said that in addition to supporting the action, but the Ministry also insists on the inspection of all shipments of alcohol sold in Villages and sales must be properly tested before being allowed to resume operation.
Mr. Ly Sovann also stated that the Ministry of Health also asked the relevant authorities and officials to monitor the import of alcohol at the entrance and distribution in the market, which affects the health and lives of people, and the Ministry of Health always And insist again to all people before drinking alcohol to check the source clearly, is there any recognition from professional officials? And drink alcohol in moderation so as not to harm their health.
The director of the Department of Industry and Handicrafts also mentioned some information about the criminals who sell and distribute alcohol, declaring that it is very profitable, so the authorities should take strict action on this issue. Kratie provincial officials confirmed that so far, people who fell ill at the hospital have recovered and left.
It should be noted that cases of alcohol poisoning causing death and illness in Kratie province often occur because the management of these wine production sites is not yet effective.
