(Phnom Penh): The fuel inspection team of the General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce through the Mobile Fuel Laboratory this morning, October 24, 2018, led by Mr. Mean Chamnap, Deputy Director of the Department, in cooperation with professional officers of the Department. The experiments inspected the quantity and quality of fuel at some stations and depots located on Antaminh Street, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Mean Chamnap said that the campaign aims to protect the economic interests of consumers, protect the machinery of all types of vehicles and protect the environment caused by improper fuel consumption, and especially to prevent fraud.
This quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as calibrators with specific volumes for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, 5L, 10L and 20L. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles.
As a result of quality control and quantity of fuel of 5 stations and depots in the above location, there is 1 station and depot that complies with the quality and measurement, while 1 depot has a lack of fuel in accordance with the standard. The other 3 depot gauges are inaccurate in terms of quality and metrics.
