Belgium is one of the seven largest producers and exporters of chocolate. Each year, Belgium produces more than 170,000 tons of chocolate, mostly for export. Those who go to Belgium and do not taste chocolate are like those who go to Cambodia and do not visit Angkor Wat. The other six countries that are famous for producing chocolate are: Switzerland, Ecuador, England, Ivory Coast, Italy and the United States.
