* About gifts for the Prime Minister
Cambodians last month reacted strongly when they saw the posting of pictures of the construction of a model Angkor Wat temple on Chinese soil. The reaction came amid fears that the construction of a Khmer temple model on Chinese soil would mislead tourists into believing that the temple belonged to China or could no longer attract tourists to Cambodia.
During their visit and coverage in China, a Cambodian media delegation was also invited to visit the tourist center. The Cambodian media delegation was warmly welcomed by the management of this tourist center and offered a tour of the large perimeter.
We have observed that many Chinese people visit this tourist center, including the construction site of the Khmer temple of Angkor. The Chinese seem to have a keen interest in the wonders of Cambodia.
Chinese tourism is an important destination for Cambodia's tourism sector. In 2017, more Chinese tourists visited Cambodia than tourists from other countries. Reports show that about 1 million Chinese tourists visit Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen presents the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia at the World Investment Forum 2018 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 23, 2018 in Geneva, Switzerland. Participate in the Global Investment Leaders Summit of the World Investment Forum 2018 under the theme: "Cambodia's Investment Outlook in the Age of Globalization".
In that meaningful forum, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, presented his investment potential to leaders and investors from around the world.
Samdech Techo stated that no matter what the situation, the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to adhere to the open policy that has contributed to high economic growth, around 7% per year for more than two decades.
Foreign direct investment for Cambodia increased by 12% in 2017 to a record $ 2.8 billion in finance, telecommunications, real estate and non-textile manufacturing, making Cambodia one of the most developed countries. At least five countries in the world have the highest growth in investment.
The head of the Royal Government stated that foreign direct investment is an important source of finance for poverty reduction. Cambodia reduced poverty from 53% in 2004 to about 13.5% in 2014. For Cambodia, foreign direct investment is considered a key factor in helping national economic development and the achievement of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
Currently, the Royal Government is working to develop a clear vision and policy to attract more foreign investment by strengthening production bases, building infrastructure and improving both soft and hard transportation systems, reducing electricity prices, and promoting trade facilitation. Human resource development, information technology system development, financial sector development and legal system and institutional reform.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia is actively promoting the implementation of the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025, focusing on building higher value-added production bases and integrating with regional and global value chains. Mr.
Samdech Techo added that the Royal Government of Cambodia is promoting investment in special economic zones that provide efficient collection services. To date, the investment has proposed the registration of 47 special economic zones, of which 19 are in the process of production and export, and 10 are in the process of building the necessary physical infrastructure.
With investment potential in all sectors, policies to protect and encourage investment, labor preferences, broad markets, as well as the many benefits of relocating factories from neighboring countries to Cambodia, as well as growing direct investment flows from the economy. Some, such as China, Japan and South Korea, Cambodia expects to continue to receive higher growth in foreign direct investment.
Regarding economic liberalization in the global framework, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is playing an active role in facilitating and urging WTO member countries to provide preferential tariffs and non-quota concessions to the rules of origin. Goods provide favorable services and provide more technical assistance to less developed countries, as well as repeal of rules that are unfavorable to global investment and trade.
