A well-known Chinese vocational and technical training institute wants to cooperate with Cambodia
(Nanning, China): A well-known Chinese Vocational and Technical Training Institute located in Nanning, Guangxi Province, would like to cooperate with Cambodia to provide vocational and technical training to Cambodian students to meet the human resource needs of Industry and food industry are booming.
Su Huaging, Director of the Nanning Vocational and Technical Training Institute, told the Cambodian delegation during a visit to the Institute on October 23, 2018 that Cambodia is currently experiencing strong industrial growth. And globalization, which requires more training in vocational and technical skills to respond to this growth.
Mr. Su Huanging claimed that the institute has just cooperated with the Cambodian consulate in Nanning, but has not yet deepened. The leadership of this institute wants to cooperate with Cambodia in providing vocational and technical training to Cambodian students.
Through the Cambodian delegation as well as the media, Su Huanging is expected to help disseminate this information to the Royal Government, relevant ministries and institutions of Cambodia to expand cooperation on these trainings. For Mr. Su Huanging is always looking forward to cooperating with Cambodia on training, which is an essential skill for human resources in Cambodia today.
Mr. Chen Peihua, Representative of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and Coordinator of the visit and reporting, also expressed the expectation of cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the above Institute.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always pointed out the lack of professional and technical resources for the labor market and has always urged more attention to training on this skill. Therefore, the expansion of more and more active cooperation in vocational and technical training is a necessary response to the Cambodian context pushing this industry and industrialization.
According to Su Huanging, Nanning Vocational and Technical Training Institute was established in 1984, training 58 vocational and technical skills, and tens of thousands of students have left the institute to help. To society and in enterprises. The institute also receives many awards related to the quality of its education.
Currently, the institute also cooperates with training institutions in ASEAN member countries and many other countries. Angkor temples and famous ASEAN tourist sites built on Chinese soil are very popular among Chinese people
