Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues a press release on the results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's working visit to the Republic of Turkey
(Turkey): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid a working visit to the Republic of Turkey from October 20 to 22, 2018 at the invitation of the Government of the Republic of Turkey.
On the afternoon of October 23, 2018, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation issued a press release on the successful results of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
During his stay in Istanbul on October 20, 2018, the Prime Minister paid a courtesy call on Mr. Binali Yildirim, President of the Turkish National Assembly. Mr. Yildirim hosted a working lunch for the Prime Minister, whose discussions focused on further strengthening friendly relations and cooperation between the two countries.
The Prime Minister and Mr. Yildirim pledged to promote high-level exchanges and visits between the National Assembly of the two countries, especially by promoting the effectiveness of the Cambodia-Turkey Inter-Parliamentary Friendship Group, as well as continuing cooperation. Operation and mutual support within the institutional framework of the Asian Parliament and the Inter-Parliamentary Union.
On October 21, 2018, Samdech Techo Prime Minister held a bilateral meeting with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan. President Erdogan warmly congratulates Samdech Techo PM on his re-appointment as Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. In response, the Prime Minister also congratulated the President on his recent election victory.
The two leaders exchanged in-depth and fruitful views to strengthen and expand bilateral relations in all areas of cooperation, especially in promoting political trust and confidence. The two leaders also reaffirmed their common position in opposing legitimate government changes through any non-democratic process and pledged to further expand cooperation in the fields of counter-terrorism and security.
The two leaders reaffirmed their strong commitment to continue to provide mutual support and close cooperation in the regional and international framework. In this context, the Prime Minister thanked the Turkish government for supporting Cambodia as a member of ECOSOC and thanked His Excellency President Erdogan for pledging to support the ASEAN Mine Action Center in Phnom Penh.
Emphasizing the importance of opening the Cambodian Embassy in Ankara, the Prime Minister reassured President Erdogan that the Embassy would be a solid foundation for Cambodia to build long-term relations with Turkey.
This is the first time that the Cambodian Prime Minister has visited Turkey. Meanwhile, the Turkish President has also expressed his intention to visit Cambodia and expect to see progress in the implementation of the agreement. All signed today. The two leaders expressed strong hopes and agreed to increase bilateral trade to one billion dollars in the near future.
At the end of the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and President Erdogan witnessed the signing ceremony of the following eight agreements / memoranda:
The future regional economic partnership in East Asia will include a market with up to 3 billion users. We have access to other major markets around the world.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister also took the opportunity to meet with Cambodian students studying in Turkey in a friendly and warm atmosphere. PM Tea Banh Meets with Chinese Defense Minister General WEI FENGHE
(Beijing, China): On the occasion of his official and friendly visit to the People's Republic of China on October 23, 2018, a delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia led by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and all members of the delegation met with General WEI FENGHE, Minister of Defense of the People's Republic of China in Beijing.
During the meeting, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said that the cooperation between Cambodia and China has been developing rapidly and has evolved into a comprehensive strategic partnership. Between the two countries, Cambodia - China.
In response, General WEI FENGHE considered that the visit of the delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to China and the participation in the 8th Xiangshan Forum in China showed that Cambodia strongly supports and cares Strongly support the Chinese People's Liberation Army and show that Cambodia fully supports the multilateral events organized by China.
The General stressed that the military relations between the two countries, Cambodia-China is an important part in promoting the closer cooperation between the two countries, Cambodia and China.
The Chinese Defense Minister also congratulated Cambodia on holding a successful general election and the CPP winning a landslide victory. "This success proves that the Cambodian people support and believe in the CPP, which provides peace and benefits in the future," he said.
On that occasion, the Chinese Minister of Defense also expressed his congratulations on the construction of the Victory Monument and the upcoming 20th anniversary of the Victory Day in Cambodia. The General considered the Victory Monument as an architectural structure that reflected that Cambodia has national reconciliation, the Cambodian people have one national unity and will all win.
In order to further strengthen the cooperation between the two armies, the Chinese Defense Minister affirmed that he will continue to promote the retention of high-level delegations between the two armies. The Golden Dragon Exercise 2019, which will be held in March 2019, will continue to help build the Ta Sek Infantry Institute, as well as continue to help train human resources for the Khmer Rouge.
