1,872 Families Affected by Drought and Floods in Pursat Province Receive Humanitarian Donations and Mosquito nets from the Cambodian Red Cross
(Pursat): During 3 days, on October 21-22 and 23, 2018, the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, donated humanitarian aid to the victims. Drought and flood and malaria - Dengue A total of 1,872 families live in Bakan, Kravanh and Veal Veng districts of Pursat province.
The donation ceremony on October 21, 2018 was held at Bakan High School, Bakan District, with 471 families affected by the drought.
For October 22, 2018, held at Hun Sen Bak Chanchean High School, Kravanh District, there were 471 families affected by the drought.
Separately, for October 23, 2018, held at Pramoy High School, Veal Veng District, there were 930 families affected by the flood and malaria-dengue fever.
During the three-day humanitarian donation program, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary-General, brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who sent a message of condolence and gratitude to the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat and the authorities. Provinces that always deal with people in need in a timely manner.
At the same time, let all people live in harmony with each other, both migrants and immigrants, and when the weather improves, please continue to grow livelihoods to restore the family economy to prosper and contribute to accelerating growth. National economy.
Dr. Mao Thunin, Honorary President of Pursat Provincial Branch, on behalf of all the victims, expressed his gratitude for the noble and noble spirit of Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always thinks and connects with the well-being of the people and I wish Samdech Kittipritthbandit and Samdech Techo Prime Minister good health, strength and long life to continue to lead the country to maintain peace, stability and sustainable development.
Separately, 930 families in Veal Veng district affected by landmines and floods affected by malaria and dengue fever received an extra mosquito net and 10,000 Riels for travel expenses. . Oddar Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor Informs Sar Kheng against Anlong Veng District Governor for "Infringing on Private Property"
In his letter, Mr. Kong Ratana stated, "I would like to inform Prince Krala Hom Metta that Hor Chin Virakyuth, male, acting as the governor of Anlong Veng district, has been charged with infringing on private property in O village. Ring, Anlong Veng commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, on June 1, 2018. "Criminal offenses stipulated and punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 248 and Article 253 of the Land Law."
On the afternoon of October 23, 2018, the Deputy Prosecutor of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court, Mr. Koy Kanya, told Fresh News that the Anlong Veng District Governor was indeed charged with The song "infringes on private property" is true and the prosecutor must write a letter to the Minister of Interior because it is the relevant ministry of this person.
However, the deputy prosecutor claimed that the case of the Anlong Veng district governor had been sent to the investigating judge of the provincial court for further action.
Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court President Aak Phalla also confirmed that he had received the Anlong Veng district governor's case, but had not yet sent it to a judge for further investigation.
Article 253 of the Land Law stipulates that any person who commits violence against a real estate occupant in good faith, even if he has not yet filed a title deed or is in dispute, shall be fined from 1,500,000 to 25,000 Riels. 000 Riels and / or imprisonment from 6 months to 2 years, not including the punishment for committing violence against people.
In addition to the above penalties, the perpetrator shall be liable for civil damages to the victims of his own violence. The commanders must be punished in the same way as the perpetrators themselves.
It should be noted that recently, the Governor of Anlong Veng District and his officials conspired with wealthy traders to encroach on more than 20 hectares of community forest land to serve individuals under the pretext of establishing a new commune administration, but this issue was resolved by Mr. Sar Thavy The provincial governor confirmed that he had sent professional officers to conduct a field search.
