(Phnom Penh): On October 23, 2018, the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia issued a statement claiming that the Paris Agreement still has moral value and historical heritage, but it can not be used to As an instrument or a tool to attract the international community to get involved in solving internal problems in Cambodia, which is a democracy.
The statement from the Royal Academy of Cambodia was made on the occasion of the 27th anniversary of the Paris Agreement, or the "Agreement on a Common Political Solution to the Cambodian Conflict", which took place on October 23, 1991 in Paris, France. Every year, October 23 is raised by politicians on a variety of topics for profit.
Opposition groups have recently called on all 18 signatories to the Paris Agreement to revise the agreement, accusing the Cambodian government of violating human rights and democracy and failing to fully implement the agreement. This is not.
The Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia affirms that Cambodia's internal affairs must be resolved by Cambodia under Cambodian internal law. The international community cannot use human rights and democracy as an excuse to violate this sovereign state.
The following is the full statement of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia:
October 23, 2018 is the 27th anniversary of the Paris Agreement, or in other words, an agreement on a common political solution to the Cambodian conflict.
Samdech Orn Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen are key players in building the Paris Peace Agreement. At the Peace Palace on the morning of October 14, 2017, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of the peace talks, emphasized that peace talks could not have taken place without Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and his statue.
Prior to the Paris International Conference, five meetings between the two political figures took place, including:
This statement was made by the Director General of the World Trade Organization (WTO) during a bilateral meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Geneva, Switzerland on the afternoon of October 22, 2018.
During the meeting, Mr. Roberto Kawahu Asevedo, Director-General of the World Trade Organization, also informed the Prime Minister that Cambodia is a less developed country but a member of the World Trade Organization. (WTO) successfully implemented among the fastest growing economies in the world.
He hopes that the Prime Minister's visit to Geneva, especially to the WTO headquarters, will not be the last.
The Prime Minister said that the cooperation between Cambodia and the World Trade Organization will be better, especially Cambodia's economy will be developed and have good cooperation with other countries, including the WTO. Also.
Samdech Techo continued that Cambodia has been a member of the WTO for 14 years and during this time, Samdech thanked the WTO for all the cooperation provided to Cambodia.
In the past, Cambodia has opened its mission to the WTO, although it is in a weak economy, but Cambodia has succeeded in establishing a trade embassy in Geneva to facilitate the work. Between Cambodia and the WTO.
The Director General said that Cambodia has been active in the past 14 years, although compared to other countries, Cambodia is qualified and the first country to appoint a permanent representative of trade. WTO body.
He also considered Samdech Techo a wise leader because the WTO is an institution that provides a lot of support and spirit to its members, which unlike other countries do not care. Keep.
He also praised Cambodia for playing a role in building bridges for other countries, especially in understanding the WTO system.
He added that at present, Cambodia is not outside the system, that is, Cambodia is in the system of the WTO, which Cambodia has explored and seized many opportunities.
He said that due to the intelligence of Cambodia, Cambodia has received technical assistance from the WTO, which spent about $ 7.7 million between 2010 and 2018 for 4 years. In the latest capacity building, up to 411 officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia have been trained in all WTO activities.
During the bilateral talks, Samdech Techo and the Director General discussed in-depth discussions on the World Trade War, especially between the United States and China, which is heating up. Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The Royal Government of Cambodia is using all means to promote the process of SME to grow and have more possibilities, especially to find markets and sources of capital.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that he was very happy to meet again with Ms. Aran Cha Gung Jalez after the first meeting in Cambodia.
In response to Samdech Techo's remarks, Ms. Aracha Mean stated that she had done a lot of work with Cambodia in the past, especially with the Ministry of Commerce.
She added that Cambodia has a lot of capacity to build and expand its potential to make Cambodia more competitive, especially to help small and medium enterprises, which makes trade stronger.
Samdech Techo thanked Ms. Aran Chagungzalez for her assistance to Cambodia, especially in developing a strategy for the strength of small and medium enterprises.
Samdech Techo continued that in the past, Samdech has contributed to the promotion of small and medium enterprises, both in the country and abroad, to promote growth in that sector stronger.
The Prime Minister continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia is using all means to promote the operation of small and medium enterprises to grow and have more possibilities in advance, especially concerns about finding markets and sources of capital.
She said that in November, she will invite Cambodian SMEs to participate in the exhibition in Shanghai, China, and next month she will survey the challenges of SMEs in Cambodia to see what the challenges will be. Find ways to help Cambodia.
