Senior Minister Meas Sophea expressed his pride in the CMAC unit's commitment to clear all mines in Cambodia by 2025
(Battambang): General Meas Sophea, Senior Minister in Charge of Mine Action, Unexploded Ordnance and Engineering Work of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, expressed his high pride to CMAC (CMAC) for its commitment to clear all mines. 2025 in accordance with the plan of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He said this on the occasion that the Senior Minister, accompanied by Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of CMAC and other officials visited the CMAC forces and to find out some of the work related to demining activities. At the 2nd Cambodian Mine Action Unit, Battambang Province, on October 23, 2018.
"There are four types of bombs left over from the two wars that still endanger the lives of the people," he said. These include bombs and unexploded ordnance: cluster munitions, chemical bombs and anti-personnel mines. "Currently, CMAC has five main tools and skills, including demining, including the use of manpower, machinery, dogs, mice and demining under rain."
However, at present, CMAC does not have enough human and financial resources to clear the land because it requires a lot of money. However, the CMAC unit has committed and cleared all mines by 2025 in accordance with the direction of the Royal Government. Good luck! Two Factory Workers Win 70 Million Riels from Carabao Energy Drink
