(Phnom Penh): October 23, 2018 is the 27th anniversary of the Paris Agreement, or in other words, an agreement on a common political solution to the Cambodian conflict.
Interview with Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong - Former Cambodian diplomat on the 27th anniversary of the Paris Agreement, October 23, 1991 - October 23, 2018 Out of the INF nuclear treaty with Russia!
BEIJING (Reuters) - China has expressed concern and called on the United States, the Russian Federation and relevant countries to resume talks on the Interim Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (INF). This is according to a statement issued by the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, quoted by Xinhua on Monday night, October 22, 2018.
Last Saturday, US President Donald Trump announced that his country would withdraw from the INF Nuclear Treaty, which the United States and the former Soviet Union (now Russia) signed in 1987, a treaty required. Let the two rival powers reduce the number of short-range and medium-range ballistic missiles.
However, the United States has accused Russia of violating the 1987 treaty by illegally deploying the banned weapons along with China, despite previous promises by China and Russia to halt development. And produce weapons of this type already.
Responding to the allegations, the Chinese Foreign Ministry issued a statement explaining that "it is very wrong for the United States to link China to the reasons for Washington's withdrawal." "That nuclear treaty."
