(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the National Council for Sustainable Development (NCSD), on the morning of October 22, 2018, considered that improving energy efficiency is the main factor. One that can promote sustainable economic development and low carbon emissions in Cambodia.
The remarks of the Minister of Environment were made at the opening ceremony of the conference on "Improving Cambodia's Energy Efficiency: Key Steps Towards Sustainable Economic Growth" at the Raffles Royal Hotel, Phnom Penh, organized by the National Council for Development Sustainable collaboration with the Swedish government and the Cambodian Climate Change Alliance (CCCA) program.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Say Sam Al also proposed to increase education to all energy users at the individual, family, enterprise, community and society as a whole in order to change attitudes to focus on improving efficiency. Energy that will enable them to reduce costs and increase benefits even more.
At the same time, the Swedish Ambassador to Cambodia, Ms. Maria Sagran, also said that energy efficiency is very important to meet the direction of Cambodia to achieve sustainable growth. The Swedish government over the last 30 years has made significant improvements in both promoting renewable energy and improving energy efficiency while achieving economic growth.
A total of 152 participants, including 36 women, national and international speakers and representatives of ministries, institutions, government, private sector research institutes, civil society, discussed best practices and tools that promote energy efficiency initiatives in Cambodia and Accelerate Cambodia's transition to development models for reducing greenhouse gas emissions.
