Calmette Hospital Holds Workshop on Nuclear Medicine to Promote Effective Cancer Treatment
(Phnom Penh): Nuclear medicine offers the best treatment options for patients, leading to an improvement in quality of life, in particular, reducing patients' costs.
"The inauguration of the National Cancer Center is part of the first nuclear medicine in Cambodia," said Calmette Hospital Director General. Earlier this year was another development in the health sector in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Dr. Kong Sanya, Deputy Director General of Calmette Hospital, said that this is the first time that Calmette Hospital has held a seminar on nuclear medicine in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
He said the use of the term "nuclear medicine" sounds strange. He said that in fact, the use of the term in nuclear medical technology is very useful in the treatment of cancer, which requires the use of this technique to kill cancer cells.
The Deputy Director General of the hospital also confirmed that in early 2018, Calmette Hospital will open a cancer treatment center with a variety of treatment techniques such as on-site radiation and nuclear medicine. Therefore, in order for the technology level of the hospital to be equal to the world, it is necessary for the hospital to have nuclear medicine as well.
At the same time, Professor Sobhan Vinjamuri said that nuclear medicine, also known as molecular medicine, which is of particular concern, has been known for more than 40 years and is used in Medical field. "But nuclear medicine does not cause health problems because in the world, nuclear medicine is everywhere," he said.
