(Phnom Penh): 837 families living in Vimean Trong Community (Nokor Thmey) in Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Sen Sok, equivalent to 837 plots of land, have received legal title to real estate from Phnom Penh Capital Administration. According to the procedure, which is the final stage of the land registration process, there is a systematic program of land administration sub-sectors that is being implemented in the 25 capitals and provinces of Cambodia.
The handing over ceremony of real estate title was held this morning, October 22, 2018, presided over by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, which was held in the Vimean Trong community with the participation of hundreds of people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that before reaching the stage of issuing legal title, we have made great efforts for the harmony of the people and ask you to keep this card well and use it effectively. He said that land registration has provided two benefits to our state and to the people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that for the people, it is to ensure the warmth, security, land and full land tenure of the people, and the real estate certificate is important as proof of their land tenure and to avoid land encroachment.
This card can also enable our people to take to the bank to borrow money to do business. For the state, this land registration provides enormous possibilities for land management and better organization and facilitation of appropriate land use planning to reduce land disputes.
