According to a press release from the General Secretariat of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, obtained by Fresh News on October 22, the seven main agendas to be included in the 30th session are: :
1: Report on the activities of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy between the 29th and 30th sessions.
2. Examine and decide on the decision of the Disciplinary Council of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.
3. Examine and decide on the change of chairman, vice chairman and judge.
4. To consult on the proposal to change the prosecutor and some deputy prosecutors at the request of the Minister of Justice.
5: Examine and decide on the continuation of the work of a judge of the Supreme Court who is 65 years old.
6: Examine and decide on the request to return to work of a judge of Kandal Provincial Court and the request for permission to continue the two-year study of a judge of Kampot Provincial Court.
