The number of refugees fleeing to the US-Mexico border has risen to 5,000!
(Guatemala): The Guatemalan refugee agency acknowledged that more than 1,000 refugees had crossed the border from Honduras on Sunday, bringing the number of Central American refugees to the US-Mexico border. 5,000 people. This is according to the release by Sputnik on Monday afternoon, October 22, 2018.
Meanwhile, according to Mexican authorities, the number of refugees on the Mexican-Guatemala border has risen to 2,000, although authorities have not yet been able to determine whether they were traveling from any country in the region. Anyway. In response, the Mexican government ordered police to close the border for undocumented refugees.
In addition, US President Donald Trump has stated that all refugees must seek asylum in Mexico first, otherwise the United States will expel them from the US border.
Last week, Donald Trump warned against sending troops to the border with Mexico to stem the flow of refugees to the US border.
Every day, more than 10 tons of vegetables and fruits are imported from Vietnam through Phnom Den International Factory, CamControl officers regularly inspect to ensure the supply on the Cambodian market without chemicals
(Takeo): In the preliminary tests on many fruits and vegetables imported from Vietnam through the Phnom Den international border crossing in Takeo province, CamControl officials confirmed that no chemicals were found on all fruits and vegetables. .
Mr. Por Leang Kong, Head of Camcontrol Branch in Takeo Province, said that Camcontrol officers at the Phnom Den International Border Crossing, in cooperation with the relevant agencies stationed at the border, inspected goods imported from Vietnam, including cauliflower, kale, cabbage, fruit and cooking oil. Preliminary tests for chemicals, but as a result, officials found no chemicals on the fruits and vegetables.
The President of CamControl Takeo Branch said that every day, about 8 to 12 tons of vegetables and fruits are imported from Vietnam to Cambodia through the Phnom Den International Gate, and CamControl officials have tested and found chemicals. Insecticides on garlic, cardamom, peppers and cabbage, and officials have banned the import of all those vegetables.
But now the vegetables are allowed to return to normal after the officials sent the vegetables to the General Department of Control to check for chemicals, but these vegetables do not contain chemicals.
According to the Camcontrol Branch Manager in Takeo Province, Por Leang Kong, although the experts did not find any chemicals on the fruits and vegetables imported from Vietnam, the Camcontrol officers at the Phnom Den International Gate will be on duty. Regularly inspect all imported fruits and vegetables to ensure that the imported fruits and vegetables on the Cambodian market contain chemicals that affect consumers.
Royal Government Advisor: One Belt, One Road policy to move the real estate sector in Cambodia forward
(Phnom Penh): One Belt One Road policy has moved the real estate sector in Cambodia forward, while many Chinese investment companies are now investing heavily in the construction industry in Cambodia.
Mr. Chhiv Koursinh, Chief Executive Officer of Prince Real Estate China, said that the presence of Prince Real Estate in the Cambodian real estate market now stems from its one-way belt policy. China, which has opened up opportunities and encouraged a lot of investment from Chinese investors to come to Cambodia.
He said that the decision to invest in real estate projects in Cambodia is because the company has seen the rapid growth of Cambodia's economic growth compared to other countries in the region, in which the construction sector has been playing an important role in Stimulating national economic growth, and the sector is also demanding more supplementation to meet demand.
He said that during the three years of Prince Real Estate Group's presence in Cambodia, the company has invested a total of more than 1,200 million dollars in large condominium and business center projects, of which three large projects will Is gradually emerging in Phnom Penh and three other large projects are also investing in Sihanoukville.
He said that the company's vision for the next 10 years, the company will increase investment capital to 6 billion dollars in the construction industry in Cambodia, while the company has now collected land for investment in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap, many locations as well.
In addition, he said that in addition to investing in Cambodia, Prince Real Estate has also set up a charity fund to help people in need in Cambodia, the donation came from the sale of condos in Cambodia.
Sok Siphana, a government adviser and legal expert, said: "This policy has really encouraged Chinese investors to invest directly in Cambodia. "For example, there has been tremendous development in infrastructure and energy projects."
As a result, the One Belt One Road policy has led to the construction of a 190-kilometer expressway connecting Sihanoukville to Phnom Penh, while investment in real estate in Sihanoukville is growing. There is more and more growth.
Dr. Ly Sovann, spokesman for the Ministry of Health, told Fresh News that poisoning in some communes in Kratie province's Sambo district has killed five people, including a woman, while the number of people who have fallen ill has risen. Up to 78 people.
