Top Cambodian, Turkish leaders agree to boost bilateral trade to $ 1 billion
(Turkey): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan have agreed to boost trade between Cambodia and Turkey to $ 1 billion in a short period of time. Ahead.
The President continued with the hope that high-level visits between the two countries would continue in the near future.
At the bilateral summit, the leaders of the two countries agreed to celebrate the 25th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries in 2020 by organizing activities for the people. Of both countries know each other from our country.
The two leaders discussed ways to boost the tourism growth of the two countries by opening up direct flights to each other in addition to the current freight forwarding. To transport passengers and tourists for both countries in the near future.
Given that Cambodia has received the ASEAN Mine Action Center in Cambodia, the President said that Turkey will look into the possibility of providing assistance to the ASEAN Mine Action Center in Cambodia, especially providing support to ASEAN.
At the bilateral summit, the leaders of the two countries, Cambodia and Turkey, discussed issues related to bilateral relations, multilateralism, regional and international issues, mutual support in the international framework, especially working. Joint commitment to the fight against crime and the fight against international terrorist networks.
During the bilateral summit, Samdech Techo Prime Minister requested the President to continue to increase the provision of scholarships to Cambodian students to study in Turkey and help buy Angkor mangoes from Cambodia to help Cambodian farmers.
In the name of His Majesty the King, Samdech Techo Prime Minister extended an oral invitation to the President to pay a state visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia at an appropriate time in the future.
