(Phnom Penh): From October 27-28, 2018, the National Employment Agency (NEA) of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in collaboration with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Phnom Penh and the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia. GMAC) together with other stakeholders will organize the 2nd National Job and Productivity Fair 2018 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
For 2018, about 20,000 job opportunities of all kinds are ready to accept job seekers provided by more than 130 large companies from major sectors such as banking and microfinance institutions, construction, hotels and hospitality, telecommunications, education and training. Professional techniques, training and private recruitment agencies will be on display at a total of 300 booths.
The National Job and Productivity Fair is expected to attract more than 30,000 visitors, mostly students, youth, job seekers and workers from all walks of life.
In addition to access to tens of thousands of job opportunities, participants will also receive information on current and future recruitment plans, plans and policies, courses, scholarships, courses and skills development programs.
This major event will also host a workshop on productivity to help raise awareness of productivity, demonstrations of work methods, innovations, skills and technological tools in line with the evolution of technology in the fourth generation of industrial era. Mainly on digital systems.
The National Job and Productivity Fair 2018 is about the Royal Government of Cambodia's job forum mechanism as stated in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 to improve the employment sector and labor market information in Cambodia, especially to provide a wide range of job opportunities to the workforce. Skilled and unskilled to get a better job, save time, reduce costs and get a higher income.
In addition, the National Job and Productivity Fair also contributes to reducing the gap between supply and demand of skills in the labor market, as well as making it easier for young people to enter the labor market to get a job after graduating from higher education. Or technical and professional skills.
For job opportunities and understanding of job creation, please all young people, students, job seekers and workers, visit and do not forget to bring your resume (CV) to apply for a job directly with the employer. Need to recruit labor.
