Cambodian Officials and Journalists Invited to Visit and Report on Development in Chinese Provinces
(Phnom Penh): Officials from the Ministry of Information and journalists from various institutions, including reporters from Fresh News, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, in cooperation with the Chinese authorities, organized visits and coverage in some Chinese provinces to disseminate information. And explore the industrial development, management system and culture of the Chinese people.
The visit and coverage will take place for 12 days from October 22 to November 2, 2018. During the visit, Cambodian officials and journalists will visit cities in China's two provinces, Guangxi and Jiangsu.
The administrative, industrial, commercial and residential locations of Chinese citizens will also be presented to Cambodian media officials and journalists during the visit.
Chinese embassy officials are optimistic that the visit and outreach will improve the relationship between the Cambodian government and the Chinese government, as well as the Cambodian-Chinese people.
It should be noted that the two provinces that Cambodian officials and journalists will visit are the economically and industrially developed provinces and important economic ports of China, especially in relation to the Chinese government's policy of the Belt and Road. Because it is a province by the sea.
Guangxi is an autonomous region of China in south-central China bordering Vietnam. In 2016, the province had a population of about 55 million.
According to the report, in 2011, Guangxi was the 18th largest province in China with annual economic revenue of 185.9 billion US dollars. The people of this province have an annual income of about $ 2,300.
The main crops in Guangxi include rice, corn, sweet potatoes, sugarcane and tobacco. The province has excellent relations in trade, tourism and education with Cambodia as well.
Jiangsu Province is a rich natural resource located in the east coast of China. Jiangsu is also one of China's strong industrial foundations. In 2017, the province had annual revenues of about 1.27 trillion US dollars, ranking second among China's fastest growing economies. The annual income of a person is about 17,176 US dollars.
Jiangsu is also one of China's oldest cultural provinces. At present, the leaders of Jiangsu Province also have many relations and cooperation with the Cambodian authorities. Various illegal fishing gears confiscated and destroyed by officers after operation found along Stung Sen River, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Various types of illegal fishing gear were confiscated and destroyed after being found in Stung Sen River after the inspection of the provincial authority and relevant professional officers of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province for 2 years. The day is October 20-21, 2018.
The director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture confirmed that as a result, many types of illegal fishing gear were confiscated and destroyed, including: 6 fishing nets, equal to 6 mouths, with a total of 85 meters long bait and wooden poles. Open 12 mouths as well.
Mr. Peng Trida added that during the operation to crack down on illegal fishing along the Stung Sen River at that time, the joint team did not arrest any suspects, only confiscated illegal fishing gear.
However, the director of the department also called on people to fish, use traditional tools, do not use illegal tools that lead to the destruction of fish species, and the use of illegal fishing gear is a challenge. And the penalty of imprisonment is there, so please, our people, do not use illegal fishing gear to avoid guilt and the destruction of fish.
