Eight agreements signed during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Turkey
(Turkey): Eight important agreements to be signed between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Turkey during the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to promote relations and expand cooperation with the two countries.
The eight agreements were signed after a bilateral meeting between the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of Turkey on the evening of October 21, 2018.
Those agreements are as follows:
1. Agreement on cultural cooperation on the Cambodian side signed by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with the Turkish side signed by Mr. Mevlüt Çavuşoğlu, Minister of Foreign Affairs.
2: Agreement on Cooperation in the field of non-discrimination on the Cambodian side, signed by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with the Turkish side, signed by Mr. Mevlüt Çavuşoğlu, Minister of Foreign Affairs.
4: Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Agriculture in Cambodia, signed by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with Turkey, signed by Mr. Bekir Pakdemirli, Minister of Agriculture and Forestry.
5: Agreement on Water Cooperation on the Cambodian side, signed by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with the Turkish side, signed by Mr. Bekir Pakdemirli, Minister of Agriculture and Forestry.
7. Agreement on the Promotion and Reciprocal Protection of Investment on the Cambodian Side, signed by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia with the Turkish side, signed by Mr. Mustafa Varank, Minister of Industry And technology.
In addition, Cambodia and Turkey will sign agreements on a number of areas, such as cooperation in agriculture, tourism, education, sports, culture and more.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that although Cambodian investors have little opportunity to invest in Turkey, Cambodia still works closely with Turkey in diplomatic relations, cooperation, investment, trade, economy, education and key sectors. Many more.
