Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues a press release on the outcome of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's participation in the Asia-Europe Summit in Brussels, Belgium
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on October 21, 2018 issued a statement on the results of the invitation to attend the 12th Asia-Europe Summit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. October 18-19, 2018 in Brussels, Belgium.
The 12th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) successfully concluded with the adoption of the Conference Chair's Statement on "Europe and Asia: Global Partners for Global Challenges".
The leaders discussed a number of issues, focusing on promoting inclusive growth and ASEM connectivity and sustainable development in line with the context of the 2030 Agenda.
During the summit, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen shared his views on the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, emphasizing the need for a coordination mechanism to address key challenges. Global issues that could affect individual countries' ability to ensure growth, address poverty reduction, improve gender equality and women's empowerment.
The Prime Minister reaffirmed his support for the multilateral system in global governance, especially the World Trade Organization. Asia and Europe should further strengthen cooperation to ensure peace, security, development and basic human rights, which are key factors in achieving the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
At the end of the summit, the Prime Minister thanked all ASEM partners for supporting Cambodia to host the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020 in Phnom Penh.
