(Kampong Chhnang): Major General Loch Vannara, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Chhnang Province, confirmed to Fresh News on the afternoon of October 21 that the assailant who killed two girls in Boribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province was arrested by the police force. He was released after two days of interrogation.
The commissioner said that the killing of the two girls was the result of a rape and murder case.
Lt. Gen. Loch Vannara added that the assailant, named Chhom Poy, was a neighbor of the victim girl. The suspect went up to rape his older sister, but at that moment, the younger sister saw and shouted, and for fear of exploding, the suspect took a pillow and held his breath, causing the two to die immediately.
The commissioner also stated that the hot operation was carried out under the direct command of Brigadier General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General and Provincial Governor of Kampong Chhnang, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, led by Brigadier General Pol Vuthy, Deputy Commissioner of Criminal Affairs. .
According to the commissioner, after the murder on October 20, 2018, the police called the mother, aunt and uncle of the victim and the perpetrator to interrogate.
He said that at first the suspect refused to confess, but eventually due to the use of the skills of the police, the suspect also confessed. In contrast, the girl's uncle and aunt were not involved.
Lt. Gen. Loch Vannara also pointed out that after the arrest of the suspect, his police force will bring the perpetrator to the scene.
It should be noted that two girls, siblings, were brutally murdered and stuffed into boxes and placed on the hut where the victims stayed every day, causing a surprise at noon on the 18th. October 2018 in Thmey Village, Phsar Commune, Baribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
After an autopsy, authorities confirmed that the body was indeed murdered and put in a suitcase. The first two victims: 14-year-old A.L.N. and the second: 7-year-old A.D.T. What is even more shocking is that the parents of the two girls were not at home with them because their mother went to work in a factory in Phnom Penh and their father went to work in Thailand.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh: The Victory Monument is divided into 3 main parts
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Committee for the Construction of a Win-Win Monument, this morning, October 21, 2018, stated that the organization of this Win-Win Monument is divided into The three main sections, the body of the monument, show everything related to win-win politics, the left and right sides show the harmonization and achievement of win-win politics.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said this on the occasion of inspecting the location of the Victory Monument to prepare for the inauguration on December 29.
The right-hand side of the monument is set up as an achievement area to prove that the win-win policy has lasted for 20 years. Also shown in this area of achievement, and what is important is in the core area, with the specific symbols 35, 7 and 7 in the document, clearly explained in this win-win policy.
His Majesty the King Kong Sam Ol expressed his assessment of the efforts to build this win-win monument, while in two months, the inauguration program will come on December 29, 30 and 31, 2018.
