At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen presented the investment potential and important advantages of Cambodia, such as:
1. Political stability and security in the country put Cambodia on top of economic and social development at an average annual economic growth rate of 7%.
2. Cambodia is strategically located in the history of ASEAN as a region that has been becoming a factory of ASEAN, and Cambodia is also in the middle of the Mekong region, the region with the highest interconnected economic growth for development. Manufacturing and service industries with countries in the region.
3. A diverse workforce, with those under the age of 35 accounting for up to 72% of the total workforce, combined with an increase in the middle-income and middle-class population will create opportunities for Cambodia in achieving this high economic growth.
4. Cambodia is open to the economy for all investors without discrimination between local and foreign investors, and foreigners can invest 100 percent.
5. Cambodian-made goods are not only supplied to the Cambodian market, but also exported to the Mekong sub-region market with about 250 million customers and many other ASEAN markets.
