National Road No. 48 from Sre Ambel district to Koh Kong town has been repaired by more than 70%, while it is scheduled to be completed before the sea festival
(Koh Kong): As of the third week of October 2018, National Road No. 48 has been repaired more than 70% under the efforts of the technical working group of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and related parties.
The road is 150 kilometers long from the intersection of Sre Ambel to the provincial town of Koh Kong, of which 63 kilometers were damaged by floods, overcrowding and other natural factors.
The road is divided into 91 short sections to be repaired in time by a joint force of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, engineering forces and stakeholders using a total of 114 vehicles, planned to cost about 12 million US dollars, now more than 70% Will be completely renovated before the upcoming Sea Festival.
Please be informed that Road 48 has been damaged due to old age and needs to be rebuilt due to overloading and incessant rainy weather conditions in the area.
