In order to promote Turkish trade, tourism and investment in Cambodia, the Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia has promoted direct flights between Cambodia and Turkey as soon as possible.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the Cambodia-Turkey Business Forum as the best opportunity for Cambodian and Turkish investors to meet, discuss and inspire business and investment networks between the two countries.
The Prime Minister also stated that Cambodia has been actively involved in regional and global trade, with the Cambodian trade volume increasing steadily to US $ 25.6 billion, equivalent to about 115% of gross domestic product (GDP). ) In 2017 ago. However, the trade volume between Cambodia and Turkey is still small.
For the first nine months of 2018, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved investment projects with a total capital of about 4.7 billion US dollars, while Turkish investment projects are still small, which previously had only three Turkish investment projects. Project and investment capital of approximately US $ 11 million registered with the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC).
As for tourism, the number of tourists visiting Cambodia increased steadily by about 5.6 million in 2017, and in the first eight months of 2018, Cambodia welcomed a total of nearly 4 million tourists, an increase of about 12% compared to the same period last year. At the same time, 2017. There are about 5,000 tourists in Turkey.
Samdech Techo also stated that within the framework of bilateral relations, the two countries have signed important memoranda of understanding in the past and eight more agreements in the fields of tourism, agriculture, culture and investment, which will be signed on October 21, 2018, which will strengthen the cooperation of our two countries.
