Cambodia, Turkey discuss opening of Cambodian embassy in Turkey as soon as possible and agree to visit at all levels to strengthen ties, solidarity and cooperation
In the face-to-face meeting, Samdech Techo and the President of the Turkish Parliament exchanged views on boosting diplomatic ties, exchanging views on boosting trade, investment, tourism and other areas. Including the promotion of direct flights from Turkey to Cambodia to boost tourism, trade and investment.
The Prime Minister and Speaker of the Turkish Parliament also discussed bilateral issues, multilateral issues, regional and international issues, especially enhancing mutual trust and assistance in bilateral, multilateral, regional and international frameworks. International that provides mutual benefits.
The Prime Minister also told the Speaker of the National Assembly that Samdech has always wanted to come to Turkey for a long time because Turkey is a land of Asia-Europe connection and considered this as a visit. It is the first and only time in the history of the first Cambodian leader to pay a working visit to the Republic of Turkey.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister and Speaker of the Turkish Parliament exchanged views on promoting exchanges of visits from all levels of the two countries in order to boost cooperation between the two countries. Even more advanced.
After a face-to-face meeting, the Prime Minister and the Speaker of the Turkish Parliament were invited to relax at the Government House in Istanbul, especially for a breath of fresh air by the sea and a working dinner. Days.
The President of the National Assembly of Turkey extended a warm welcome to the Prime Minister and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which selected Turkey for the first working visit in the history of the two countries' relations. Only 20 years ago.
The Speaker of the National Assembly agreed with the Prime Minister's views on promoting exchanges of visits from all levels in order to further enhance the cooperation between the two countries.
Afterwards, Mr. Binali Yidirim, President of the National Assembly and former Prime Minister of Turkey, hosted a working luncheon for Samdech Techo Prime Minister and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who paid a working visit to Istanbul, Republic of the Philippines. Turkey.
Later in the afternoon, the Prime Minister presided over the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-Turkey Business Forum. The Cambodia-Turkey Business Forum, held at the Istanbul Chamber of Commerce, was attended by senior Turkish government officials, the private sector and many Cambodian and business dignitaries.
In that significant ceremony, after listening to the intervention of the leaders of the Turkish economy, trade and business, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, gave a keynote speech at the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-Turkey Business Forum.
Afterwards, Samdech Techo Prime Minister witnessed the signing ceremony of the document on cooperation between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, with Duke Kith Meng as the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the President of the Turkish Chamber of Commerce to strengthen solidarity. Between the two institutions to be even stronger.
It should be noted that at the signing ceremony, private institutions of both countries, Cambodia and Turkey, also presented souvenirs to each other.
The Republic of Turkey covers an area of more than 783 thousand square kilometers, bordering Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bulgaria, Georgia, Greece, Iran, Iraq and Syria and has a population of over 80 million.
On diplomatic relations, Cambodia established diplomatic relations with Turkey on June 14, 1994, and on November 1, 2013, the Republic of Turkey opened its embassy in Phnom Penh. Cambodia currently has two honorary consulates in the Republic of Turkey, with Cambodia planning to open its embassy in Ankara in 2019.
