Below are the details surrounding the murder of this journalist:
Khashoggi left his native Saudi Arabia in September 2017 to live abroad. The Saudi government has banned him from using Twitter. He later wrote a newspaper article criticizing the government of his home country. He also expressed opposition to intervention in Yemen led by the Saudi government.
* Relationship with Osama bin Laden
Khashoggi met Osama bin Laden in the 1980s and 1990s. He has interviewed the terrorist leader several times. During that time, he was hired by Saudi intelligence to persuade bin Laden to reconcile with the Saudi royal family.
* Disappearance
However, the Saudi government said he had left the consulate through the back door. But the Turkish government has said he has not yet come out. Turkish authorities claimed that security camera footage of the incident had been removed from the consulate and that Turkish consular staff had been told to rest on the day Khashoggi went missing while inside the building.
Turkish police investigators told the media that security cameras at the consulate did not provide any evidence that Khashoggi had left the consulate. Security cameras at the eastern part of the consulate, which showed him inside, did not show him leaving, while another camera installed at the kindergarten opposite the eastern entrance of the consulate did not show him. Leave the same.
Analysts have suggested that Khashoggi could be considered a serious threat to the leadership of Saudi Arabia, not only because he is an opposition figure, but also because he knows a lot of internal issues of power. Generations of leaders of this oil country, as well as former heads of intelligence agencies.
* Investigation
* The accused perpetrators:
* Reaction: The Saudi government initially claimed that the victim left the consulate shortly after entering. But later admitted that the journalist actually died at the consulate, in conflict with people and fought to the death, not by order. The Turkish president, meanwhile, believes Khashoggi was assassinated in connection with a Saudi royal family.
He demanded that the government of the oil country release evidence that Khashoggi had indeed left the consulate alive. The United States has asked the Saudi government to assist in the investigation into the disappearance.
Anlong Veng district authorities are suspected of colluding with traders to take more than 20 hectares of community forest land to serve individuals under the pretext of establishing a "new commune administration."
(Oddar Meanchey): Samaki Community Forest Rescue, a community of more than 4,000 hectares of forest protection activities in Romchek village, Anlong Veng commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, appealed to the Royal Government and relevant authorities to help protect their community forest land after It is suspected that the Anlong Veng local authorities are colluding with wealthy traders to clear the community land.
Mr. Sot Pek, President of the Solidarity Community to Save the Forest, which was established in 2002, told Fresh News on October 20, 2018 that about 4,000 hectares of community forest land with the above location is owned by the people in The village has been jointly protected since 2002. Because the forest is a place to provide various by-products to support the livelihood of the people and also want to protect many rare wildlife that live in the forest.
The community leader went on to claim that the Anlong Veng district authorities had recently asked the community for about 20 hectares of land to build schools, hospitals and pagodas, as the area was planned to be a new commune administrative system.
For reasons of public service, the people in the community did not ban anything. But when the authorities put a tractor down to clear and the community to ask for other documents suddenly did not show. This is according to Mr. Soth Pek.
Mr. Soth Pek further stated that after not finding the relevant documents approved by the relevant ministries and institutions, especially from the provincial hall, the people also forbade further clearing.
After the discovery of these documents, the community suspected that the Anlong Veng district authorities, headed by Hor Chin Virakyuth, were planning to conspire with wealthy traders to take the land. Their ownership.
In connection with this issue, Oddar Meanchey provincial governor Sar Thavy confirmed to Fresh News that he had not yet received all the information, and was providing further research on the matter. However, the provincial governor claimed that there was no permission from the Ministry of Interior to study the establishment of the area to the new commune administration in Anlong Veng district, just to study the division. Boundaries only.
If what the provincial governor claims is true, it means that Anlong Veng district governor Hor Chin Virakyuth is acting beyond his jurisdiction, because even the governor does not know about the creation of a new commune, why Chhean district governor To clear land to use as a location to establish a commune administration? Or is the district governor really being negotiated as a trader to take this land as his own, as the community suspects?
However, Sar Thavy, the provincial governor, claimed that he would do his best to investigate the matter. At the same time, the community also called on the Royal Government and relevant ministries to take action to protect this community forest land, because it is important for the community to find non-timber forest products to support livelihoods and is also an important wildlife sanctuary in that area. .
The community claims that they will not block the authorities if the land is actually used for public use, but what they are worried about is that the land will be used for the benefit of individuals with money and power.
Mr. Sot Peak claimed that the people in Anlong Veng commune have been working together to protect the community forest since 2002, and this forest land has many rare wildlife. Community forest land is also opposite to the Ministry of Environment's conservation forest land.
