Phnom Penh Governor Leads Officials to Inspect and Solve Flood Areas in Front of Phnom Penh International Airport
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, this morning, October 20, 2018, led the specialized departments and authorities of Khan Sen Sok and Khan Por Sen Chey to inspect the area in front of Phnom Penh International Airport and some flooded areas. Due to flooding in these two districts.
In connection with this work, Mr. Khuong Sreng inspected the drainage system along the Russian Federation Road from 2011 to Dangkul Road and continued to see the Tuol Sampov Canal in the geographical area of Damnak Village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
Toul Sampov Canal plays an important role in releasing water from the Russian Federation Road, Sangkat Choam Chao I, II, III, Khan Por Sen Chey and some areas in Khan Sen Sok, such as Damnak Village, Kork Khleang Commune, Kraing Angkrang Village, Kraing Thnong Sangkat.
The homes of some people in the area were also affected by the floods. The authorities of Po Sen Chey district, as well as the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, are concerned and consider this issue in order to find effective measures to release water outside the area.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also instructed Daun Penh Company, which is the contractor to install the drainage system at the latrine point on the road of the Russian Federation, to improve the technical characteristics of the drainage well to ensure the water flow and on time.
Drainage officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh said that in this area, the sewer system is connected. But the point to be resolved is to rehabilitate the watermelon plantation canal and the Tuol Sampov canal to bring water to the Tuol Sampov pumping station in time.
Currently, Toul Sampov canal, Taing Krasang canal has been violated, landslides, dumping of garbage into the canal and a lot of weeds and other plants grow on the canal, which is one of the main reasons why the canal is shallow. Requires restoration and refurbishment.
It should be noted that last weekend, the authorities of Po Sen Chey and Sen Sok districts together with the Department of Public Works worked to restore the Tuol Sampov canal, which is adjacent to both districts. The Tuol Sampov canal plays an important role in relieving flooding from the area in front of Phnom Penh International Airport and the surrounding area.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to build five bridges across the Tuol Sampov canal, which will help facilitate the flow of water. At the same time, the Department of Public Works and Transport has submitted a proposal to Phnom Penh Capital Hall to rehabilitate the Stung Meanchey and Boeung Tumpun canals, which are under regular maintenance, which are important for the release of water in the south and west of Phnom Penh. .
