(Brussels, Belgium): In the opening ceremony of the 12th Asia-Europe Summit in Brussels, Belgium on October 19, 2018, in front of Asia-Europe Leaders, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia Welcome and welcome the new positive developments on the Korean Peninsula. In particular, the unprecedented summit between the United States and North Korea, as well as several summits between the two Koreas in the past.
Samdech Techo said that those historic summits were a major step towards an era of relief, conducive to further talks on the complete elimination of nuclear weapons and the gradual establishment of lasting peace. In the Korean Peninsula.
"It is clear that the road to complete nuclear disarmament is still a long way off and requires the patience of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea and the United States," he said. "Cambodia believes that the reaction approach should be consistently adopted and that both sides should work together in good faith to increase mutual trust and confidence."
"We welcome the commitment and will of both the United States and Korea, especially the Republic of Korea's new policy for a peaceful Korean Peninsula," he added.
The Prime Minister continued to call on all parties concerned to exercise restraint and remain committed to constructive and peaceful dialogue in order to reduce tensions and achieve a complete disarmament of controllable nuclear weapons. Yes and no return on the Korean Peninsula.
