Kampong Cham Ministry of Mines and Administration Holds Public Forum with More Than 1,000 People in Srey Santhor District to Address Concerns About Landslides and Sand Dredging
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Dith Tina, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, on October 19, 2018, organized a public forum with more than 1,000 people living along the river. People in Srey Santhor district to solve the concern about the river bank collapse, which has always been said to be from the sand dredging business in the area.
He pointed out that the river always has river bank collapse every year. He said that all river bank collapses are not all caused by the sand dredging business, but also caused by nature, which means that if one side of the river collapses, the other side grows, which is caused by the condition of the river. Where there is a strong current, there will be a landslide.
"Therefore, in order to prevent the landslide from becoming serious, we need to make sure that the center of the river has a deep water flow so that the water does not hit the river bank," he said. "This is a technique that technical officials from the Ministry of Mines and Energy have presented and explained techniques to reduce riverbank landslides."
According to the provincial governor, along with the river bank collapse during 2017 and 2018, the provincial authorities also went to help dismantle the houses of people who face river bank collapse to avoid them from danger. By the collapse of the river bank. With this natural disaster, the provincial authorities have organized social work with the victims, and so far, according to statistics, more than 20 families have been affected by the river bank collapse.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun added, "The only thing that needs to be addressed is to gather the brothers and sisters to think together as a group, if they encounter such an incident, where will they go to live so that the provincial authorities will organize The village is rebuilt. ”
"The provincial authorities are also involved with you in helping to organize the infrastructure and some issues related to the needs, such as roads, water, electricity or schools and some other services for you to use the message," he said. "Once again, to stop the threat of river bank collapse." Asia-Europe Leaders Recognize Importance of Asia-Europe Connectivity for Sustainable Development
(Brussels, Belgium): As planned, the 12th Asia-Europe Meeting on "Europe and Asia: Global Partners for Global Challenges" under the theme "Building a Future Together: Promoting Environmental Growth and Sustainable Connections ”was officially opened on October 19, 2018.
The Heads of State / Government of the leaders of Asia-Europe countries were invited to the opening ceremony of their annual summit to exchange views and ideas on the planned agenda.
The leaders praised the importance of Asia-Europe connectivity for sustainable development, economic and trade cooperation, and connectivity in new areas such as taxation, digitalization, economicization and the environment. The connection between the people and the people that should be connected and the development of the environment without leaving anyone behind.
The Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia provides three important tips to become a good leader for subordinates.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia, presented three important tips to become a good leader in the family and society to the staff under the supervision of the National Bank.
The three key points of the Governor-General were made when he was invited to preside over the closing ceremony of the 5th Basic Level Kulen Course on "Leadership" on the afternoon of October 19, 2018. On the occasion of the closing of the course, the Governor-General also handed out certificates to many participants who completed this course.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that in order to develop into a qualified leader, staff officers must continue to understand and keep abreast of the situation, develop skills and learn from good experiences, as well as prepare the right attitude.
"I find that good leadership always shows through three qualities: 1: Integrity, 2: Ability, and 3: Understanding. These three keys will make us a leader," he said. A good one. ”
In that, the Governor-General explained in detail these three phrases to the officers under his supervision as follows:
1: Integrity refers to trusting someone who does the right thing and thinks of the common good. This integrity is manifested through leadership attitudes, team development, dedication and responsibility without blaming or blaming any member.
2: Ability refers to a leader who has the ability to turn a vision into reality. Understanding the situation from all angles, combined with clear professional skills, makes the decision and leadership to carry out the work correctly and effectively.
3: Empathy refers to the actual attention to the staff under the supervision. Employee leaders are not afraid to share success with their members.
In addition, the Governor-General instructed all participants to work hard to strengthen their capacity through self-study, research and exchange experiences with Ream Chbom. Strengthen knowledge of information technology and foreign languages for working life, know how to use and synthesize knowledge available for the benefit of daily work and have the virtues and culture to help each other and unity.
This is the fifth summit between North and South Korea for 2018. Although the first meeting between the leaders of the two countries is expected to boost the peace process on the Korean Peninsula, so far some goals have not been achieved.
We know that before the opening of the Pyeongchang Winter Olympics, the Korean Peninsula was covered by a serious conflict, but now the North-South Korean relationship has achieved many successes, so solutions to other problems are possible. Happens in the future. In fact, at the heart of changing the situation on the peninsula is a shift in diplomatic relations.
After US President Donald Trump took office, he stepped up military pressure on North Korea, which has expressed its opposition to nuclear and missile tests. At the same time, the Republic of Korea has previously been preparing to strengthen its military, not only to strengthen its defense, but also to its military alliance with the United States.
But now South Korea has changed its attitude since South Korean President Moon Jae-in took office. He reformed his foreign policy, instead of standing by the United States and preparing for war, he tried to negotiate peacefully with North Korea.
The move has eased tensions, stopped the use of military force as a solution by Pyongyang and opened the way for dialogue between Seoul, Pyongyang and Washington to lead to nuclear disarmament on the Korean Peninsula. The South Korean president paid a nine-day visit to the European Union.
He spoke of the changing situation on the Korean Peninsula and the efforts made by the South Korean government in the past, and called on all parties to support South Korea's policy toward the Asia-Europe Meeting. Cheng Xiheng also stressed that the European Union plays an important role in helping the process of eliminating nuclear weapons.
Through his trip to the European Union, Moon Jae-in was able to show the leaders of those countries the achievements that can be achieved. "Through visits to European countries, South Korea is encouraged to continue to make positive progress toward the elimination of nuclear weapons and missiles," he said.
Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone announces the issuance of 14 million additional shares after the success of the securities market
PPSP first appeared on the Cambodia Securities Exchange in 2016, two years ago. In these two years, the company has achieved great success for the Cambodian capital market.
At the press conference on the listing of additional equity securities of Phnom Penh SEZ on the morning of October 19, 2018, Mr. Fong Nee Wai, Chief Financial Officer of PPSP Company, spoke about the additional listing of the company and the benefits of the listed company. Using various financial instruments.
He said that in the past 18 months, the company has achieved a net profit of $ 9.85 million, and the company will use the net profit after paying for the sale proposal for new business expansion opportunities and for general purposes. Of the company.
Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, said that today PPSP announced to the public that the company has issued an additional 14 million new shares. Whether this publication is public or private.
Mr. Sou Socheat further stated that the new IPO of PPSP is a private publication, not a public offering.
Hong Sochua, CEO of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, said that with the additional listing of PPSP, the number of shares of the company will increase to more than 72 million shares.
He added that the issuance and listing of additional securities today is a consensus that businesses that can issue and list shares on the Cambodia Securities Exchange can also raise additional purchases when needed. The initial public offering takes a little more time and money, but the subsequent issuance will be easier.
Please note that this is the first private sale of securities by a listed company in Cambodia.
To increase the power of the US Navy, it plans to buy more than 300 new types of military ships of all kinds until 2048!
The US Navy plans to buy 245 warships and 56 military aid ships from now until 2048. This is according to the report of the Parliamentary Budget Office (CBO) quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday evening, October 19, 2018.
In its report released on Thursday, the CBO said that the purchase of warships and maintenance costs could cost $ 28.9 billion a year, and that would make the United States achieve its ambitions. To expand the size of the navy to be equipped with 355 warships in just 30 years.
The report also states that under the administration of US President Donald Trump, the US Navy has increased its purchase of 47 more warships over the next 30 years than planned for fiscal year 2017. By the administration of former US President Barack Obama.
Many new ships will replace the old ones that are due to be retired, and this is also considered a large-scale naval modernization that the administration of US President Donald Trump wants to achieve.
In addition, ships that are engineered by engineering experts will be required to extend the number of years of operation, for example, seven destroyer submarines will have to be extended from 33 years to 43 years and some destroyers will be increased from 35 years or 40 years to 45 years.
