(Phnom Penh): This morning, October 19, 2018, the joint police force inspected the quality and safety of food products at Chumpouvorn Market, and found 2.50 fish meatballs containing banned chemicals (Borax). Kg. After the meatballs were found to contain this chemical, CamControl officers continued to search for sources for distribution and production.
The coalition forces operating on this task include Camcontrol officers at the Phnom Penh International Airport branch, laboratory staff of the General Department of Camcontrol, mobile laboratory vehicles, Camcontrol branch officials at the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, officials from the Department of Commerce and the Chompou Voan Market Commission.
Coalition forces educate and disseminate information on food safety and serious health effects, as well as legal risks to traders who bring and receive all kinds of goods of poor quality and without clear sources.
At the same time, CamControl officers also took samples of 20 food products, such as seafood, all kinds of meatballs, prahok, etc. to find banned chemicals that affect the health of consumers.
As a result, after a preliminary analysis on the spot by laboratory officials and a mobile laboratory vehicle, 2.50 kg of banned chemical (borax) was found in the fish salad. CamControl officials worked on the procedure, confiscating and destroying it, and are still searching for distribution sources.
