Speaking at the opening of the Sangkat-Khan Investment Integration Workshop and Khan 3-Year Rolling Investment Program 2019-2021, Mr. Cheng Monira said that in the 2018 Khan 3-Year Rolling Investment Integration Workshop, Khan received a total support project. 83 projects so far, 95% completed.
For 2019, there are 94 projects in the three-year rolling program 2019-2021, including 34 projects in the economic sector, 37 projects in the social sector, 14 projects in the field of land management, natural resources, environment, and 14 administrative and security services. 9 projects.
He added that the integration workshop in Chbar Ampov district, which was organized now, is in line with the five-year development plan of both the commune and the district, in which it needs the support of professional officials and philanthropists to make the project. Prepare to reflect the priority needs at the local level and use resources to target and implement effectively and sustainably.
At the same time, Mr. Cheng Monira also expressed his belief that officials of specialized departments, civil society organizations, the private sector, development partners and philanthropists will support the projects of Khan and Sangkat according to their respective resources.
He said that special departments, NGOs, the private sector and philanthropists who have pledged to support projects now must be included in their 2019 action plan and strive to implement in a timely and effective manner as planned. However, if the project is supported at this time but has not been implemented, the district or sangkat should be notified.
