(Phnom Penh): Traders of Cambodian products have asked the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Commerce, to provide more support for their products, especially various movements to promote the use of Cambodian products.
On the occasion of the trade fair of Khmer products of the campaign to buy Khmer products (Season 3) organized by the Ministry of Commerce on October 18, 2018, many Cambodian traders and producers came to sell and display their products. Because those products are made by Khmer children. Each product is processed, packaged and refined, not inferior to imported products.
Mr. Sim Meng Try, owner of Khmer Meng Try 999 Production Enterprise, said, "In order to increase the momentum of using more Khmer products, I would like to request the Ministry of Commerce to organize more programs related to Khmer, Khmer products." In addition, let the Ministry help promote all Khmer products or bring to distribute to the people so that they can see and know the quality of Khmer.
In addition, the business owner also asked all business owners to produce each product with the right standards and focus on quality first, to be able to support the needs of the people.
"In addition, I want the government to create low-interest loans for small and medium-sized enterprises to have the opportunity to use this budget to establish or expand their business to be more competitive with neighboring countries," he said. .
Mr. Cheng Bunleang, a trader in Khmer products and owner of Mi Angkor, said, "As a owner of a charity, I would like to ask the Royal Government to facilitate more activities such as training and guidance because the opening of the charity. Small scale does not have much insight. "Obviously, like me, I do not fully understand the details of this area, such as sanitation, packaging and marketing."
He added that the exhibition of Cambodian products organized by the Ministry of Commerce is a good campaign to mobilize Cambodians to use local products rather than imported products.
At the same time, Mr. Leang Leng, owner of Leang Leng Fish Sauce Factory, said, "I would like to request the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the relevant ministries in all SMEs to help prevent the flow of substandard and standard goods imported to sell in Cambodia. In addition, please facilitate the regulations to apply for permission to create a charity.
He added that he would like to propose to the Royal Government to establish a policy of low-interest financial loans, because this financial adjustment is very important if the low interest rate will enable SMEs to expand from small to medium-sized enterprises. A giant company like other countries.
Please be informed that "Khmer Product Trade Fair on the occasion of the campaign to buy Khmer products" Season 3 is held for 4 days from October 18-21, 2018 in Phnom Penh.
Regarding the trade fair of Cambodian products, Mr. Pan Sosak said that this exhibition provides benefits for the integration and diversification of economic growth, because strengthening the quality of domestic products and increase production volume, not only provide jobs to people and increase money. Not only revenue, but also the growth of Cambodia's export sector, this is to help boost Cambodia's economic growth to another level.
He added that the Ministry of Commerce has already organized two seasons of successful Khmer product purchasing campaign, the first season in four capitals and provinces: Siem Reap, Kampong Cham, Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh, and the second season. In 5 capitals and provinces: Stung Treng, Battambang, Svay Rieng, Phnom Penh and Kep.
