(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Major General Chea Chandin, Provincial Police Commissioner, on October 19, 2018, cooperated and inspected the overweight vehicles at the gate. International border is located in Phsar Prom village, Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district.
The operation was led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, the head of the overweight vehicle inspection team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and the team raided 3 overweight trucks.
During the hot operation to suppress these overweight trucks, Mr. Seng Chhuon said that in accordance with the instructions of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, the overweight vehicle inspection team will inspect the overloaded vehicles. Transport everywhere to prevent overloading that leads to serious road damage.
The working group leader emphasized that the operation to suppress the overweight truck was carried out in a transparent manner without any intervention, even if the overweight truck belonged to an influential or powerful person, and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol had confirmed that the operation Preventing this overweight truck is not backing down.
Mr. Seng Chhuon called on truck owners to respect the transport laws and weight limits set by law to avoid damaging the roads that the Royal Government has tried to build. The Royal Government as well as the Ministry do not want fines for Overweight because the money from the fine can not be offset with the amount of road damage and can not be used to repair the road.
It should be noted that in the operation to check the weight of these trucks out of 5 cross-border trucks, 3 overweight trucks were found, carrying more than 5 tons to 8.5 tons and All are detained waiting for the car owner to come and deal with the procedure, especially to pay the fine according to the transport law in force.
