Senior Minister Osman Hassan Requests Islamic Development Bank to Increase Scholarships for Cambodian Students on Local Studies
(Saudi Arabia): Special Mission Minister Osman Hassan has asked the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB) to increase the number of local scholarships for Cambodian students to study at Cambodian universities without having to send them abroad because Cambodia has voted. Step forward in the field of education, both public and private, and have quality and reasonable prices.
The request was made on the occasion of Senior Minister Osman Hassan's continued discussions with Mansour Mudek, Vice President of the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB) at the Bank of Saudi Arabia.
The Senior Minister also briefly described the situation in Cambodia, especially the Islamic community under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and the achievements that the Royal Government has decided to provide, especially in the field of education, which plays an important role in the Royal Government. Pay attention and classify in other priority areas.
At the same time, Mr. Osman Hassan also asked the bank to support the project of Wakafa Business Center to support students and immunization.
In response, the Vice President of the Bank agreed to the request for additional scholarships because the students who used to receive IDB Scholarships are getting back the positive results and the important human resource nursery that now gets good jobs to contribute to the society. In the private sector and government institutions, in particular, some have become high-ranking officials in various institutions, including the National Assembly and other ministries.
It should be noted that IsDB Bank has been providing scholarships to 95 Cambodian students since 1992, including 78 graduates from 46 countries and 32 from abroad (Indonesia). Students who receive an IsDB Bank scholarship program are fully covered by tuition, fees and accommodation. Senior Minister Osman Hassan pays courtesy call and discusses work with key Saudi leaders
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of attending the meeting of the Supreme Council of the World Islamic Alliance in Saudi Arabia on October 17-19, 2018, Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister for Special Mission, paid a courtesy call and discussed with key leaders. Of Saudi Arabia.
