(Phnom Penh): As the demand for agricultural machinery in Cambodia is growing steadily, a local company, Men Sarun MD Co., Ltd., in cooperation with Japanese tractor company Mark Myanmar, decided to import and Distribute Solos tractors from India to meet domestic demand.
On the morning of October 19, 2018, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presided over the official inauguration ceremony of the Solos Tractor Distribution Agreement in Cambodia, which was held at Sunway Hotel, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his congratulations with high appreciation and appreciation to Men Sarun MD Co., Ltd., which intends to invest in the agricultural sector by deciding to import and distribute exclusively. Max Solis tractor for sale in Cambodia.
Mr. Veng Sakhon added that the investment of both companies is in line with the new strategy and vision of the head of the Royal Government to develop priority sectors, especially the vision of the agricultural sector is to turn Cambodian agriculture into agriculture. Modern.
He added that Cambodian agriculture has become more competitive, environmentally resilient and sustainable, with the promotion of foreign direct investment and the local private sector as key tools to achieve the goals of its new growth strategy. Cambodia.
On the other hand, in response to the current trend of declining labor consumption in the agricultural sector, we observed that only 3.62% of farmers plowed with the remaining cattle and mechanized. Increased to about 96.38%.
At the same time, Mr. Veng Sakhon also recommended the company to import this agricultural machinery to continue to pay more attention to:
1: Research and research of new technologies to reach more equipments for agricultural machinery on land preparation, sowing and harvesting to suit the actual needs of Cambodian farmers today. In line with the geography and type of land in Cambodia, in particular, this supply is in line with the new turn of participation in the fourth phase of the Industrial Revolution in the Digital Age.
2: Long-lasting use, durable to use with better service to users.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to attend the UN Conference on Trade and Development of the 2018 World Investment Forum from October 22 to 24 in Geneva
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Moki Sakituyi, Secretary-General of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead a high-level delegation to attend the UN Conference. On Trade and Development of the World Investment Forum 2018 "which will be held from October 22 to 24, 2018 in Geneva, Switzerland under the common theme" Investment in Sustainable Development ".
At the Global Investment Leaders Summit, the Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address on "Investment in the New Era of Globalization and Industrialization and Business Opportunities in Cambodia in the Context of an Integrated Market."
In addition to attending the meeting, the Prime Minister will have separate meetings with leaders of a number of key international organizations, such as Mr. Francis Gary, Director-General of the World Intellectual Property Organization, Ms. Aran Chagonzalez, Executive Director of the International Trade Center. Roberto Cavalho Azavevedo, Director-General of the World Trade Organization, and Moki Sakituyi, Secretary-General of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development.
