Below is a video of people's interest: More than 1,000 people in Baray district receive free medical check-ups from Vietnamese volunteer doctors
(Kampong Thom): More than 1,000 people in Baray district, Kampong Thom province, received free medical examination and treatment from the Vietnamese volunteer doctor "Tam Viet", a group of Vietnamese volunteer doctors in Cambodia.
This humanitarian activity will take place from October 17 to 21, 2018 at the residence of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, under the close cooperation of government officials of the Ministry of Tourism and district doctors, and Vietnamese doctors. There are 180 people.
According to the survey, more than 1,000 people from three communes of Baray district came to be examined and treated for diseases such as pediatrics, gynecology and the elderly by a group of Vietnamese volunteer doctors waiting to receive them. Check the treatment with a fresh, friendly and responsible face. The 1,000 people who came for examination and treatment at that time included people from Baray commune, Chhouk Khsach commune and Treal commune.
Mr. Top Sopheak, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on behalf of Minister Thong Khon, expressed his deep gratitude to the Vietnamese Volunteer Doctors of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam for devoting their time to diagnose and treat the Cambodian people. Free Baray residents now.
