At the 12th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting, in addition to approving the planned agenda, the meeting raised the threat of terrorism and weapons of mass destruction, including chemical, biological and radioactive weapons.
The meeting also discussed and exchanged views on counter-terrorism, terrorism and all the challenges that need to be addressed through enhanced cooperation, joint patrol training and information sharing. Come on. The ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting considers better security in the ASEAN region as a key driver in the Asia-Pacific region.
He expressed confidence that terrorism would not be suppressed by military means alone, but should begin to consider "protective measures" for a lasting solution.
