(Phnom Penh): Camcontrol officials at Phnom Penh International Airport this morning, October 19, 2018, inspected the quality and safety of food products at Chumpouvorn Market, Phnom Penh to find banned chemicals that affect consumers' health.
The inspection of the quality and safety of the above products was led by Mr. Chan Phea Hoeun, Deputy Chief of Post, Mr. Ton Bora, Mr. Ang Mina, Mr. Ly Heng Bunlen and in collaboration with the laboratory staff of the General Department of CamControl and the mobile laboratory vehicle. Camcontrol Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch and Department of Commerce Officer, Chompou Voan Market Commission.
On that occasion, CamControl officials also instructed traders on how to store goods properly and understand the legal responsibilities of their food products that are displayed for sale when there is a serious health risk. Traders who bring and receive all kinds of goods that do not have quality and have no clear origin.
Officials from Phnom Penh International Airport Camcontrol took 20 samples of food products such as seafood, all kinds of meatballs and frozen prahok, etc. to find banned chemicals that affect consumers' health.
As a result, after a preliminary analysis on the spot by mobile laboratory laboratory officials: 2.50 kg of banned chemical (borax) was found in the smart fish meatballs. Authorities have carried out confiscation procedures and are still searching for distribution sources.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration: The water of Boeung Prek has been stopped since 2016 due to the inflow of sewage. Currently, the clean water in Preah Sihanouk is drawn from Prek Teuk Sap Kbal Chhay.
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has confirmed that Prek Top water, the provincial administration has stopped supplying and distributing water since 2016, because the lake water has sewage inflow and can not be used as before. Saath has taken the water source from Kbal Chhay freshwater canal to use until now.
Please be informed that the announcement of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration was made after the reaction around the deletion of this lake, as well as the decision of the Royal Government signed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to cut more than 11 hectares of land from the protected area. Boeung Prek Top.
