Russia pledges new aid from 2019 and wants to use old debt to invest in Cambodia
The Russian Prime Minister made the remarks during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of October 18, 2018 in Brussels, Belgium, where the two leaders attended the Asia Summit. - The 12th Europe.
During the meeting, the two leaders discussed ways to strengthen ties and cooperation between the two countries. Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned the debt that Cambodia owed to the former Soviet Union, and wanted to turn that debt into investment in Cambodia instead.
At this point, the Russian Prime Minister said that from 2019, Russia will provide some more assistance to Cambodia. Regarding the debt that Cambodia owes, Russia will use that debt for investment in Cambodia, which is a good priority for Cambodia, which Russia wants to help.
The Russian Prime Minister also informed Samdech Techo about providing technical assistance in addition to assisting in the renovation of the Khmer-Russian Friendship Hospital, and that Russia intends to assist in the restoration of some of Cambodia's ancient temples due to the large number of Russian tourists. Visit and be very interested in Cambodia.
Samdech also thanked Russia for promising to help modernize the Khmer-Russian Friendship Hospital. Samdech considered that the Khmer-Russian Friendship Hospital is very valuable for Cambodia, including the Cambodian Institute of Technology.
On that occasion, the Russian Prime Minister also promised that Russia will continue to cooperate with Cambodia in many areas, including security, economy, trade and investment to further strengthen the relationship between the two countries.
