Minister of Commerce Supports Representatives of Garment Manufacturers to Join Cambodia Garment Manufacturers Association (GMAC)
The Minister's declaration of support was made on the occasion of chairing a meeting to discuss the possibility of membership (GMAC) of representatives of travel equipment manufacturers, which was held on Thursday morning, October 18, 2018 at Angkor Wat. Of the Ministry of Commerce.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak encouraged all representatives of travel equipment factories to report to their leaders and meet some of the requirements of the Association to receive various benefits from the Royal Government, such as: Discount on electricity prices. , Exemption of export fees and preferential tariffs from key markets in Cambodia's partner countries.
He added that currently, with the support and coordination of the Ministry of Commerce, since 2011, 463 garment factories, 55 shoe factories and 18 travel accessories factories have joined GMAC. All are enjoying the export of goods to major markets in the world.
At the same time, representatives of GMAC member factory owners praised the benefits of the association in addition to the many offers from the Royal Government of Cambodia, including: Access to key market information. Training, labor dispute resolution services and free consultation, etc.
