More than 1,000 candidates to participate in the recruitment of officials within the Ministry of Labor, in 2018, the Ministry of Labor needs only 14 new officials
(Phnom Penh): During the opening ceremony of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training Civil Servants Recruitment Exam, Mr. Teav McTell, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Labor stated that in the Ministry of Labor Framework Examination in 2018, there were 1,212 candidates, including 45 contract staff of the Ministry of Labor, 17 disabled people, in addition to monks, students, etc. This exam was held at the National Institute of Kosamak this morning, October 19, 2018.
Speaking to the media on the occasion, Mr. Teav Mactel confirmed that the examination committee always organizes the exam according to the procedure by setting up a sub-committee responsible for each building and examination room.
At the same time, the Ministry of Labor also issued instructions for the guardians and responsible persons in the rooms to check the exam activities and other irregular activities of the candidates. At the same time, the Ministry also issued internal regulations for candidates to ensure that the 2018 recruitment of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will be effective, transparent and fair.
The Undersecretary of State said that the Commission and the Sub-Committee on Organizing and Responsible for the Recruitment Examination of Officials of the Ministry of Labor will continue to strengthen the inspection work as well as thoroughly revise the worksheet to select new officials with the actual capacity that will be To be a force to promote national development.
According to Mr. Teav Maktel, for the 2018 exam, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training needs 14 new officials.
Please be informed that the Civil Service Examination of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is divided into two subjects: General Knowledge, which lasts 2 hours, and English, which lasts 1 hour and 30 minutes. The exam is co-organized by the Ministry of Public Works and is monitored by the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU).
Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia urges companies to seize the opportunity to obtain financing through the securities market
(Phnom Penh): At the "Awarding Ceremony for Leading Companies Excellence Program" on October 18, 2018, Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, urged all companies throughout Cambodia to seize the opportunity. Of obtaining financing through the securities market.
Mr. Sou Socheat said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy, paying close attention and launching policies to promote small enterprises. And the medium, which is the backbone of the national economy.
He said that through this, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, has set out a policy to support the development of small and medium enterprises, by promoting the financing mechanism for small and medium enterprises.
At the same time, Mr. Sou Socheat said, "As the Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, I would also like to encourage companies to seize the opportunity to receive financing through the securities market."
The Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia added that, of course, the securities market process is still limited in terms of trading activities as well as market size, with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia having five companies listed and the sixth and seventh companies are nearing completion. Preparation and preparation for registration in the near future.
