China supports Cambodia to host Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020
(Brussels, Belgium): Chinese Premier Li Keqiang has said that China has always supported Cambodia's role in organizing various meetings, including hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020. Also.
The Chinese Prime Minister made the announcement during a meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of October 18, 2018 in Brussels, Belgium. Attended the 12th Asia-Europe Summit.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also invited the Chinese Prime Minister to attend the 13th Asia-Europe Summit to be held in Cambodia in 2020.
To host this important meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has sought a lot of support from countries in Asia and Europe, and those countries have also expressed their agreement. The decision to host Cambodia at the Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020 will be made at the 12th Summit in Belgium on October 19.
Cambodia became a member of this forum at the 5th ASEM Summit held in Hanoi, Vietnam on October 8, 2004. It is an honor for Cambodia to host this important meeting and an opportunity to expand better cooperation with the 50 member countries.
It should be noted that during the meeting in Brussels, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Li Keqiang also exchanged views on bilateral, multilateral cooperation, regional and international issues, especially on China-ASEAN relations. The two heads of government discussed the import of rice from Cambodia to China, which China has previously given a quota of 300,000 tons of rice from Cambodia to China.
The Chinese Prime Minister stressed that China will continue to support the import of products from Cambodia to China.
