(Kampong Cham): Due to the people living along the Mekong River mentioned the collapse of the river bank caused by sand dredging, only on the morning of October 18, 2018, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham led a professional officer from Ministry of Mines and Energy to gather people to hold a full day public forum in 4 communes in Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province to discuss clearly and accept all.
According to the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, it is true that river bank collapses occur every year, and in 2017, there were more than 5,000 meters of river bank collapses with a depth of 2-10 meters, in which Kang Meas district collapsed More than 3,000 meters long.
In particular, in 2018, the river bank will continue to collapse, a total of 11,957 meters in Kampong Cham province, but 2,200 meters in Kang Meas district at a depth of 5-20 meters, meanwhile, the provincial authorities inspected The housing situation of the people who helped to dismantle their houses is also affected by the landslide.
The provincial governor said that according to the report of Kampong Cham province from the beginning, there are always landslides, if not this side, that side every year, but since then, landslide cases have always raised concerns from people who are worried. That from dredging, even though it is known that with or without dredging, riverbanks still break every year.
The provincial governor confirmed that the collapse of the river bank, it depends on the flow of water because the river is curved up and down, so if the water hits the corner, it will break, so people can say that this is a natural process. And natural disasters.
In particular, today, in order to follow the policy of the Royal Government, we have met together to explain and explain to each other so that the people can understand and accept all of them, in which we have professional officials from the Ministry of Mines and Energy. Explain the technique so that the people understand and agree with each other.
Please note that in the process of the public forum was resolved smoothly by the people as well as the owners of the dredging business can be accepted by all. The Eighth Committee of the National Assembly requested the Minister of Labor to appoint a liaison officer with the National Assembly to work closely with the commission.
(Phnom Penh): The Eighth Committee of the National Assembly has requested Minister Ith Sam Heng to appoint a liaison officer and work closely with the commission to complement each other.
The purpose of the 8th Committee of the National Assembly was made during a visit to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of the 8th Committee of the National Assembly led by Ms. Lok Kheng, Chairman of the Committee on Health, Social Affairs, Veterans, Youth Rehabilitation, Vocational Training. And Women's Affairs of the National Assembly on the afternoon of October 18, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that in line with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 3 for Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency in Cambodia of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Labor and Vocational Training Life in Cambodia has really made great progress in recent years, especially in the fifth term of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with a lot of achievements.
In addition to job creation and increase productivity of workers, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training as its staff, has been paying close attention to improving the health and safety of workers and expanding the regime. Social security for those who are also subject to the provisions of the Labor Law.
The Minister stated that these are successful achievements in the field of employment and vocational training in the fifth mandate of the Royal Government, while some challenges remain to be addressed in the sixth mandate of the Royal Government. Government through the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 for Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency: Building the Groundwork for Achieving Cambodia's Vision 2050.
On behalf of the Chairman of the Eighth Commission in this new mandate, Ms. Lok Kheng, together with the members of the Commission, will strengthen the cooperation with the Ministry by jointly thinking, implementing and taking responsibility for the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government. .
She also asked Minister Ith Sam Heng to appoint a liaison officer to work closely with the commission to help complement each other.
In response, the Minister accepted these requests from the Chairman of the Commission, and the Minister and his colleagues are pleased to continue the successful cooperation with the Eighth Commission. Is Iranian oil falling to zero? This is just a hoax!
