The Ministry of Labor and all UN agencies in Cambodia work together to develop a decent work program for Cambodia 2019-2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, together with all UN agencies in Cambodia, has been working together to develop a "Decent Work Program for Cambodia 2019-2023" to create productive employment opportunities. Proper income, safe work environment and appropriate social protection for each stage of Cambodia's development.
In order to make this national program run smoothly, the Ministry of Labor held a national workshop on the preparation of a decent work program for Cambodia 2019-2023 at the Raffles Royal Hotel this morning, October 18, 2018, chaired by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
A review of the Appropriate Work Program for Cambodia 2016-2018 was conducted to identify what worked and did not work and identify new priorities that need to be developed in the Country Appropriate Work Program. Cambodia 2019-2013.
The program will help identify priority priorities for support, targeting vulnerable groups, and to link most effectively to national development priorities in support of the 2030 Agenda for Development. Sustainably, while running a high level of decent work agenda in Cambodia.
The current National Workshop is organized to review the key achievements that Cambodia has achieved in the Decent Work Program for Cambodia 2016-2018 and to identify priority work activities to promote the achievement of the Decent Work Program for Cambodia. 2019-2023 onwards.
