(Battambang): On October 18, 2018, Battambang Provincial CamControl officers and all relevant institutions cracked down on 70 kilos of damaged chicken meat, chicken bones embedded in a truck transporting fruits and vegetables imported from Thailand through Phnom Dey checkpoint, Sampov Loun district. And confiscated and burned immediately.
Mr. Hak Sokrin, President of CamControl Branch, said that in order to prevent any defective goods and to protect the daily health of the people, professional officers cooperated with the officials of the Department of Commerce and local authorities to inspect goods imported from Thailand. Phnom Dey International Checkpoint, Sampov Loun District, apparently today intercepted 70 kilograms of damaged chicken bones and bones embedded in a fruit and vegetable cart.
The President confirmed that the professional officers continue to regularly inspect the education through the media by putting stickers on the outlets or educating directly about the health effects of food on the market. Import, sale of defective goods, mixing of chemicals, no specific date, no more traffic in the market.
He also called on people to be careful before buying goods at the market, especially daily food, please check carefully to avoid touching the goods to damage the health of your health in the future.
