However, while the United States is concerned that China may use the special location to raid its communications and intelligence satellites, the United States has already sent two satellites to Point L2 of the Moon-Earth system as well. Drug trafficking dispute in Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province leads to murder, now the perpetrators have been arrested
(Banteay Meanchey): Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police arrested and identified a murderer and his accomplice in a case of intentional murder in a drug trafficking dispute at Intam School, Teuk Thla Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Brigadier General Sithi Loh, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police, told Fresh News Agency that the suspect and his accomplices were arrested on the morning of October 17, 2018, after residents reported The body of a young man was found dead in a bush on National Road 5 at Intam School, Teuk Thla Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Serey Sophorn City on the afternoon of October 15.
Immediately, the specialized police force and the Serei Sophorn City Police Force under the direct command of the Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Ath Cam, went to investigate the incident and concluded that the suspect had died as a result of the murder.
At the same time, the police also searched and found the identity of the victim named Chung Un, male, 31 years old, no real occupation, living in Preah Ponlea Village, Sangkat Preah Ponlea, Serey Sophorn City.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, after the authorities knew the identity of the victim's body, the police force searched and identified the suspect as the killer under the coordination of Mr. Meas Chanpiseth, Prosecutor of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court. Police arrested Meas Kihong, a 21-year-old unemployed man living in Sophy Village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City on the night of October 15, 2018.
Brigadier General Sithi Loh confirmed that between the suspect and the victim, a drug dealer in Serei Sophorn City, the parents were evicted from the house. Drugs.
According to the suspect's confession, Meas Kihong said that before the incident, they had a dispute over the drug business, the victim embezzled money from selling drugs to everyone, the suspect, anger and victims The victim found out that he fell in love with the victim's girlfriend and was angry that the victim used his motorcycle as a means of selling and distributing drugs without returning the motorcycle to him.
Late at night on October 15, the two of them took a motorbike taxi from Chamkar Khnor Guesthouse to Poipet City to buy drugs from Ouk Pin, a 51-year-old man living in Palilei 2 Village, Poipet Sangkat. After buying the drugs, the two of them returned to Serei Sophorn on a motorbike with the suspect, Meas Kihong, as the driver.
The Deputy General Commissioner added that they were riding a motorbike to the scene. The suspect, Meas Kihong, also rode a motorbike to drop off a motorbike, explode and explode on the national road to wake up the victim. Want to fall?
At that time, the victim named Jung Un did not say anything. Caused the victim to faint, so the suspect squeezed the victim's neck until he died. He (the suspect) then rode a motorcycle to Serei Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The deputy provincial commissioner added that he later concluded and identified Ouk Pin (the suspect) in Poipet City as a drug dealer.
Currently, the suspect named Meas Ki Hong was arrested by the police force of the Office of Case Management and sent to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court for legal action. Separately, the suspect, Ouk Pin, was not involved in the murder, as he was involved in drug offenses, and a drug case was filed in court.
Svay Rieng CamControl Officers Find 2 Gas Stations and 3 Good Fuel Stations in Svay Rieng City
(Svay Rieng): CamControl Svay Rieng Branch On October 18, 2018, in cooperation with the General Department of CamControl and the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected the quantity and quality of fuel at 5 depots and stations in Svay Rieng Province. Found 2 petrol stations selling substandard, substandard and substandard, while the other 3 stations were full liters and good quantity.
Mr. Pheng Nil, Chief of CamControl Svay Rieng Branch, told Fresh News Agency in Svay Rieng that after using Camcontrol's mobile fuel laboratory vehicle to check the quantity and quality of fuel at 5 depots and gas stations in the province. That some are correct and some are not yet up to standard (3 correct stations and 2 incorrect stations).
Mr. Pheng Nil added that the CamControl team has instructed depot and gas station owners to ensure that the quality and quantity are standard. For some depots and stations that are not normal, the officials of the working group asked them to make a contract for the first time so that they can change the quantity and quality.
"At this time, we have not yet revealed the location of depots and stations that do not sell enough liters and do not have the quality, leaving the opportunity for the owners to adjust to the correct technical standards again," he said. "But if there is a second sale of less than a liter and cases of irregularities are found, they may face closure of the depot or station and the license will be revoked according to the procedure."
