After the previous free monthly screening and treatment program for this course, Cho Ray Hospital, Phnom Penh, in collaboration with DHG Pharma, organized a free screening and treatment program for the first 50 new patients in one day. The collaboration will be held for up to 1,000 patients by a highly experienced Vietnamese specialist from Cho Rai Hospital in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
"Let normal people do not have high blood pressure, have a blood pressure below 120/80, from 120/80 to 130/80, more likely to have high blood pressure if more than 130/80 leads to high blood pressure," explained Dr. Letith Two Tweez. The first stage of bleeding requires the patient to check the diet and exercise regularly, if it reaches 140/80 or higher requires treatment with medication to lower blood pressure.
