(Preah Vihear): Major General Yin Chamnan, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, has ordered all district and district inspectors in Preah Vihear province to pay more attention to cracking down on drug cases in their localities.
The General Commissioner said this on the afternoon of October 16, 2018, when he chaired a meeting of the Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commission at the Provincial Police.
During the meeting, Major General Yin Chamnan praised the eight district and district inspectors of Preah Vihear province, who for some time have successfully completed many major tasks, especially in protecting security and order in their localities. Body well.
He said that in the past, the crackdown on drug cases in each city-district inspector has always cooperated with the provincial police commissioner, but from now on, all district and district inspectors must stand on their own to crack down on drugs themselves. If any city-district has a drug offense, the city-district inspector is responsible.
