(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on October 17, 2018, requested the relevant institutions, private sector development partners, all national and international organizations to continue to implement all measures to reduce the destruction of soil quality. Unsustainable land use and ecosystem destruction.
In order to participate in the prevention of the effects of the effects of the natural phenomenon "El Nino", Mr. Veng Sakhon also provided some key messages to the whole ceremony to consider the implementation of effective interconnection in order to include:
First, increase the capacity of institutions and human resources on the development of new technologies of crops, animal breeds and fishery resources that can adapt to drought, floods, heat and damage from diseases and pests caused by the impact. Climate change and the influence of the natural phenomenon "El Nino" by strengthening the research experiments of the Agricultural Research and Development Institute of Cambodia (CADI).
Second, increase the capacity of vulnerable farmers to use new technologies in the production of crops and animals that can adapt to climate change, the effects of the natural phenomenon "El Nino", by promoting effective and effective outreach services. Transfer of technologies developed into practical production conditions to ensure food security and optimize intervention, rescue and restoration of damage caused by the effects of natural phenomena.
Third, reduce the loss and degradation of forests and inappropriate agricultural production by encouraging the conservation, management and sustainable development of natural resources, especially the strengthening of community forests, including animal husbandry, some crops in Increase deforestation and benefit communities economically.
At the same time, it is necessary to promote the development and optimization of fisheries management in response to climate change, the influence of the natural phenomenon "El Nino", with a strong focus on improving water ecosystems, preventing the destruction of flooded forests. And mangrove forests, increase research and development of all types of aquaculture, as well as strengthen the capacity to manage fishing communities more effectively.
Fourth, promote the development of human resources as a key contribution to adaptation and mitigation of the effects of the natural phenomenon "El Nino" Climate change on crop production, wildlife and fisheries through education, training, change And share information and dissemination of knowledge and skills related to climate change and global warming.
At the same time, the agricultural statistics system, which provides specific data on the impact of the effects of the natural phenomenon "El Nino" will be strengthened accordingly. The National Committee for Disaster Management is an effective mechanism for alleviating the suffering of the affected people, and the Cambodian Food Reserve System continues its activities to assist victims of natural disasters, especially women. And children primarily.
Sixth, to promote good and stable agricultural practices in terms of green water management, agricultural innovation, with the use of new technologies in cultivation that are resistant to climate change, as well as the natural phenomenon "El Nino". Incorporate basic ecosystem principles.
At the same time, it is necessary to identify and disseminate smart agricultural practices to ensure the exchange of experiences between farmers and farmers, as well as to improve the identification and management of natural risks and capabilities in accordance. And changing weather conditions at all levels.
