The arrival of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation was warmly welcomed by EU leaders and the Cambodian Ambassador to Belgium. In particular, there is a huge welcome from people living and studying in Belgium, as well as from other European countries.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the 12th Asia-Europe Meeting will be held under the theme "Europe and Asia: Global Partners for Global Challenges", aimed at strengthening dialogue and cooperation between Asia and Europe. The two regions are working together to tackle issues ranging from increased trade and investment, connectivity, sustainable development and climate change.
As for the meeting process, ASEM consists of a summit meeting, a ministerial meeting, a senior official meeting and a working class meeting. ASEM meetings are held every two years and are held alternately in Asia and once in Europe. Meetings in Europe are usually chaired by the President of the European Union.
The ASEM Foreign Ministers' Meeting (ASEM FMM) is a continuation of the ASEM Dialogue under the political pillar. This meeting is held every two years between the summits and is held alternately in Asia and once in Europe. The ministerial meeting focuses on many other areas of cooperation, including society, culture and education.
Asia-Europe has also set up a fund (ASEF) to fund its cooperation. The Asia-Europe Foundation, established in 1997, is the sole body of the Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM), which aims to raise awareness, strengthen relationships and facilitate cooperation among people, institutions and organizations in Asia and the Middle East. Europe.
In the last 18 years, ASEF has established a people-to-people network with tens of thousands of people from Asia and Europe and is currently working on 700 projects on economy, culture, education, public health and sustainable development. The fund receives financial contributions from ASEM members on a voluntary basis.
(Koh Kong): The Engineering Division "No. 178 Bridge-Road" of the Ministry of National Defense, led by Lt. Gen. Soeun Roeut, Deputy Director of the Engineering Department of the Ministry of National Defense, has been actively working to repair National Road No. 48 connecting National Road No. 4 to Koh Kong province to achieve as planned before the Sea Festival in December 2018.
During the recent rainy season, section of National Road 48 was severely damaged, with some areas damaged by flooding and others damaged by overcrowding. Of the total road length of more than 150 kilometers, the damaged road is 63 kilometers long, divided into 91 places.
Since 2018, Koh Kong province is responsible for hosting the Sea Festival, so National Road No. 48 will play an important role for people to travel to visit this festival. Renovation of this national road is absolutely necessary if the current difficult situation will not be able to attract people to visit the sea festival at the end of the year.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, took the force to repair the road from the Ministry of Public Works and the Ministry of National Defense's engineering team to work together to repair the road as planned. Mr. Sun Chanthol said that a total of 114 vehicles were deployed to repair this stretch of road day and night.
The engineering team deployed 57 units and 63 troops to repair the road. Lt. Gen. Soeun Roeut, Deputy Director of the Engineering Department of the Ministry of National Defense and a personal assistant to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, stated that his forces are actively working responsibly on road repairs. This makes it easier for people to travel.
Brigadier General Nan Boreth, Deputy Director of the Ministry of National Defense's Engineering Department, also pointed out that the Ministry of National Defense's "178 Bridges-Roads" Engineering Division has many years of experience and expertise in road and bridge construction. Not only that, there are good machinery and enough strength to repair this road to achieve the plan of the Royal Government.
He also vowed to work hard to lead the task force to achieve the plan before the Sea Festival begins. It should be noted that the repair of the damaged road will cost about 12 million US dollars, which is the budget of the Royal Government. Reproduction technology with the help of 30 years in China has achieved good results (Video inside)
The third hospital of Peking University (PUTH) is the birthplace of modern assisted reproductive technology. The hospital has been searching for ways to help infertile couples for many years, including couples in generations where China allows people to have only one child per family.
"The third hospital of Peking University has been closely monitoring the leading institutions in this field," said Liu Ping, deputy director of the Reproductive Medicine Center of Peking University Third Hospital. For more than 30 years, we have gradually learned about this assisted reproductive technology from scratch. "Now our hospital is of the highest quality in the world."
Thirty years of technological development have coincided with political and economic changes in China.
"Reform and market opening have provided opportunities that pave the way for China to learn about the latest technology," said Liu Ping, deputy director of the Center for Reproductive Medicine at Peking University Third Hospital. And can share many new ideas with other countries. "It has helped us to overcome the difficulties of experimenting with human resources and to create our own systems and treatments."
"I think he probably remembers the hospital," said Liu Ping, deputy director of the Center for Reproductive Medicine at Peking University Third Hospital. He has an emotional connection with here. "She came to train here when she was in university, and she has been working here since she graduated."
