Minister of Rural Development inspects the condition of roads and bridges damaged by floods in Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province
(Prey Veng): Mr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development and his delegation and Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province, on October 16, 2018 inspected the condition of 8,700 roads and bridges damaged by the Mekong River flood. The meter is located in Kampong Kramuon village, Prey Konlong commune to Po Rieng Tbong village, Po Rieng commune, Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province, in order to temporarily allow people to travel.
In addition to inspecting the condition of the damaged roads and steel bridges, the Minister and the delegation also inspected the project to study the spillway dam located between Kampong Khsach and Kampong Kramuon.
At the same time, the broken bridge (Saang bridge) in Thmey village, Prek Ante commune, Po Rieng district (one side of the bridge is broken at the end of the bridge), which is 30 meters long and 10 meters wide, is planned to rebuild the steel bridge to cross temporarily, but this bridge is broken It will be studied for reconstruction soon. Separately, between Po Rieng District Hall to the broken bridge and there are plans to study the construction of another bridge with a length of 60 meters.
Mr. Chea Somethy and the people of Prey Veng province would like to thank the Minister for coming down to solve the problem and take urgent measures for these damaged roads and bridges.
